      "name": "SafeDelete",
      "signature": "void SafeDelete(void * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Safely deletes a dynamically allocated object using the C++ delete operator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the object pointer is not NULL\n2. If valid, call the delete operator (Ordinal_403) with the object pointer\n3. Pass \"delete\" string constant, -1, and 0 as additional parameters to the delete operator\n4. Return (no return value)\n\nParameters:\npObject (void *): Pointer to the object to be deleted. Can be NULL for safe operation.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check prevents crashes from deleting NULL pointers\n- Function acts as a safe wrapper around the underlying C++ delete operator\n- Magic number 0xffffffff (-1) likely indicates size or allocation flags",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
