      "name": "ProcessEqualityOperation",
      "signature": "int ProcessEqualityOperation(int nLeftOperand, int nRightOperand)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Process equality operation between two operands through dispatcher framework.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Signal equality operation by calling function with character '=' (0x3d)\n2. Forward both operands to processing function for evaluation\n3. Return success status (1) to indicate operation completed\n\nParameters:\n\nnLeftOperand - Left-side operand for equality comparison\nnRightOperand - Right-side operand for equality comparison\n\nReturns:\n\n1 - Operation completed successfully (always returns success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3d (61 decimal) - ASCII character '=' used to identify equality operation type",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
