      "name": "ProcessGameCommandPacketMode1",
      "signature": "void ProcessGameCommandPacketMode1(byte * pbPacketData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Thunk wrapper for game command packet processing with mode 1.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Move packet data pointer from ECX to EDX (second parameter)\n2. Set ECX to 1 (mode/type indicator for primary command processing)\n3. Tail-call jump to FUN_6fb34fb0 for actual packet dispatch\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData (ECX) - Pointer to game command packet data structure.\n                       Byte offsets: +1 = command type, +2 = flags,\n                       +3 = status, +4 = additional data.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (tail call to dispatcher)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a thunk that forwards all calls to FUN_6fb34fb0 with\n    mode parameter hardcoded to 1\n  - Mode 1 appears to be the primary/default command processing mode\n  - No direct callers found - likely invoked via function pointer table\n\nRelated:\n  FUN_6fb34fb0 - Main command packet dispatcher that handles all\n                  game state commands based on packet flags and type",
