      "name": "StoreGlobalValueAndSetFlag",
      "signature": "void StoreGlobalValueAndSetFlag(uint * pValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores a global DWORD value from a pointer and activates the global flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the DWORD value from the memory address pointed to by pValue (ECX)\n2. Store the loaded value into the global DWORD variable g_dwStoredGlobalValue\n3. Set the global flag g_dwGlobalFlagActive to 1 (activated/enabled state)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npValue (uint *) - __fastcall parameter in ECX; pointer to a 4-byte DWORD value to be stored globally\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function modifies global state only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The value 0x1 is a constant flag indicating the activated/enabled state\n- Global g_dwStoredGlobalValue is read by GetStoredGlobalValue (0x6ff30b50) to retrieve the stored value\n- Global g_dwGlobalFlagActive is written by ProcessDownloadModeOperation (0x6ff2f355)\n- Multiple write operations at 0x6ff30bfb, 0x6ff30c0b, 0x6ff30c16, 0x6ff30c26, 0x6ff30c36, 0x6ff30c46, 0x6ff30c56, 0x6ff30c66 suggest g_dwStoredGlobalValue is part of a multi-write sequence",
