      "name": "ValidateBattleNetClientCredentials",
      "signature": "uint ValidateBattleNetClientCredentials(BNClientCredentials * pCredentials, uint dwCredentialsSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates Battle.net client credentials structure and logs authentication data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate credentials pointer is non-null (TEST ECX, ECX)\n2. Validate credentials buffer size is at least 16 bytes (CMP EDX, 0x10)\n3. If either validation fails, jump to error handler and return 0\n4. Extract four credential fields from structure at specified offsets:\n   - Offset 0x0: clientId (32-bit value)\n   - Offset 0x4: clientToken (32-bit value)\n   - Offset 0x8: registrationAuthority (32-bit value)\n   - Offset 0xc: registrationKey (32-bit value)\n5. Enable debug logging for category 2 with flag 4 (ManageLoggingState)\n6. Write each credential field to registry via WriteRegistryValueWithValidationThunk\n   - Writes clientId with label \"Client ID\"\n   - Writes clientToken with label \"Client Token\"\n   - Writes registrationAuthority with label \"Registration Authority\"\n   - Writes registrationKey with label \"Registration Version\"\n7. Log success message \"client acknowledged\" via LogFormattedDebugMessage\n8. Restore logging state by clearing flag 4 (ManageLoggingState with -4)\n9. Return 1 to indicate successful validation and credential logging\n10. On validation failure, log error \"ERROR BDClientId: invalid response\" and return 0\n\nParameters:\n  pCredentials - Pointer to BNClientCredentials structure containing four 32-bit authentication fields\n  dwCredentialsSize - Size of credentials buffer in bytes (must be >= 16 bytes for all fields)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Credentials validated successfully and all fields logged to registry\n  0 - Validation failed (null pointer or insufficient buffer size)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Minimum credentials size is 0x10 (16 bytes) to accommodate four 32-bit fields\n  - Logging category 2 targets Battle.net client subsystem\n  - Logging flags are additive/subtractive (4 enables, -4 disables category logging)\n  - Registry writes perform validation via dedicated thunk function\n  - Error message indicates Battle.net response validation failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name             | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------------------|------|----------------------------------\n  0x0  |   4  | clientId               | uint | Battle.net client identifier value\n  0x4  |   4  | clientToken            | uint | Client authentication token\n  0x8  |   4  | registrationAuthority  | uint | Authority granting registration\n  0xc  |   4  | registrationKey        | uint | Session/registration key value",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
