      "name": "SetFlagIfValueZero",
      "signature": "void SetFlagIfValueZero(int * pValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Conditionally sets a global flag when the dereferenced value is zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference the parameter pointer (ECX register contains pointer)\n2. Compare dereferenced value against zero\n3. If value equals zero, set global flag g_dwZeroValueFlag to 1\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npValue (int *) - Pointer to integer value to test (passed in ECX register)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global flag g_dwZeroValueFlag (at 0x6ff3ef48) is only set when *pValue == 0\n- If *pValue is non-zero, function returns without modifying the flag\n- Uses __fastcall convention with parameter passed in ECX register\n- Used as a conditional setter for initialization or state tracking logic",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
