      "name": "ValidateCryptProviderHandle",
      "signature": "int ValidateCryptProviderHandle(HANDLE * phProvider)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates cryptographic provider handle and updates global validation state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read the handle value from the pointer parameter using ECX (first fastcall parameter)\n2. Load handle value into EDX from the memory address pointed to by phProvider\n3. Clear EAX register for use as result accumulator\n4. Test EDX against zero to determine if handle is NULL\n5. Set AL=1 if handle is NULL (invalid), AL=0 if non-NULL (valid)\n6. Store validation result (AL) to global variable g_dwCryptProviderValid\n7. Load return value 1 into EAX to indicate validation completed\n8. Return to caller with success code\n\nParameters:\n  phProvider (HANDLE *) - Pointer to cryptographic provider handle to validate\n    Passed in ECX register per __fastcall calling convention\n    Points to a HANDLE value that will be tested for NULL\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success (1) after updating validation state\n    Actual validation result stored in global g_dwCryptProviderValid\n    Return value of 1 indicates function executed without error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If *phProvider is NULL (0x0), sets g_dwCryptProviderValid to 1 (invalid state)\n  - If *phProvider is non-NULL, sets g_dwCryptProviderValid to 0 (valid state)\n  - Global state persists for consumption by other cryptographic functions",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9ea1ad207d8db7b2d4b1da751913ced4",
