      "name": "CopyStringToGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "int CopyStringToGlobalBuffer(char * lpszSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Copies a string to the global string buffer using STORM.DLL string copy function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push maximum copy length (0x7fffffff) to limit buffer overflow\n2. Push source string pointer from ECX register (fastcall parameter)\n3. Push destination buffer address (g_abGlobalStringBuffer at 0x6ff399f0)\n4. Call STORM.DLL ordinal 501 string copy function with bounds checking\n5. Return success code (1) to indicate operation completed\n\nParameters:\nlpszSource (char *): Pointer to source null-terminated string to copy\n\nReturns:\n1: String copy operation completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x7fffffff (2147483647): Maximum signed 32-bit integer used as\n  safety limit for string copy operation to prevent buffer overflow\n\nError Handling:\nFunction always returns 1 (success) - actual error handling delegated to\nSTORM.DLL ordinal 501 implementation",
