      "name": "SkipEOL",
      "signature": "char * SkipEOL(void * this, char * param_1, char * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Advances a character pointer past all consecutive end-of-line characters within bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointers - ensure start pointer is less than end pointer\n2. Loop while character is not null terminator:\n   a. Load current character at input pointer position\n   b. Check if character is carriage return (0x0D) or line feed (0x0A)\n   c. If neither CR nor LF, return current position (non-EOL character found)\n   d. Increment input pointer to skip EOL character\n   e. Validate pointer hasn't exceeded end boundary\n3. Return updated pointer position (either at non-EOL char or end boundary)\n\nParameters:\nthis - BNGatewayAccess instance pointer (unused in implementation)\nlpszInput - Starting character position to scan from\nlpszEnd - End boundary pointer, scanning stops when this is reached\n\nReturns:\nchar* - Updated pointer position:\n  - Points to first non-EOL character if found\n  - Points to end boundary if reached during scanning\n  - Points to original position if bounds check fails initially\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input pointer >= end pointer: Returns input pointer unchanged\n- Null terminator encountered: Returns position at null terminator\n- All characters are EOL until boundary: Returns end boundary position\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0D (13) - Carriage return character '\\r'\n0x0A (10) - Line feed character '\n'",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
