      "name": "ProcessNetworkCredentials",
      "signature": "int ProcessNetworkCredentials(uint dwUserId, uint dwPasswordLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Process network authentication credentials for user login.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy password data to local buffer using Ordinal_501 with 128-byte limit\n2. Calculate password string length using Ordinal_506\n3. Convert password to lowercase using CharLowerBuffA for case-insensitive comparison\n4. Generate password hash using FUN_6ff2acd0 into hash buffer\n5. Copy user ID data to separate buffer using Ordinal_501 with 128-byte limit\n6. Send authentication packet with validation via SendNetworkPacketWithValidation\n7. Return success status code (1)\n\nParameters:\n- dwUserId: User identification value passed in ECX register\n- dwPasswordLength: Length of password data passed in EDX register\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Authentication packet sent successfully\n- Function appears to always return success (no visible error paths)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Password buffer limited to 128 bytes (0x80) to prevent overflow\n- User ID buffer also limited to 128 bytes (0x80)\n- Password converted to lowercase for standardized comparison\n- Uses ordinal imports for memory operations (likely kernel32 functions)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x80 (128): Buffer size limit for both password and user ID data\n- 0x1: Success return value\n- 0x114 (276): Total stack frame size allocated",
