      "name": "InitializeRandomGeneratorStates",
      "signature": "uint InitializeRandomGeneratorStates(byte * pStateBuffer, uint dwStateCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes or reinitializes random number generator state buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return success (1) immediately if stateCount is 0\n2. Initialize loop counter to 0, setup pointers to seed buffer (state+1) and random data buffer (state+2)\n3. Loop for each state index from 0 to stateCount-1:\n   a. Check if index reached maximum limit (0xFF), return failure (0) if exceeded\n   b. Load state byte from pStateBuffer[loopCounter]\n   c. If state is 0x00 (uninitialized): call SMemRandom to generate 256 bytes, set seed to 0x01, mark state as 0xFF\n   d. If state is 0xFF (needs reinitialization): call SMemRandom to generate 256 bytes, set seed to 0xFF, mark state as 0xFF\n   e. Increment all pointers (pCurrentStateEntry, pSeedByte, pRandomDataBuffer) and loop counter\n4. Return success (1) after processing all states\n\nParameters:\npStateBuffer - Pointer to state buffer array containing state entries (passed in EBX via __fastcall)\nstateCount - Number of state entries to process (passed on stack via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, all states initialized/reinitialized successfully\n0 - Failure, state index exceeded maximum limit (0xFF/255)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Maximum state index is 0xFF (255); function fails if reached\n- State value 0x00 indicates uninitialized state requiring random data generation\n- State value 0xFF indicates state requiring reinitialization with new random data\n- SMemRandom called with 0x100 (256) bytes for random data buffer\n- Each state entry occupies 258 bytes total: [state_flag:1][seed_value:1][random_data:256]\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n------  ----  -----------   --------  ----------------------------------\n+0x0    1     stateFlag     byte      State indicator (0x00=uninit, 0xFF=init)\n+0x1    1     seedValue     byte      Seed value (0x01 for init, 0xFF for reinit)\n+0x2    256   randomData    byte[256] Random data from SMemRandom call",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:7160d3a08bcde6dc3638147356e99635",
