      "name": "InitializeRandomNumberGenerator",
      "signature": "int InitializeRandomNumberGenerator(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize the random number generator for cryptographic operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8 bytes on stack for local variables\n2. Clear EAX and test EDX register value\n3. Set AL to 1 if EDX is non-zero (condition flag)\n4. Prepare parameters for randomization: base offset 0x8, size 0x16 (22 bytes)\n5. Load stack pointer into EDI to reference local randomDataBuffer\n6. Store condition flag at stack offset 0xc\n7. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData with prepared parameters\n8. Set return value to 1 (success)\n9. Restore EDI and clean up stack, return to caller\n\nParameters:\nEDX (implicit) - Condition flag from caller context\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGenerateCryptographicRandomData performs actual randomization only if global state allows it:\n- g_dwRNGInitEnabled must be non-zero (RNG subsystem enabled)\n- g_dwRNGStateOverride must be zero (no override active)\nIf these conditions are not met, the operation is cancelled.\n\nThe function generates cryptographic random data with base offset 0x8 and buffer size 0x16 bytes\nusing the cryptographically secure random number generator from the Win32 API via SMemRandom.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
