      "name": "InitializeGameLogging",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameLogging(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game logging system for diagnostic and event logging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call WriteLogFile to log initialization message to \"BnetLog.txt\" with priority 0\n2. Push exit handler function address (InitializeDefaultLoggingBuffer) onto stack\n3. Call _atexit to register the exit handler for process termination cleanup\n4. Pop return value from _atexit call\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The logging file path is \"BnetLog.txt\" which may be in the game directory\n- Priority level 0 used for initialization logging messages\n- Exit handler (InitializeDefaultLoggingBuffer) ensures graceful shutdown and buffer flushing when the application terminates\n- This function is registered as a one-time initialization routine",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
