      "name": "InitializeMD5State",
      "signature": "void InitializeMD5State(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes MD5 hash state to standard initial values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set state[0] to 0x67452301 (A initialization constant)\n2. Set state[1] to 0xefcdab89 (B initialization constant)\n3. Set state[2] to 0x98badcfe (C initialization constant)\n4. Set state[3] to 0x10325476 (D initialization constant)\n5. Set state[4] to 0xc3d2e1f0 (E initialization constant)\n\nParameters:\n- pState: Pointer to array of at least 5 uint32 values to hold MD5 state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- These are the standard MD5 initial hash constants as defined in RFC 1321\n- The constants are derived from the 32-bit binary representation of sin(i+1) where i=0..4\n- State values are stored in little-endian format as unsigned 32-bit integers",
