      "name": "Int64ToCharInternal",
      "signature": "void Int64ToCharInternal(int nLow, int nHigh, char * szOutput, uint dwRadix, int nSigned)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Convert signed/unsigned 64-bit integer to string with base radix (2-36).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nSigned flag set, prefix output with '-' and negate the 64-bit value (nHigh:nLow)\n2. Loop: divide 64-bit value by dwRadix, get remainder via __aullrem\n3. Convert remainder (0-35) to ASCII digit: 0-9 -> '0'-'9', 10-35 -> 'A'-'Z'\n4. Store digit at current position, advance write pointer\n5. Continue until quotient is zero\n6. Null-terminate string\n7. Reverse string by swapping head/tail bytes inward until pointers meet\n\nParameters:\n- nLow: low 32 bits of 64-bit value (int)\n- nHigh: high 32 bits of 64-bit value (int)\n- szOutput: pointer to output buffer (char *)\n- dwRadix: conversion base 2-36 (uint)\n- nSigned: non-zero to treat as signed, add minus sign if negative (int)\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies szOutput in-place, null-terminated)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input value 0 outputs \"0\"\n- Negative values get minus sign prefix\n- Base-10 typical usage, base-16 for hex conversion\n- dwRemain type is undefined8 from __aullrem return (uint in practice)\n\nStructure Layout: None",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:369c5cc3a730f9873f64436a6d5d84ba",
