      "name": "InitializeSHA1Context",
      "signature": "void InitializeSHA1Context(SHA1_CTX * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize SHA-1 hash context with standard initial values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear ECX register to zero for initialization value\n2. Set h0 to 0x67452301 (SHA-1 initial value A per FIPS 180-1)\n3. Set h1 to 0xefcdab89 (SHA-1 initial value B per FIPS 180-1)\n4. Set h2 to 0x98badcfe (SHA-1 initial value C per FIPS 180-1)\n5. Set h3 to 0x10325476 (SHA-1 initial value D per FIPS 180-1)\n6. Set h4 to 0xc3d2e1f0 (SHA-1 initial value E per FIPS 180-1)\n7. Clear bytesProcessedHigh counter (+0x18 offset in context)\n8. Clear bytesProcessedLow counter (+0x14 offset in context)\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - SHA1_CTX pointer (passed in EAX via __fastcall) - Pointer to uninitialized SHA1_CTX structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - Context initialized in place with standard SHA-1 initial state values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses FIPS 180-1 standard SHA-1 initialization constants\n  - Byte processed counters set to zero for fresh hash operation\n  - Context modified in place; caller must ensure valid pointer passed in EAX\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type | Description\n-------|------|---------------------|------|------------------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | h0                  | uint | SHA-1 state A = 0x67452301\n+0x04  |  4   | h1                  | uint | SHA-1 state B = 0xefcdab89\n+0x08  |  4   | h2                  | uint | SHA-1 state C = 0x98badcfe\n+0x0c  |  4   | h3                  | uint | SHA-1 state D = 0x10325476\n+0x10  |  4   | h4                  | uint | SHA-1 state E = 0xc3d2e1f0\n+0x14  |  4   | bytesProcessedLow   | uint | Low 32 bits of bytes processed\n+0x18  |  4   | bytesProcessedHigh  | uint | High 32 bits of bytes processed\n+0x1c  | 64   | buffer              | byte | Message block buffer (512 bits)\n-------|------|---------------------|------|------------------------------------------\nTotal: 92 bytes",
