      "name": "ProcessDownloadCallback",
      "signature": "int ProcessDownloadCallback(void * pCallbackParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Maps download callback status codes to file download operation flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load callback status code from parameter structure offset +0x0\n2. Compare status code with 0x80000005 (STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW)\n3. If buffer overflow status detected, jump to error handling path\n4. Compare status code with 0x80000006 (STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE)\n5. Load default download flags value 4 for non-error status codes\n6. If invalid handle status detected, jump to error handling path\n7. Set download flags to 2 for both error status conditions\n8. OR flags with 0x1 to enable download operation bit\n9. Call InitiateFileDownload with mapped flags and source/dest paths\n10. Return 1 to indicate successful callback processing\n\nParameters:\npCallbackParams (__fastcall ECX): Pointer to callback parameter structure containing:\n  - Offset +0x0 (DWORD): Status code to be mapped to download flags\n  - Offset +0x8 (char*): Source file path\n  - Offset +0x10 (char*): Destination file path\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating callback processed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW (0x80000005) and STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE (0x80000006) both map to flags = 2\n- All other status codes default to flags = 4\n- Final flags value before download call: 3 (2|1) or 5 (4|1) based on status\n- Function always returns success even for error status codes",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:70b44c5d739084829a1ea4bb1abe7121",
