      "name": "ValidateAndProcessCryptographicData",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndProcessCryptographicData(char * szInputData, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates input string and flags before performing cryptographic processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if szInputData pointer is not null\n2. Test if szInputData is not an empty string (first byte != 0)\n3. Test if nFlags parameter is non-zero\n4. If all three validations succeed, call cryptographic processor with magic constant 0x80000006\n5. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\nszInputData (char *) - Pointer to input string to validate and process. Passed in ECX register via __fastcall convention.\nnFlags (int) - Flags parameter controlling whether processing should occur. Must be non-zero to trigger processing. Passed in EDX register via __fastcall convention.\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success code), regardless of whether validation checks passed or processing was skipped.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If szInputData is null pointer, validation fails silently and returns success\n- If szInputData points to empty string (first byte is 0x00), validation fails silently and returns success  \n- If nFlags is 0, validation fails silently and returns success\n- Magic constant 0x80000006 is the cryptographic processing identifier passed to ProcessStringWithMD5AndRandom",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
