      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined1",
      "comment": "Returns a constant byte value of 60 (0x3C).\n\nThis function serves as a constant-returning interface, likely used as a callback or\nvirtual table entry for a function pointer table at 0x6ff3dcc0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load constant 0x3C (60 decimal) into AL register\n2. Return the constant value to caller via RET instruction\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nbyte - Always returns constant value 60 (0x3C). This value likely represents a timing\nconstant such as a frame delay count (60 frames at 25 FPS = 2.4 seconds) or another\ngame mechanic parameter.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Referenced from function pointer table at address 0x6ff3dcc0 with DATA xref\n- The constant 60 (0x3C) is ASCII character '<' which may have semantic meaning",
