      "name": "ValidateAlignmentBoundary",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAlignmentBoundary(ArrayPool * pArrayPool)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates that an alignment boundary value is a valid power of 2.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive alignmentBoundary from ArrayPool.flags field (+0xC)\n2. If alignmentBoundary >= 8, clamp to 8, set ArrayPool.flags=8, return 8\n3. If alignmentBoundary < 8, perform bit-isolation loop: test (n-1) & n\n4. Loop: shift through bits clearing lowest set bit until none remain\n5. After loop, check if final alignmentBoundary equals 1 (valid power-of-2)\n6. If equals 1 or original was 0, return 1 (valid alignment)\n7. Otherwise return calculated alignmentBoundary value\n\nParameters:\npArrayPool (Stack +0x4): Pointer to ArrayPool structure\n  - Used to read alignment boundary from flags field (offset +0xC)\n  - Used to write clamped value if >= 8\n\nReturns:\nEAX: 1 if boundary is valid (power-of-2: 1,2,4,...), 8 if clamped, else non-power-of-2 count\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Boundary 0: Invalid power-of-2 check, returns 0\n- Boundary 1: Valid (2^0), returns 1\n- Boundary 2,4,8,16,...: Valid powers-of-2, return 1\n- Boundary 3,5,6,7: Invalid non-powers-of-2 < 8, return count\n- Boundary >= 8: Clamped to 8 in ArrayPool.flags field",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
