      "name": "Sha1_UpdateBuffer",
      "signature": "void Sha1_UpdateBuffer(uchar * pBuffer, uint nDataLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sha1UpdateBuffer - Update SHA-1 context with new input data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current bit count from context[5] and extract byte position (0-63) in current block\n2. Calculate new bit count by adding (nDataLength * 8) to context[5], detect 64-bit overflow\n3. If overflow occurred, increment high counter context[6]\n4. Add high bits of nDataLength (for >4GB inputs) to context[6]\n5. Check if input data will cross a 64-byte block boundary (bytePosition + nDataLength >= 64)\n6. If crosses boundary: copy bytes to fill current 64-byte block, process with ProcessSha1Block\n7. Loop: process all remaining complete 64-byte blocks from input with ProcessSha1Block\n8. Copy any partial remaining block data to buffer for next update call\n\nParameters:\npBuffer: Pointer to input data buffer containing bytes to add to SHA-1 hash\nnDataLength: Number of bytes in pBuffer to process\npContext (EBX): Implicit pointer to SHA1_CTX structure (modified in place)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates SHA-1 context in place, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input length 0 still updates bit counter but does no block processing\n- Partial blocks are buffered in context[7..31], not processed until complete\n- 64-bit bit counter can handle inputs larger than 4GB\n- Context[5] = bit count low dword, Context[6] = bit count high dword\n- Context[7..31] = 25-dword message buffer for partial block storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:996569cbec98d4b86028ce8125738a27",
