      "name": "FastcallToStdcallAdapter621",
      "signature": "void FastcallToStdcallAdapter621(uint param1, uint param2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Calling convention adapter wrapper for external ordinal 621.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push EAX register value (implicit third parameter) onto stack\n2. Push ECX register value (first fastcall parameter) onto stack\n3. Push EDX register value (second fastcall parameter) onto stack\n4. Call DispatchExternalOrdinal621 with three stack-based parameters in order [EDX, ECX, EAX]\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  param1 (ECX): uint - First parameter in ECX register\n  param2 (EDX): uint - Second parameter in EDX register\n  IMPLICIT param3Eax (EAX): uint - Third parameter in EAX register\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; result managed by external ordinal function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This adapter converts __fastcall convention to __cdecl stack-based calling convention\n  Used to bridge callers that use fastcall with external ordinal 621 dispatch\n  Parameter order on stack: [EDX, ECX, EAX] due to push order (reverse of register order)",
