      "name": "ExportObjectDataWithPadding",
      "signature": "void * ExportObjectDataWithPadding(void * pObject, uint bufferSize, char * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ArrayPool *",
      "comment": "Exports object data to buffer with zero-padding for unused space\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX and ESI registers to stack\n2. Copy bufferSize parameter from EAX to ESI\n3. Get address of local bytesWritten variable from stack (ESP+4)\n4. Call ExportObjectData with buffer, object, size, and output pointer for bytes written\n5. Load actual bytes written from stack location into EAX\n6. Compare bytes written (EAX) against requested buffer size (ESI)\n7. If bytes written < buffer size, calculate remaining bytes (ESI - EAX)\n8. Call ZeroMemory to fill remainder of buffer from (bytesWritten + buffer base) for (bufferSize - bytesWritten) bytes\n9. Load and return pointer to bytesWritten stack value in EAX\n\nParameters:\npObject - Pointer to source object to export (passed in ECX register via __d2regcall)\nbufferSize - Maximum size of output buffer in bytes (passed in EAX register via __d2regcall)\npOutputBuffer - Destination buffer for exported data (passed in EDI register via __d2regcall)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to uint value on stack containing actual bytes written to buffer. Return value allows caller to determine how much data was serialized.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses custom __d2regcall convention: parameters in ECX, EAX, EDI registers\n- ZeroMemory called only when bytesWritten < bufferSize (conditional optimization)\n- Buffer fully initialized: either contains exported data or zero-filled remainder\n- Return value points to stack frame location containing the byte count (not the bytes written value itself)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
