      "name": "CleanupObjectData",
      "signature": "void CleanupObjectData(ObjectData * * ppObjectData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "CleanupObjectData - Destroys child objects and clears object data pointer\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load the ObjectData pointer from the double pointer parameter stored in ESI\\n2. Check if the status field at offset +0x0 is non-zero to determine if cleanup is needed\\n3. If status is non-zero, load and destroy pObject2 from offset +0x8 via DestroyObject()\\n4. Load and destroy pObject1 from offset +0x4 via DestroyObject()\\n5. Set the ObjectData pointer to NULL to prevent reuse\\n6. If status is zero, skip destruction and only set pointer to NULL\\n7. Return void (no return value)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  IMPLICIT ppObjectData (ESI) - Pointer to pointer to ObjectData with child objects\\n    ObjectData structure: status at +0x0, pObject1 at +0x4, pObject2 at +0x8\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - No return value, function always succeeds",
