      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a 76-byte structure with exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up Windows SEH (Structured Exception Handling) by saving FS:[0x0] to stack frame\n2. Call AllocateMemory with size 0x4c (76 bytes), source file path, and line number 0x157\n3. Test if allocation succeeded by checking EAX for NULL pointer\n4. If allocation failed (EAX == NULL), set EAX to NULL and jump to cleanup\n5. If allocation succeeded, initialize two fields to zero:\n   - Field at offset +0x0 (first dword)\n   - Field at offset +0x48 (field index 0x12, the last dword)\n6. Restore SEH state by retrieving previous exception handler from stack\n7. Return with result pointer in EAX (callee cleanup per __stdcall)\n\nParameters: None\nReturns: void* - Pointer to allocated structure (76 bytes), or NULL on allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Memory allocation at 0x4c (76) bytes always\n- Only two fields initialized (0x0 and 0x48); other fields left uninitialized\n- Windows SEH exception handling employed for safety\n- Calling convention is __stdcall (callee cleanup with RET immediate)\n\nStructure Layout (inferred from initialization offsets):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Purpose\n0x00   | 4    | field_0    | dword| Initialized to zero\n0x04   | 68   | ...        | ...  | Uninitialized fields\n0x48   | 4    | field_18   | dword| Initialized to zero (offset 0x48 = index 0x12)",
