      "name": "ComputeSha1Hash",
      "signature": "void ComputeSha1Hash(uint * pDataBuffer1, uint * pDataBuffer2, uint * pDataBuffer3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes SHA-1 cryptographic hash from three concatenated input buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SHA-1 state with standard initial hash values (0x67452301, 0xefcdab89, 0x98badcfe, 0x10325476, 0xc3d2e1f0)\n2. Process first input buffer (32 bytes / 0x20) via Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n3. Process second input buffer (20 bytes / 0x14) via Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n4. Process third input buffer (40 bytes / 0x28) via Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n5. Finalize SHA-1 computation and produce hash digest\n\nParameters:\n- pDataBuffer1: Pointer to first data buffer (32 bytes)\n- pDataBuffer2: Pointer to second data buffer (20 bytes)\n- pDataBuffer3: Pointer to third data buffer (40 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- Hash digest stored in local stack buffer (5 dwords = 20 bytes SHA-1 output)\n- Final state buffer address passed to Sha1_Finalize for finalization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Total input data: 92 bytes concatenated for hashing\n- SHA-1 produces 20-byte (160-bit) cryptographic hash digest\n- Stack frame: 0x5c bytes (92 bytes) allocated for state and intermediate values\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleanup: RET 0xC)",
