      "name": "ComputeHmacSha1",
      "signature": "void ComputeHmacSha1(int nContextPtr, uchar * pSecretKey, uchar * pSha1InitVectors1, uchar * pSha1InitVectors2, uchar * pSha1InitVectors3, uchar * pSha1InitVectors4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Compute HMAC-SHA1 authentication code using SHA1 cryptographic hashing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Export inner padding data from context structure at offset +8 into 32-byte working buffer\n2. If exported inner padding size is less than 0x20 bytes, zero-fill the remaining buffer space\n3. Initialize SHA1 state registers with RFC 3174 standard constants (A=0x67452301, B=0xefcdab89, C=0x98badcfe, D=0x10325476, E=0xc3d2e1f0)\n4. Process inner padded buffer data through SHA1 update and finalization functions\n5. Export outer padding data from context structure at offset +4 into working buffer\n6. If exported outer padding size is less than 0x20 bytes, zero-fill the remaining buffer space\n7. Reinitialize SHA1 state registers and process outer padded buffer through SHA1 functions\n8. XOR-combine inner and outer hash results byte-by-byte in 5-byte loop iterations (total 20 bytes processed)\n9. Retrieve secret key string length using strlen() for null-terminated C string\n10. Reinitialize SHA1 state and process secret key through SHA1 update function\n11. Initialize final SHA1 state and sequentially process XORed hash (0x14 bytes), outer hash (0x14 bytes), input vector 1 (0x20 bytes), input vector 2 (0x20 bytes), input vector 3 (0x20 bytes), and input vector 4 (0x28 bytes)\n12. Finalize SHA1 computation to produce HMAC-SHA1 result\n\nParameters:\nnContextPtr: int - Pointer to context structure containing padding buffers at offsets +4 (outer) and +8 (inner)\npSecretKey: uchar * - Pointer to null-terminated secret key string for HMAC computation\npSha1InitVectors1: uchar * - First input vector buffer (32 bytes)\npSha1InitVectors2: uchar * - Second input vector buffer (32 bytes)\npSha1InitVectors3: uchar * - Third input vector buffer (32 bytes)\npSha1InitVectors4: uchar * - Fourth input vector buffer (40 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value. HMAC-SHA1 result is stored in the SHA1 state array maintained as local variable throughout computation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Inner and outer padding buffers are zero-filled if exported size is less than 32 bytes\n- XOR loop processes exactly 20 bytes in 5-byte strides for optimal performance\n- Secret key length is calculated using strlen() assuming null-terminated ASCII string\n- SHA1 state array (24 DWORDs) is reinitialized multiple times for cascading hash computations\n- Standard RFC 3174 SHA1 initial vectors are used for all hash state initializations",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
