      "name": "ComputeDualSha1Hash",
      "signature": "void ComputeDualSha1Hash(LPCSTR pInputString, LPBYTE pHashOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes dual-channel SHA-1 hashes for input string data with runtime-dependent secret integration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize first SHA-1 hash state with RFC 3174 standard constants (A=0x67452301, B=0xefcdab89, C=0x98badcfe, D=0x10325476, E=0xc3d2e1f0)\n2. Get length of input string using strlen(pInputString)\n3. Update SHA-1 with input string data via Sha1_UpdateBuffer(pInputString, strlen_result)\n4. Get length and process global padding constant (g_pszPaddingConstant) via strlen and Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n5. Get length and process ESI register string data via strlen and Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n6. Finalize first SHA-1 computation via Sha1_Finalize, storing 20-byte hash in sha1HashResult\n7. Reinitialize SHA-1 state with same RFC 3174 constants for second hash computation (A-E reset, counters cleared)\n8. Update SHA-1 with first hash result (0x20 bytes) via Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n9. Update SHA-1 with local hash buffer (0x14 bytes) via Sha1_UpdateBuffer\n10. Finalize second SHA-1 computation via Sha1_Finalize\n11. Call ResolveImportedFunction_Ordinal624 to obtain runtime-dependent secret value\n12. Call ImportObjectData to import/process secret into 20-byte buffer with second hash\n13. Store result pointer in output parameter via pHashOutput[0]\n\nParameters:\npInputString: Pointer to null-terminated input string for first-pass hashing\npHashOutput: Pointer to destination for final result pointer (receives address of 20-byte hash)\n\nReturns:\nNone - result pointer written to memory location specified by pHashOutput parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SHA-1 state uses standard RFC 3174 initialization constants repeated for dual-pass computation\n- Function preserves ESI register for implicit state data during processing\n- Uses unaffected registers (ESI, EDI, EBP) for state preservation across function calls\n- ResolveImportedFunction_Ordinal624 provides runtime-dependent secret value (dynamically resolved)\n- Final result is obtained through ImportObjectData call, suggesting encrypted/obfuscated storage or runtime transformation\n- Global g_pszPaddingConstant referenced at 0x6ff3e300 points to data at 0x6ff3b02c\n- Total stack allocation: 0x74 bytes (116 bytes) for local SHA-1 state and result buffer",
