      "name": "ProcessSha1InputBuffer",
      "signature": "void ProcessSha1InputBuffer(SHA1_CTX * pHashContext, uchar * pInputBuffer, uint dwInputLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Incrementally processes input buffer data through SHA-1 hash computation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if input length is zero\n2. Load SHA-1 context pointer and current buffer fill level from context[0x48]\n3. If buffer has remaining space, fill buffer with input bytes until full or input exhausted\n4. For each full 64-byte block in input:\n   a. Copy bytes from input to internal buffer (DW copy + remainder)\n   b. Update SHA-1 intermediate hash values from context offsets 0x0c, 0x34, 0x20\n   c. Call Sha1_UpdateBuffer for hash block A (20 bytes from 0x0c)\n   d. Call Sha1_UpdateBuffer for hash block E (20 bytes from 0x34)\n   e. Call Sha1_UpdateBuffer for hash block C (20 bytes from 0x20)\n   f. Call Sha1_Finalize to complete one hash round\n   g. Reset buffer fill level to 0x14 (20 bytes, accounting for overlap/state)\n5. Copy any remaining input bytes to buffer without processing\n6. Update context[0x48] with new buffer fill level\n\nParameters:\n- pHashContext: Pointer to SHA1_CTX structure (92 bytes)\n- pInputBuffer: Source buffer with input data to hash\n- inputLength: Number of input bytes to process\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Modifies SHA1_CTX in place.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty input (inputLength == 0): Function returns without processing\n- Partial block: Remaining bytes copied to buffer but not processed until next call\n- Buffer management: Context stores partial state at offset 0x48 between calls\n- State persistence: Hash state (A/E/C) accumulated across multiple calls",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:07ed516e62d486112195861acf22fc26",
