      "name": "InitializeSha1RandomHash",
      "signature": "void InitializeSha1RandomHash(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes SHA-1 hash with cryptographically random seed for session tokens.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system time (32-bit Unix timestamp) via GetCurrentUnixTime32()\n2. Seed thread-local random number generator with time value via SeedThreadRandomNumber()\n3. Generate 32-bit random number via _rand() for additional entropy\n4. Initialize SHA-1 hash state with standard FIPS 180-1 constants (h0-h4)\n5. Initialize SHA-1 bit counters to zero (for 0-length message)\n6. Update SHA-1 context with 12 bytes of time buffer data via Sha1_UpdateBuffer()\n7. Finalize SHA-1 computation to produce 20-byte digest via Sha1_Finalize()\n8. Copy 20-byte digest to output buffer at offsets +0x20 through +0x30 (5 dwords)\n9. Zero-initialize padding fields at offsets +0x34 through +0x48 (5 dwords)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EAX (in_EAX): randomSeed value passed by caller for entropy\nIMPLICIT EBX (pSha1Context): Pointer to SHA1_CTX structure (80+ bytes minimum)\nIMPLICIT ESI (unaff_ESI): Pointer to output buffer structure (0x48+ bytes minimum)\nIMPLICIT EDI (pOutputBuffer): Pointer to 20-byte hash digest buffer from Sha1_Finalize\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies output buffer with initialized SHA-1 digest at offsets +0x20-+0x30\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SHA-1 constants per FIPS 180-1: h0=0x67452301, h1=0xEFCDAB89, h2=0x98BADCFE, h3=0x10325476, h4=0xC3D2E1F0\n- Bit counters start at zero for empty message (0 bits processed initially)\n- Time buffer contains __time32_t result (Unix timestamp) - exactly 12 bytes copied to SHA-1\n- Output buffer stores final 20-byte digest at offset +0x20-+0x30 (5 consecutive dwords)\n- Padding fields at +0x34-+0x48 are zeroed to ensure consistent buffer initialization\n- Uses thread-local CRT random functions requiring initialized process state",
