      "name": "ComputeContextHash",
      "signature": "void ComputeContextHash(HashContextState * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes SHA-1 hash from three data buffers within a hash context state structure.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load pointer to first data buffer at context offset +0x60 (32 bytes)\\n2. Load pointer to second data buffer at context offset +0xe8 (20 bytes)\\n3. Load pointer to third data buffer at context offset +0xc0 (40 bytes)\\n4. Call ComputeSha1Hash with three buffer pointers to compute SHA-1 digest\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pContext (IMPLICIT EAX): Pointer to HashContextState structure containing data buffers\\n  - The context pointer is passed implicitly in EAX register\\n  - Contains three data buffers at specific offsets for hash computation\\n\\nReturns:\\n- void - Hash computation performed in called function\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Total input data: 92 bytes (32 + 20 + 40 bytes from three buffers)\\n- SHA-1 produces 160-bit (20-byte) cryptographic hash digest\\n- Uses custom calling convention with implicit EAX parameter (not ECX)\\n- EDI preserved across call (pushed at entry, restored before return)\\n- Callee cleanup: RET 0x4 (single parameter removed from stack)\\n\\nStructure Layout (HashContextState):\\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type      | Description\\n-------|------|---------------|-----------|---------------------------\\n  +0x60 |   32 | dataBuffer1   | byte[32]  | First hash input buffer\\n  +0xc0 |   40 | dataBuffer3   | byte[40]  | Third hash input buffer\\n  +0xe8 |   20 | dataBuffer2   | byte[20]  | Second hash input buffer\\n-------|------|---------------|-----------|---------------------------\\nTotal: 304 bytes (HashContextState structure)",
