      "name": "ProcessSha1ObjectTransformation",
      "signature": "void ProcessSha1ObjectTransformation(void * pContextObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "SHA1-based cryptographic transformation of object data with import/export operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and initialize sourceData1 object container via ordinal 624 function\n2. Import 32-byte input from pBufferBase+0x20 into sourceData1 via ImportObjectData\n3. Process SHA1 hash of buffer at pBufferBase+0x80 via ProcessSha1InputBuffer\n4. Allocate and initialize sourceData2 object container via ordinal 624 function\n5. Import 32-byte input from pBufferBase+0x80 into sourceData2 via ImportObjectData\n6. Allocate and initialize empty transformedObject container via ordinal 624 function\n7. Initialize transformedObject with zero value via InitializeObjectWithValue\n8. Load vtable pointer from pContextObject and extract iterator function pointers\n9. Dispatch iterator operation to setup container traversal via ForwardToOperationHandler\n10. Compare transformedObject size against container size limit from vtable+0x8\n11. Enter size-constrained processing loop: while transformedObject size > limit, call ProcessOrCopyObjectData and re-compare\n12. Destroy sourceData2 temporary object via DestroyObject\n13. Destroy sourceData1 temporary object via DestroyObject\n14. Export transformedObject to pBufferBase+0xa0 (up to 32 bytes) via ExportObjectData\n15. If export count < 32 bytes, zero-fill remaining bytes via ZeroMemory\n16. Destroy transformedObject container and return\n\nParameters:\n- pContextObject: Pointer to context object with vtable containing function pointers for iterator dispatch and size comparison\n- IMPLICIT pBufferBase (EBX): Base address of 256-byte data buffer used for all buffer operations\n\nReturns:\n- void - Result stored at pBufferBase+0xa0 (SHA1 transformation output)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Size limit enforcement: Loop continues until transformedObject size <= container size from vtable\n- Partial export: If exported bytes < 32, remainder filled with zeros to complete 32-byte output\n- Container iteration: Vtable at pContextObject+0x0, functions at offsets +0x4 (dispatch) and +0x8 (size check)\n- Magic constant 0x20: Used for all 32-byte buffer operations (input, output, comparison)",
