      "name": "VerifyComputedSha1Hash",
      "signature": "bool VerifyComputedSha1Hash(void * pGameState, uint * pExpectedHash)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Verifies that a computed SHA-1 hash matches an expected hash value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Prepare three offset-based pointers to game state data regions:\n   - Region 1 at pGameState + 0x80 (third hash region, 40 bytes)\n   - Region 2 at pGameState + 0xa8 (second hash region, 20 bytes)\n   - Region 3 at pGameState + 0x60 (first hash region, 32 bytes)\n2. Call ComputeSha1Hash to compute SHA-1 digest from three concatenated regions\n3. Store computed 20-byte SHA-1 hash in local stack buffer (5 dwords)\n4. Initialize ECX register with 5 (dword count for comparison)\n5. Use CMPSD.REPE instruction to compare computed hash against expected hash dword-by-dword\n6. Set AL=1 if all 5 dwords match, AL=0 if any dword differs\n7. Return boolean result in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState (void*): Base pointer to game state structure containing three data regions for hashing\n    - Offset +0x60: First hash region (32 bytes)\n    - Offset +0x80: Third hash region (40 bytes)\n    - Offset +0xa8: Second hash region (20 bytes)\n  pExpectedHash (uint*): Pointer to expected SHA-1 hash array (5 dwords = 20 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  bool: true (AL=1) if computed hash matches all 5 dwords of expected hash\n        false (AL=0) if any dword comparison fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Hash verification uses CMPSD.REPE for fast dword-by-dword comparison\n  - Function uses __stdcall convention with callee cleanup of 8 bytes (2 parameters)\n  - Three data regions are non-contiguous within game state but concatenated for hashing\n  - Total input data size: 92 bytes (32 + 40 + 20)",
