      "name": "ProcessCryptographicObjectCollection",
      "signature": "bool ProcessCryptographicObjectCollection(int nObjectHandle, ObjectData * pObjectData, ObjectData * pSourceObject, ObjectData * pTargetObject, ObjectData * pTempBuffer, ObjectData * pContextData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates a cryptographic object collection against hash and size constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute SHA1 hash of the input object using ComputeObjectSha1Hash\n2. Check if hash computation succeeded; return false immediately if hash is NULL\n3. Initialize first crypto context phase via ResolveImportedFunction_Ordinal624\n4. Initialize target object with value 0 using InitializeObjectWithValue\n5. Initialize second crypto context phase via ResolveImportedFunction_Ordinal624\n6. Initialize temp buffer with hash object reference using InitializeObjectWithValue\n7. Process collection item using ForwardToOperationHandler with source and hash objects\n8. Destroy temp buffer and load context size from contextPointer offset +0x8\n9. Process external ordinal using ProcessCollectionItem with hash and context size\n10. Dispatch iterator operation via DispatchExternalOrdinal621\n11. Initialize temp buffer with value 1\n12. Compare hash object size against 1 using CompareObjectSize\n13. Destroy temp buffer and check comparison result\n14. If hash size > 1: proceed to full validation path\n15. If hash size <= 1: skip to cleanup and return false\n16. Initialize iterator buffer with value 0\n17. Initialize temp buffer with value 1\n18. Dispatch iterator operation on buffers using DispatchIteratorOperation\n19. Destroy temp buffer\n20. Compare iterator buffer size against context size from offset +0x8\n21. If sizes not equal: destroy iterator buffer and return true (success)\n22. If sizes equal: destroy iterator buffer and return false (validation failed)\n23. Cleanup: destroy hash object in both code paths and return result\n\nParameters:\n- nObjectHandle (ECX): Handle to cryptographic object to process\n- pObjectData (EDX): Pointer to ObjectData structure containing hash information\n- pSourceObject (Stack[0x4]): Pointer to source ObjectData for collection item processing\n- pTargetObject (Stack[0x8]): Pointer to target ObjectData for result storage\n- pTempBuffer (Stack[0xc]): Pointer to temporary ObjectData buffer for operations\n- pContextData (Stack[0x10]): Pointer to context ObjectData with configuration (implicit via EDI)\n\nReturns:\n- bool (EAX): true (1) if collection validation passed; false (0) if validation failed or hash computation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL hash result: Immediate return with false value\n- Context size validation: Uses offset +0x8 from context pointer (contains size threshold)\n- Size comparison logic: Returns true if computed size differs from context threshold, false if equal\n- Memory management: All temporary objects destroyed in all execution paths to prevent leaks\n- EDI register: Contains implicit context pointer used for accessing offset +0x8 (context size field)",
