      "name": "ValidateAndProcessCryptoObject",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndProcessCryptoObject(CryptoState * pKeyContext, ObjectData * pInputData, ObjectData * pOutputData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and processes cryptographic object data using HMAC-SHA1 verification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Import initial object data from pInputData parameter (32 bytes)\n2. Initialize temporary object and compare with original imported object\n3. If comparison fails (result != 1), destroy objects and return 0 (validation failed)\n4. Compute SHA1 hash of pInputData content and store result in computedHash variable\n5. Initialize second temporary object with zero value\n6. Import second object data from context buffer at offset +0x40 (32 bytes)\n7. Call ValidateAndProcessObjectHash to validate and process the cryptographic hash\n8. Destroy temporary objects; if validation returns 0, destroy remaining objects and return 0\n9. Export processed object data to hashBuffer local array (max 32 bytes)\n10. If exported size < 0x20 bytes, zero-fill remaining buffer space\n11. Compute dual-channel SHA1 signature from context buffer at offset +0x80\n12. Compute final HMAC-SHA1 verification using multiple context offsets\n13. Return 1 on complete success, 0 on any validation failure\n\nParameters:\npKeyContext - Pointer to CryptoState containing encryption key material and context\npInputData - Pointer to ObjectData input buffer containing object to validate (32 bytes)\npOutputData - Pointer to ObjectData output buffer for processed data (32 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Cryptographic validation succeeded and object was successfully processed\n0 - Validation failed at any stage (size comparison, hash validation, or size export)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEDI (implicit parameter) - Context structure containing:\n  +0x00 - Scratch buffer for object operations (32 bytes)\n  +0x20 - Secondary object storage (32 bytes)\n  +0x40 - Source object data for second validation phase (32 bytes)\n  +0x60 - HMAC-SHA1 output buffer (32 bytes)\n  +0x80 - SHA1 computation workspace (40+ bytes)\n  +0xa8 - Additional context for dual-channel computation\n\nMagic Values:\n0x20 (32) - Standard object/buffer size for crypto operations\n0x1 - Successful comparison result from CompareObjectSize",
