      "comment": "Algorithm:\n1. Check if caching system is initialized (g_dwCacheInitialized flag)\n2. Verify global cache buffer pointer (g_pGlobalBuffer) is non-NULL\n3. Validate cache header structure:\n   - Version field at +0x0 must equal 1\n   - Count field at +0x4 must match expectedCount parameter\n   - Metadata field at +0x8 must match metadataFlag parameter\n4. If validation passes, iterate through cached strings starting at offset +0xc\n5. For each string in the array:\n   a. Check if string is empty (first byte is null terminator)\n   b. If empty, write null terminator to destination buffer\n   c. If not empty, copy using strncpy with size limit from pSizeArray\n   d. Null-terminate the copied string at destination\n   e. Get original string length using strlen\n   f. Advance source pointer by (strlen + 1) to skip null terminator\n6. Return 1 on success, 0 if cache invalid or uninitialized\n\nParameters:\nexpectedCount: Number of strings expected in cache (passed in ECX register)\nmetadataFlag: Metadata identifier to validate against cache header (passed in EDX register)\npStringArray: Array of destination string buffer pointers for storing copies\npSizeArray: Array of maximum buffer sizes for each destination string\n\nReturns:\n1 if cache is valid and all strings successfully retrieved\n0 if cache is uninitialized, invalid, or validation failed\n\nStructure Layout (Cache Buffer at 0x6ff3f890):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n0x0     4     version         dword     Cache format version (must be 1)\n0x4     4     stringCount     dword     Number of cached strings\n0x8     4     metadataFlag    dword     Metadata identifier for cache\n0xc     var   stringData      bytes     Null-terminated strings sequential\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if g_dwCacheInitialized is 0\n- Early return if g_pGlobalBuffer pointer is NULL\n- Empty strings result in single null terminator at destination\n- String offsets calculated as (strlen + 1) to account for null terminators\n- Uses __fastcall convention with ECX/EDX for first two parameters",
