      "name": "CopyAndCachePacketBuffer",
      "signature": "void CopyAndCachePacketBuffer(void * pSourceBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies packet buffer to global cache with network byte order conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global cached buffer pointer (g_pCachedPacketBuffer) and test if exists\n2. If buffer exists, free it using memory pool 0x3e2\n3. Clear global cache pointer to null\n4. Allocate new buffer of size (bufferSize+4) using AllocateBuffer with pool 0x3eb\n5. Store bufferSize at offset +0x0 as size header\n6. Set destination pointer to offset +0x4 (data area start)\n7. Store allocated buffer pointer in global cache (g_pCachedPacketBuffer)\n8. Perform optimized copy of bufferSize bytes from source to allocated buffer\n9. Calculate DWORD count (bufferSize >> 2) and use REP MOVSD for bulk copy\n10. Calculate remaining bytes (bufferSize & 3) and use REP MOVSB for tail\n11. Check if bufferSize > 0x48 (72 bytes) AND bufferSize != 8\n12. If true, load word at offset +0x18 from buffer start\n13. Convert word from network to host byte order using ntohs()\n14. Store converted word back at offset +0x18\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceBuffer (void *) - Pointer to source packet buffer to copy\n  bufferSize (uint in EBX) - IMPLICIT register parameter: size in bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies global cache pointer (g_pCachedPacketBuffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  bufferSize == 8 skips network conversion (protocol version/flags)\n  bufferSize <= 0x48 skips conversion (minimum threshold)\n  Offset +0x18 is protocol header flags requiring endian conversion\n  Pool IDs: 0x3eb allocate, 0x3e2 free",
