      "name": "InitializeCryptographicContext",
      "signature": "uint InitializeCryptographicContext(HashDataBuffer * pHashData, char * szSeedString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the cryptographic context by performing multi-stage hash operations and generating secure random data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pHashData pointer is not null, return 0 if null\n2. Load global cryptographic context handle from g_hCryptographicContext\n3. Increment global sequence counter g_dwCryptographicSequenceCounter and store locally\n4. Calculate length of szSeedString using inline strlen loop (subtract 1 for offset)\n5. Compute SHA-1 hash of the seed string using calculated length\n6. Compute SHA-1 hash of the sequence counter and local state (0x1c bytes total)\n7. Compute MD5 hash of the input hash data buffer (256 bytes)\n8. Clear two global state fields (g_dwCryptographicStateField1 and g_dwCryptographicStateField2) to zero\n9. Generate cryptographic random data using GenerateCryptographicRandomData with resource identifier 0x3e\n10. Check if random data generation succeeded (result >= 0)\n11. If succeeded, wait for resource 0x3e to be ready using WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout\n12. Return the global result value from g_dwCryptographicResultValue on success, or 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\npHashData - Pointer to HashDataBuffer (256-byte buffer) containing hash data to be processed with MD5\nszSeedString - Null-terminated string used as seed for SHA-1 hash generation\n\nReturns:\nuint - Value from global g_dwCryptographicResultValue on success, 0 on failure or null pointer input\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if pHashData is null\n- Increments global sequence counter with each invocation for unique randomization\n- Magic value 0x3e (62 decimal) used as resource identifier for cryptographic operations\n- SHA-1 hash operation processes 0x1c (28) bytes for counter/state combination\n- MD5 hash processes exactly 0x100 (256) bytes from input buffer\n- Uses __fastcall convention: pHashData in ECX, szSeedString in EDX",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
