      "name": "InitializeCryptographicSeedWithMD5Hash",
      "signature": "uint InitializeCryptographicSeedWithMD5Hash(byte * pInputBuffer1, byte * pInputBuffer2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize cryptographic random number generator seed using MD5 hashing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute indirect jump thunk for security/anti-tampering check\n2. Initialize random seed array with base value 0x44324456 plus conditional offset\n3. Conditionally add 0x13fa to seed if thunk returned non-zero (security check passed)\n4. Set seed array size to 0xd (13 bytes)\n5. Compute MD5 hash of first input buffer (256 bytes) into hash buffer at local_200\n6. Compute MD5 hash of second input buffer (256 bytes) appending to hash buffer\n7. Generate 34 bytes of cryptographic random data using MD5-derived seed\n8. Return success status 1\n\nParameters:\n  pInputBuffer1 - Pointer to first 256-byte input buffer for MD5 hashing\n  pInputBuffer2 - Pointer to second 256-byte input buffer for MD5 hashing\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 indicating successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic value 0x44324456: Base seed initialization constant\n  - Magic value 0x13fa: Conditional offset added if security check passes\n  - Buffer size 0x100 (256): Fixed size for both input buffers\n  - Random data size 0x22 (34): Number of bytes generated for RNG seed\n  - Seed array size 0xd (13): Length of seed data structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
