      "name": "GenerateSeededRandomData",
      "signature": "int GenerateSeededRandomData(char * szSeed1, char * szSeed2, char * szSeed3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Generates cryptographically secure random data by seeding with MD5-hashed input strings\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate three seed string pointers, using empty string default (g_szObfuscatedVerificationData at 0x6ff3a813) for any NULL parameters\n2. Initialize randomOutputBuffer structure (0x1c/28 bytes) to zero in stack space\n3. Check if second seed string (pSeed2) is non-empty and set randomOutputBuffer[0] flag accordingly (1 if non-empty, 0 if empty)\n4. Hash first seed string (pSeed1) using MD5HashData with 0x100 byte limit, storing 16-byte digest in firstHashBuffer\n5. Hash second seed string (pSeed2) with MD5, appending 16-byte digest after first hash at offset [firstHashLength]\n6. Hash third seed string (pSeed3) with MD5, appending 16-byte digest after second hash at offset [firstHashLength + secondHashLength]\n7. Calculate total concatenated hash size and pass to GenerateCryptographicRandomData as seed material\n8. Generate 0x1c (28) bytes of cryptographically secure random data into randomOutputBuffer\n9. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\npSeed1 - First seed string pointer (ECX register via __fastcall), defaults to g_szObfuscatedVerificationData if NULL\npSeed2 - Second seed string pointer (EDX register via __fastcall), defaults to g_szObfuscatedVerificationData if NULL\npSeed3 - Third seed string pointer (loaded from stack at [ESP+0x128]), defaults to g_szObfuscatedVerificationData if NULL\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL seed pointers are substituted with g_szObfuscatedVerificationData constant to ensure deterministic hashing\n- randomOutputBuffer[0] bit flag indicates whether pSeed2 was non-empty (used for randomization context)\n- Each MD5 hash operation is limited to processing 0x100 (256) bytes maximum from input strings\n- Total concatenated hash size (up to 48 bytes for 3 x 16-byte MD5 digests) is used as seed for cryptographic random generation\n- Stack allocation is 0x114 (276) bytes for temporary hash buffers and random output",
