      "name": "InitializeNetworkRandomization",
      "signature": "int InitializeNetworkRandomization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes network randomization and security parameters for connection setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x50c (1292) bytes on stack for working cryptographic buffer\n2. Store magic constant 0x49583836 as seed value 1 (dwSeed1)\n3. Call system random thunk at 0x6ff28126 to retrieve entropy\n4. Negate result and sign-extend using SBB EAX, EAX instruction\n5. Mask sign-extended value with 0x13fa to get random component\n6. Add masked value to 0x44324456 to compute final seed value 2 (dwSeed2)\n7. Load global entropy source from address 0x6ff3f648 (g_dwNetworkEntropySource)\n8. Initialize buffer flags at offsets [ESP+0x14] and [ESP+0x15] to zero\n9. Load buffer base pointer into EDI register\n10. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData with buffer, flags=0x21, size=0xe to finalize randomization\n11. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n1 - Network randomization initialized successfully\n0 - Would indicate initialization failure (not currently returned by this function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0x49583836 is seed component 1\n- Computed seed uses NEG/SBB pattern for sign extension with 0x13fa mask\n- Result added to 0x44324456 for seed component 2\n- Global value g_dwNetworkEntropySource provides additional entropy source\n- Stack allocation is 0x50c bytes for cryptographic buffers and working space\n- Flags value 0x21 indicates specific security initialization mode\n- Size parameter 0xe (14 bytes) specifies randomization buffer length",
