      "name": "InitializeCryptographicBuffer",
      "signature": "int * InitializeCryptographicBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes cryptographic buffer by generating and waiting for random data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global state flags g_dwCryptoInitState1 and g_dwCryptoInitState2 to reset initialization state\n2. Allocate 4-byte buffer on stack (EDI points to buffer location)\n3. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData() with resource ID 0x41 (cryptographic RNG)\n4. Test result for failure (EAX < 0 indicates error)\n5. If generation failed, jump to crypto_failed label and return NULL\n6. Wait for cryptographic resource 0x41 to become ready via WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout()\n7. Load global buffer pointer from g_pGlobalSendBuffer\n8. Test if buffer was allocated (non-NULL check)\n9. If buffer exists, add 4-byte offset and return pointer (skips header/metadata)\n10. If buffer NULL or failed, return NULL\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no explicit parameters. Uses implicit stack pointer (ESP).\n\nReturns:\nint * - Pointer to cryptographic buffer at g_pGlobalSendBuffer + 4 on success\nNULL  - If crypto generation fails (0x41 resource error) or buffer not allocated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Resource ID 0x41 is the cryptographic random number generator resource\n- Buffer offset +4 skips first 4 bytes, suggesting header or metadata storage\n- State flags g_dwCryptoInitState1 and g_dwCryptoInitState2 must be cleared before initialization\n- Calling convention is __stdcall (callee cleanup with RET 0x0 implied)",
