      "name": "ProcessAndHashSecurityData",
      "signature": "int ProcessAndHashSecurityData(SecurityDataBuffer * pDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes and validates security data through cryptographic hashing and transformation pipeline.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 532-byte (0x214) stack workspace for hash buffers and intermediate data\n2. Compute MD5 hash of implicit EAX source buffer (256 bytes), store in primaryHashBuffer\n3. Calculate string length of MD5 hash result (max 32 chars for hex representation)\n4. Convert all hash characters to lowercase using CharLowerBuffA function pointer\n5. Pass lowercase hash through transformation function (0x6ff372c0) for encoding/processing\n6. Compute second MD5 hash of input pDataBuffer parameter (256 bytes), store in secondaryHashBuffer\n7. Increment hash length by 1 for offset calculation (range 1-33)\n8. Add 0x14 bytes to length result to compute final buffer offset\n9. Call finalization function (0x6ff2eb00) with 0x3d (61 decimal) padding size\n10. Return success status code 1\n\nParameters:\npDataBuffer (SecurityDataBuffer *): Pointer to 256-byte security data buffer to be hashed\n\nReturns:\nint: Status code - always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic value 0x3d (61 decimal) represents padding/chunk size for final hashing stage\nFirst hash input comes from implicit EAX parameter (non-standard calling convention detail)\nBoth MD5 operations process fixed 256-byte (0x100) buffers\nHash offset calculation (length + 0x15) suggests fixed 21-byte frame alignment\n\nStack Layout:\nOffset | Size | Name                  | Type          | Description\n-------|------|------------------------|---------------|---------------------------\n-0x214 | 0x100| primaryHashBuffer     | byte[256]     | MD5 hash of EAX source\n-0x114 | 0x14 | processedHashData     | uint[5]       | Transformed hash storage\n-0x100 | 0x100| secondaryHashBuffer   | byte[256]     | MD5 hash of pDataBuffer\n0x0    | 0x4  | pDataBuffer           | SecurityDataBuffer * | Input parameter",
