      "name": "InitializeBattleNetRegistration",
      "signature": "int InitializeBattleNetRegistration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net client registration by loading configuration and generating random data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read \"Registration Version\" configuration value from Configuration section into 4-byte versionData buffer\n2. Read \"Registration Authority\" configuration value from Configuration section into 4-byte authorityData buffer\n3. Read \"Client ID\" configuration value from Configuration section into 4-byte clientIdData buffer\n4. Read \"Client Token\" configuration value from Configuration section into 4-byte tokenData buffer\n5. Initialize randomDataBuffer to 1 (seed value for random number generator)\n6. Zero out bufferTerminator1 and bufferTerminator2 (null terminators)\n7. Generate exactly 0x1e (30) bytes of cryptographic random data starting at randomDataBuffer address\n8. Return success status (1) indicating initialization completed\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The randomDataBuffer initial value of 1 serves as seed for the PRNG\n  - Exactly 30 bytes of cryptographic random data are generated\n  - ReadConfigurationValue called with parameter 2 for all configuration reads\n  - All config reads target the \"Configuration\" section (g_szConfigurationSection)\n  - Buffer terminators (bufferTerminator1/2) are zeroed before random data generation\n  \nConfiguration Keys:\n  - \"Registration Version\" (g_szRegistrationVersionLabel @ 0x6ff3aca8)\n  - \"Registration Authority\" (g_szRegistrationAuthorityLabel @ 0x6ff3ac90)\n  - \"Client ID\" (g_szClientIdLabel @ 0x6ff3ac84)\n  - \"Client Token\" (g_szClientTokenLabel @ 0x6ff3ac74)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
