      "name": "InitializeVerificationSystem",
      "signature": "int InitializeVerificationSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the verification system with cryptographic validation and resource synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear verification flags (g_dwVerificationInitializedFlag, g_dwDownloadProgressFlag)\n2. Hash version string \"ver-IX86-1.mpq\" using MD5 and store result\n3. Set up local buffer with magic header 0x49583836 (\"IX86\") and size field 0x0d\n4. Compute platform-specific signature: ((platform != 0) ? -0x13fa : 0) + 0x44324456\n5. Initialize verification context flags (g_dwContextInitializationFlag, g_dwVerificationErrorFlag) to zero\n6. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData(0x10, 6) - return on error (< 0)\n7. Wait in polling loop for version string to be loaded, checking szVersionFilePath[0]\n8. Exit wait loop if g_dwVerificationInitializedFlag or g_dwCancellationFlag becomes nonzero\n9. Enter critical section and initialize byte flags at g_byRandomDataBuffer/g_byPatchRandomData\n10. Set magic constant 0x66 at g_dwPatchInitializationFlag\n11. Clear 64-byte verification buffer using REP.STOSD pattern\n12. Call VerifyGameFilesWithRevisionCheck to retrieve hash and size\n13. On failure (return 0), call error handler InitializeGlobalStateOnce(1) and return\n14. Call InitializeRandomNumberGenerator with parameter 2\n15. Call ValidateDataSignature with hash, size, and verification buffer\n16. Call WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout(7) for finalization\n17. Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates entirely on global state and static resources\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 0 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Platform signature uses conditional negation with NEG/SBB instructions for sign extension\n- Polling loop has 10ms sleep interval waiting for async resource loading\n- Critical section protects global flag initialization from concurrent access\n- 64-byte buffer cleared with REP.STOSD (16 dwords) + STOSW (2 bytes) + STOSB (1 byte)\n- Version string loaded asynchronously from external source (file or network)\n- Cancellation can occur during wait loop via g_dwCancellationFlag",
