      "name": "PrepareNewsBuffer",
      "signature": "bool PrepareNewsBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Prepares a serialized buffer of news/bulletin entries for transmission to game clients.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates that the number of pending news items does not exceed 256 (0x100)\n2. If validation fails, triggers assertion failure at line 315 (0x13b) and exits with code -1\n3. First pass: Iterates through all pending news items to calculate required buffer size\n   - Loads each item's string content from global news table (stride 0x408 bytes)\n   - Scans each string to find null terminator and validate length (max 1023 bytes / 0x3ff)\n   - Accumulates buffer space: 4 bytes per name field + string length + 1 null + 4 padding\n4. Allocates a fixed 340-byte (0x154) buffer via AllocateBuffer\n   - Returns false immediately if allocation fails\n5. Initializes buffer header:\n   - Offset +0: 4-byte version/seed identifier from g_dwNewsRandomSeed\n   - Offset +4: 4-byte count of news items to serialize\n   - Offset +8: Start of serialized item data\n6. Second pass: Copies item data into allocated buffer\n   - For each item: copies 4-byte name field, then string data with padding\n   - Uses complex pointer arithmetic to calculate offsets and copy positions\n   - Each item string is null-terminated with 4 additional padding bytes\n7. Gets current system time via GetSystemTime API\n8. Converts system time to Windows FILETIME format via SystemTimeToFileTime\n9. Calls ValidateAndUpdateCacheFile to transmit prepared buffer with timestamp\n10. Frees any temporary allocation and returns transmission result\n\nParameters: None (uses global data directly)\n- g_dwNewsValidationCounter: Index of first item to serialize\n- g_dwNewsItemCount: Total item count or end index\n- g_pNewsTable: Base pointer to news item array (stride 0x408 per item)\n- g_dwNewsRandomSeed: Version identifier for buffer header\n- g_pNewsResourcePointer: Context pointer passed to ValidateAndUpdateCacheFile\n\nReturns: bool\n- true if buffer prepared and transmission successful (from ValidateAndUpdateCacheFile)\n- false if string length exceeds 1023 bytes or buffer allocation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Item count overflow: If count > 256, triggers assertion and calls _exit(-1)\n- String length validation: Any item string > 1023 bytes causes early return false\n- Empty news queue: If no items pending, still allocates buffer and calls transmission function\n- Fixed buffer size: Always allocates 0x154 (340) bytes regardless of actual data size\n- Magic constants: 0x408 = per-item structure size, 0x3ff = max string length, 0x100 = max count\n\nStructure Layout:\nBuffer format (0x154 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field                 Type      Description\n0x0     4     dwVersionSeed         DWORD     Version/seed identifier\n0x4     4     dwItemCount           DWORD     Number of serialized items\n0x8     var   arrSerializedItems    array     Array of serialized item entries\n                                              Each entry: 4-byte name field + string + padding",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
