      "name": "LoadNewsTableFromCache",
      "signature": "uint LoadNewsTableFromCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Loads news articles from serialized cache file and populates global news table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Deserialize news data from global g_pNewsResourcePointer resource\n2. Extract article count and validate it is within limits (0 to 0x100/256)\n3. Compare current capacity (g_dwNewsTableCapacity) with required count\n4. Expand news table capacity if current < required, calling ExpandNewsTableCapacity\n5. Initialize news table globals: clear item count, validation counter, and temporary flags\n6. Loop through each article in serialized data:\n   a. Check if table has capacity for new item (g_dwNewsItemCount < g_dwNewsTableCapacity)\n   b. If capacity insufficient, call IsPowerOfTwo and ExpandNewsTableCapacity\n   c. Calculate storage offset using stride 0x408 bytes per article\n   d. Store article ID at offset 0 in article structure (initially 0)\n   e. Store pointer to article text data at offset 0x4\n   f. Scan string for null terminator to calculate string length\n   g. Validate string length < 0x400 bytes (1024 character limit)\n   h. Copy null-terminated string into article buffer at offset 0x8\n   i. Load article ID from pointer for validation check\n   j. Verify article ID matches previous ID (sequential validation)\n   k. Advance to next article in serialized buffer\n7. Verify all articles loaded successfully (itemsLoaded == articleCount)\n8. Clean up on error: call DeleteObjectTrampoline to free table/buffers\n9. Free temporary input buffer via DeleteObjectTrampoline\n10. Return success flag (1) or failure code (0)\n\nParameters:\nNone. Operates on global news table and serialized cache resource data.\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if all articles loaded successfully, 0 if validation failed or deserialization error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0x100 = max article count, 0x400 = max string length, 0x408 = article struct stride\n- If capacity expansion fails, entire table is cleared and freed\n- String validation checks for length < 0x3ff bytes (1024 char limit)\n- Article ID sequential validation ensures data integrity during parsing\n- Clears all globals on parse failure: capacity, count, pointer, counters, seed set to 0\n- Calls ExpandNewsTableCapacity multiple times if needed during load loop\n- Power-of-two capacity calculations for efficient memory allocation\n\nStructure Layout:\nNewsArticle structure at g_pNewsTable, stride 0x408 bytes:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name      Type      Description\n  0x0     0x4   articleId       uint      Article identifier/validation field\n  0x4     0x4   textDataPtr     void*     Pointer to article text (unused in this impl)\n  0x8     0x400 textContent     char[1024] Null-terminated article text buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
