      "name": "ExpandKeySchedule",
      "signature": "void ExpandKeySchedule(ushort * pKeyBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Expands a 16-byte cipher key into a 104-byte key schedule using 44 rounds of bit rotation and combination.\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy source key buffer (8 words) to destination buffer\n2. Initialize loop counter: roundCount = 44 (0x2c), wordIndex = 0\n3. For each round: Calculate nextWordIndex = (wordIndex + 1) & 7, load and rotate words, combine with bitwise OR, advance buffer pointer every 8 iterations, decrement roundCount until zero\n4. Return with expanded key schedule in destination buffer\nParameters:\npSourceKey: Pointer to 16-byte source key buffer (8 uint16 words) in ECX\npDestKeySchedule: Pointer to destination buffer in EAX (implicit __fastcall parameter)\nReturns:\nvoid - Result written to pDestKeySchedule buffer (52 words total: 8 original + 44 expanded)\nSpecial Cases:\n44 total expansion rounds (0x2c), circular word index wrapping [0-7], buffer pointer advanced 16 bytes every 8 iterations, total 104 bytes output",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:015e27c7d17f6b96e8539dcc4559e114",
