      "name": "ComputeModularInverse",
      "signature": "uint ComputeModularInverse(uint divisor)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Computes modular multiplicative inverse using Extended Euclidean Algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if divisor < 2; if so, return divisor unchanged (base case)\n2. Compute quotient and remainder of 0x10001 / divisor\n3. If remainder equals 1, return the first B\u00e9zout coefficient (1 - quotient) & 0xFFFF\n4. Initialize coeffB = 1 and enter extended GCD loop\n5. Loop iteration: divide current divisor by remainder to get next quotient\n6. Multiply quotient by coeffA and add to coeffB\n7. If remainder becomes 1, return coeffB as result\n8. Divide current remainder by new remainder to get next quotient\n9. Multiply quotient by coeffB and add to coeffA\n10. If remainder becomes 1, return (1 - coeffA) & 0xFFFF; otherwise loop\n\nParameters:\n  divisor (EAX): The value to compute the inverse of. Must be in range [0, 0xFFFF] and coprime with 0x10001 (65537 in decimal).\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: The modular multiplicative inverse of divisor modulo 0x10001, as a 16-bit value masked to 0xFFFF.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - divisor < 2: Returns divisor unchanged (base case optimization)\n  - remainder == 1 early: Direct calculation via (1 - quotient) & 0xFFFF avoids loop\n  - Result masked to 0xFFFF: Ensures 16-bit output even if intermediate calculations overflow\n  - Magic constant 0x10001 (65537): The modulus, used in ECC and RSA implementations\n\nStructure Layout:\nAlgorithm uses no structured data, operates entirely on scalar values via registers and stack.\nRegister mapping: ESI=divisor, EDI=initial quotient, ECX=current remainder, EBX=coeffB, EDX=quotient results.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
