      "name": "TransformMatrixBlock",
      "signature": "void TransformMatrixBlock(ushort * pMatrixData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Transforms an 8x6 matrix block of 16-bit coefficients through modular inversion and negation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract initial 6 matrix elements (indices 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) from input array\n2. Compute modular inverses of negated B and A coefficients via ComputeModularInverse(EDI)\n3. Store initial inverse coefficients in stack buffer: invCoeffNegB, negBCoeff, negACoeff, invCoeffA\n4. Loop 8 times (blockCounter = 0x7) to process matrix blocks:\n   - Load 6 elements from current input block at ESI\n   - Call ComputeModularInverse 4 times on EDI context with various negations\n   - Store transformed coefficients backward in stack buffer (12 bytes per iteration)\n   - Advance input pointer ESI by 12 bytes (6 uint16 elements)\n5. Process final 6-element block with same transformation (indices 48-53)\n6. Copy 52 transformed uint16 elements (0x34 items) from stack buffer to output at EDX\n7. Clear source buffer during copy operation\n\nParameters:\n  pMatrixData: unsigned short * - Pointer to output matrix buffer (written via stack parameter)\n  (Implicit) EDI: uint - Modular inverse context/seed passed from caller\n\nReturns:\n  void - Transformed matrix written to caller's output buffer, accessed via stack at ESP+0x84\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - EDI register contains modular inverse context (caller-provided, not a normal parameter)\n  - Stack buffer transformBuffer[48] accumulates 96 bytes of transformed data\n  - Final copy processes exactly 52 elements (0x34 in decimal) despite buffer having 48 slots\n  - Backward stack buffer storage pattern requires careful offset calculation during copy\n\nStructure Layout - Stack Buffer (96 bytes, ESP-0x68 to ESP-0x08):\n  Offset    Size    Field Name              Type        Description\n  ESP-0x68  2       [0]  invCoeffNegB       uint16_t    Initial inverse of negated B\n  ESP-0x66  2       [1]  negBCoeff          uint16_t    Negated B coefficient\n  ESP-0x64  2       [2]  negACoeff          uint16_t    Negated A coefficient\n  ESP-0x62  2       [3]  invCoeffA          uint16_t    Initial inverse of A\n  ESP-0x60  48      [4-51] loop_elements    uint16_t[24] Transformed elements from 8 blocks\n  (12 bytes per iteration: element, inverse, neg_a, neg_b, inverse, pad)",
