      "name": "LogMessageToSystem",
      "signature": "int LogMessageToSystem(int nUnused, char * szInputMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Logs a message string to the game's log system by calculating string length and dispatching to logging handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ESI pointer to position one past string start for length calculation\n2. Load current character from message string and increment pointer\n3. Continue looping through string until null terminator is encountered\n4. Calculate total message length by subtracting pointers (final - start - 1)\n5. Load global context pointer from g_dwRNGInitEnabled (0x6ff3f654)\n6. Call dispatch handler with calculated message length as parameter\n7. Load global context pointer again\n8. Call dispatch handler with constant value 1 and Battle.net connection message address\n9. Set return value to 1 indicating success\n10. Return from function\n\nParameters:\n- nUnused (int, ECX): First parameter in __fastcall convention but not used by function\n- szInputMessage (char *, EDX): Pointer to null-terminated message string to output to log\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 to indicate successful message output",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
