      "name": "StoreSocketHandleAndDelay",
      "signature": "void StoreSocketHandleAndDelay(SOCKET socketHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores a socket handle to global storage and introduces a brief delay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push 10 (sleep duration in milliseconds) onto stack\n2. Store socket handle parameter (in EAX register) to global variable g_hNetworkSocket at offset 0x6ff3f1f8\n3. Call Sleep(10) function to allow network stack to process socket creation\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  socketHandle (SOCKET) - Implicit in EAX register: Socket handle to store globally\n  \nReturns:\n  void - No return value, but updates global g_hNetworkSocket with the socket handle\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The 10ms delay allows the underlying network stack to process the socket creation\n  - Global g_hNetworkSocket is subsequently accessed by multiple network functions\n  - This function is called immediately after socket creation to ensure proper initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
