      "name": "ProcessPacketData",
      "signature": "void ProcessPacketData(int nBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes variable-length packet data with record dispatch callbacks\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Scan buffer from start, locating first non-0xFF marker byte\n2. Calculate offset from buffer start to marker position\n3. For each record in buffer:\n   a. Read word-sized length field at offset +2 from record start\n   b. Validate record fits in buffer (minimum 4 bytes, length <= available space)\n   c. If validation fails: copy remaining data to buffer start via DWORD moves, exit\n   d. Extract record type byte at offset +1 from record start\n   e. If type < 0x5E: fetch handler function pointer from g_pPacketHandlerTable[type*4]\n   f. If handler pointer non-NULL: call handler callback with record data\n   g. Mark record type as dispatched in g_byPacketDispatchFlags[type]\n   h. Advance to next record by adding recordSize to current position\n4. Loop back to step 1 until 0xFF sentinel or validation failure\n\nParameters:\n- pBuffer (EAX): Pointer to packet buffer containing variable-length records\n- bufferSize (Stack+0x14): Total size in bytes of data to process\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies buffer in-place by copying remaining unprocessed data to buffer start\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0xFF byte: End-of-packet sentinel marker (not processed as record)\n- Record type 0x5E-0xFF: Not dispatched via callback; only processed during remainder copy\n- Minimum record size: 4 bytes (1 marker + 1 type + 2 size field)\n- Copy operation: Uses REP MOVSD for aligned DWORDs, then REP MOVSB for final bytes\n- Handler dispatch: NULL function pointers are skipped (JZ to skip_handler_call)\n- Dispatch tracking: Records handler invocation in byte array indexed by record type\n\nStructure Layout (Packet Record Format):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0x00    1     marker            byte    0xFF = end-of-packet, other = record start marker\n0x01    1     recordType        byte    Packet record type (0-0xFF); 0x5E-0xFF skipped\n0x02    2     recordSize        word    Length in bytes of entire record (including marker/type/size)\n0x04    N     recordData        byte[]  Record payload; size determined by recordSize field",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a99e2d6eee2857b72fb45bd928e7ab0d",
