      "name": "GetAuthProviderByMode",
      "signature": "uint GetAuthProviderByMode(uint * pOutProviderType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Selects and returns cryptographic authentication provider based on Battle.net download mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store the current cryptographic provider type (g_dwCryptographicProviderType) into output pointer\n2. Load global download mode value (g_dwDownloadMode) into EAX\n3. Compare download mode against 0 (default mode)\n4. If mode equals 0, return password verification state (g_dwPasswordVerificationState)\n5. If mode does not equal 0, decrement EAX to test if mode equals 1\n6. If mode equals 1, return key generation state (g_dwKeyGenerationState)\n7. If mode is neither 0 nor 1, return 0 (invalid/unsupported mode)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutProviderType - Pointer to uint where current cryptographic provider type (from g_dwCryptographicProviderType) will be stored. Always written regardless of download mode.\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Authentication provider state based on download mode:\n         Mode 0 (default): Returns g_dwPasswordVerificationState\n         Mode 1 (alternate): Returns g_dwKeyGenerationState\n         Other modes: Returns 0 (error/invalid mode indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Provider type is always stored to output pointer before mode check\n  - Download mode values outside 0-1 range are treated as errors, returning 0\n  - Used by Battle.net download authentication subsystem\n  - Function uses __fastcall convention with mode value in ECX",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
