      "name": "ProcessIncomingNetworkDataLoop",
      "signature": "DWORD ProcessIncomingNetworkDataLoop(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes incoming network data in a continuous loop with mutual exclusion and timeout handling.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate 16KB stack buffer and initialize process status to success (return value 1)\\n2. Check if background thread already running via g_dwBackgroundThreadRunning counter\\n3. If already running, set status to 1 (success) and return immediately\\n4. Otherwise, increment g_dwBackgroundThreadRunning using interlocked operation\\n5. Wait for initialization signals (g_dwRNGStateOverride or g_dwConnectionInitializationFlag)\\n   - Sleep 10ms intervals until either signal becomes non-zero\\n6. Record initial tick count via GetTickCount() for timeout calculation\\n7. Begin main processing loop while g_dwRNGInitEnabled data source pointer is valid:\\n   a. Check abort conditions: g_dwRNGStateOverride, data source termination (offset +0x2c)\\n   b. Call ValidateProcessingReadiness() to check if processing should proceed\\n   c. If validation succeeds:\\n      - Read up to (0x2000 - current_offset) bytes from data source\\n      - If read returns 0 or negative, set g_dwCancellationFlag=1 and exit loop\\n      - Process packet data, update buffer offset\\n   d. Get current tick count and calculate elapsed time\\n   e. Check if elapsed time exceeds 180000ms (3 minutes):\\n      - On timeout: set g_dwCancellationFlag=1\\n      - Generate random data via SMemRandom()\\n      - Dispatch function ordinal 10007 for timeout handling\\n      - Reset base tick count\\n   f. Check data source still valid, continue loop if so\\n8. Decrement g_dwBackgroundThreadRunning using interlocked operation\\n9. Return status code: 1 indicates success, 0 indicates read failure\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nDWORD - Status code: 1 for successful completion, 0 for read/abort failure\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Thread-safe mutual exclusion using interlocked increment/decrement counter\\n- Timeout value hardcoded to 0x2bf20 ms (180 seconds)\\n- Buffer capacity 0x2000 bytes (8192 bytes)\\n- Sleep interval during initialization: 10 milliseconds\\n- Global abort flags checked every iteration\\n- Data source structure field offset +0x2c indicates termination status",
