      "name": "TokenizeAndHashDelimitedString",
      "signature": "void TokenizeAndHashDelimitedString(char * szInputString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Tokenizes input string and adds each token to hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tokenization by calling strtok() with input string and carriage return delimiter\n2. Loop through all tokens returned by strtok()\n3. For each token, check if it starts with newline character (0x0A)\n4. If newline found, increment pointer to skip the character\n5. Add the token to hash table with hash ID 1 via CreateAndAddHashEntry()\n6. Continue tokenization with NULL input to get next token\n7. Exit loop when strtok() returns NULL (no more tokens)\n\nParameters:\n  szInputString (char*) - IMPLICIT EAX - Input string containing tokens separated by carriage returns\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Input string passed via EAX register (non-standard __cdecl variant)\n  - Delimiter is carriage return (0x0D) stored at g_szTokenDelimiter\n  - Leading newline (0x0A) characters in tokens are skipped before hashing\n  - Hash table ID is always 1 for all entries\n  - Uses strtok() which modifies the input string; passing NULL continues from last position",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b1a4c7312ea6c4bca616bc4d5a615c41",
