      "name": "InitiateGameShutdown",
      "signature": "int InitiateGameShutdown(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initiates graceful game shutdown by coordinating cleanup across multiple background threads.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Invoke first handler (cryptographic cleanup) if g_dwCryptographicInitStatus is set; clear flag\n2. Invoke second handler (buffer cleanup) if g_pBNSendBufferPtr is set; clear flag\n3. Call game state finalizer (FUN_6ff332d0) to perform final state housekeeping\n4. Call general cleanup routine (FUN_6ff2fd20) to deallocate temporary resources\n5. Destroy game objects at offsets +0x8 and +0x4 in g_dwCryptoContextState array if valid\n6. Clear g_dwCryptoContextState reference and signal first background thread (set g_dwRNGStateOverride=1)\n7. Poll g_dwBackgroundThreadRunning in 10ms intervals until it clears (first thread completion)\n8. Check if server is active (g_dwRNGInitEnabled != 0); if so, signal cleanup via g_dwCancellationFlag=1\n9. Poll g_dwServerCleanupComplete in 10ms intervals until it clears (server thread completion)\n10. Call CloseServerConnection() if server handle exists; clear g_dwRNGInitEnabled flag\n11. Signal third background thread via g_dwThirdThreadCleanupSignal=1\n12. Poll g_dwFileDownloadThreadRunning in 10ms intervals until it reaches 0 (file download completion)\n13. Verify g_dwServerCleanupComplete has cleared; if not, accumulate 10ms sleep intervals with 0x3c (60ms) timeout\n14. Return 1 if all cleanup threads complete within timeout, 0 if timeout exceeded\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 if shutdown completed successfully within timeout limits; 0 if final cleanup exceeded 60ms timeout\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timeout mechanism uses 10ms sleep granularity, accumulating timeout counter by 0x64 (100) per iteration to track elapsed time\n- Multiple background threads signaled via separate global flags (RNG state, cancellation, download signal)\n- Server connection cleanup conditional on g_dwRNGInitEnabled being non-zero\n- Game object array destruction skipped if g_dwCryptoContextState is null\n- First and second handlers use fixed parameter values (0x224 and 0x39a respectively) passed to shared handler routine",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
