      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net authentication credentials through MD5 hashing and cryptographic randomization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 268 bytes (0x10c) on stack for MD5 hash buffer and working storage\n2. Store magic value 0x80000004 at ESP+0x10 (initialization/context flag)\n3. Call MD5HashData to compute MD5 hash of bnserver-D2DV.ini configuration filename\n4. Use returned hash length (EAX) to calculate target offset: hash_length + 9\n5. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData to generate 51 bytes (0x33) of random data at computed offset\n6. Clean up stack frame and return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone. Function takes no parameters; uses global string constant g_szBNetServerConfigFilename.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. No return value; initializes credentials in-place via stack buffers.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- MD5 hash result in EAX used directly as byte offset calculation (EAX + 9)\n- Magic value 0x80000004 stored at offset ESP+0x10 (context/flag identifier)\n- Random data size hardcoded to 51 bytes (0x33)\n- Preserves and restores EDI register (used as parameter to cryptographic function)\n- Called by ConnectToBattleNetServer during Battle.net connection initialization",
