      "name": "InitializeAndShuffleServerList",
      "signature": "int InitializeAndShuffleServerList(hostent * pServerInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes server list from hostent and shuffles addresses for load balancing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Detect IP vs hostname: Check if h_aliases[0] is numeric using _isdigit\n2. Parse IP address: If numeric, convert with inet_addr; otherwise use gethostbyname DNS lookup\n3. Handle parse errors: Return 0 if invalid IP or DNS lookup fails, with error logging\n4. Create temporary hostent: For numeric IPs, build temporary hostent structure at g_TempHostentForNumericIP\n5. Count server addresses: Iterate h_addr_list until NULL pointer to get address count\n6. Seed random: Call GetTickCount for system tick and SeedThreadRandomNumber for RNG\n7. Fisher-Yates shuffle: Loop from count-1 down to 0, swap addresses at random indices\n8. Validate shuffle: Assert that computed swap index >= current index (security check)\n9. Generate hash: Concatenate inet_ntoa results of each shuffled address with MD5 separators\n10. Return success: Return 1 on completion, 0 on any failure\n\nParameters:\npServerInfo (hostent*): DNS hostent structure with h_name (hostname), h_aliases (address string array), h_addr_list (server addresses)\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 on success (shuffle complete), 0 on parse/DNS failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNumeric IP detection: First character of h_aliases checked with _isdigit\nInvalid IP: inet_addr returns 0xffffffff for invalid address string\nTemporary hostent: Used only for numeric IP case, allocated at static address 0x6ff3f91c\nShuffle algorithm: Uses modulo arithmetic with (value * count) >> 15 + current_index pattern\nHash buffer: Concatenates with 0x7fffffff max length limit per segment\nAssertion trigger: Line 0x1ad fires if shuffle index becomes invalid (randomIndex < shuffleIndex)",
