      "name": "DispatchAuthenticationByMode",
      "signature": "int DispatchAuthenticationByMode(char * szPassword, void * pHashSource, char * szSaltOrHash)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatches authentication operations based on global download mode setting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_dwDownloadMode from global address 0x6ff3f878\n2. If mode == 0 (password verification):\n   - Clear g_PasswordVerificationState at 0x6ff3ee1c\n   - Clear g_PasswordHashBuffer at 0x6ff3ef9c\n   - Call VerifyPasswordHash with password and salt parameters\n   - Return 1 (success)\n3. If mode == 1 (encryption key generation):\n   - Clear g_KeyGenerationState at 0x6ff3eeb0\n   - Clear g_EncryptionKeyBuffer at 0x6ff3f030\n   - Call GenerateEncryptionKeyWithHashing with hash source and salt parameters\n   - Return encryption result (0 or 1)\n4. For any other mode value:\n   - Return 0 (invalid mode)\n\nParameters:\npPassword (ECX): char* - Password string for verification (mode 0) or hash input (mode 1)\npHashSource (EDX): void* - Hash source data for encryption key generation (mode 1 only)\npSaltOrHash (stack): char* - Salt buffer (mode 0) or secondary hash source (mode 1)\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 for successful password verification (mode 0), encryption result for mode 1, 0 for invalid mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 0: Clears two state buffers before password verification\n- Mode 1: Clears two different state buffers before key generation\n- Invalid modes (not 0 or 1): Returns 0 without calling other functions\n- Global g_dwDownloadMode at 0x6ff3f878 determines execution path\n- Function uses __fastcall convention with callee cleanup (RET 0x4)",
