      "name": "ConnectToBattleNetServer",
      "signature": "int ConnectToBattleNetServer(char * szServerListString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Establishes connection to Battle.net servers with account handshake and version validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 0x2108-byte stack buffer and clear global state flags\n2. Return success if serverList is null (fallback behavior)\n3. Parse comma-delimited server addresses from input string using strtok()\n4. For each address, create connection thread with ProcessIncomingDataLoop callback\n5. Use socket select() with 1-second timeout to monitor write-readiness for all connections\n6. When a socket becomes writable, set it as primary connection in g_dwRNGInitEnabled\n7. Close all non-primary connections via CloseServerConnection()\n8. If no servers available, log error and return 0\n9. Enter critical section to verify no cancellation flags set\n10. Call GetPeerSocketAddressThunk() to retrieve connected server IP address\n11. Set status to 3 (account access phase) and call DispatchOrdinal10017, DispatchIndirectOrdinal10007\n12. Call WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout(0x50) for account validation response\n13. If account validation succeeds, set status to 4 (version check phase)\n14. Clear patch state and call func_0x1021a640() to request version validation\n15. Call WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout(0x51) for version response\n16. Call InitializeAuthenticationCredentials() on success and return 1\n17. Return 0 on any failure (connection timeout, cancellation, auth failure)\n\nParameters:\npServerListString - Comma-delimited null-terminated string of Battle.net server addresses (e.g. \"useast.battle.net,uswest.battle.net\")\n\nReturns:\n1 - Successfully connected to Battle.net, authenticated, and version-validated\n0 - Connection failed, no servers available, authentication failed, or version check failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pServerListString is null, returns 1 immediately (no connection attempt)\n- Maximum 32 concurrent server connections (0x20)\n- 5-second timeout (0x1388ms) between parsing operations\n- 60-second total connection window (0x3c retry counter)\n- Uses g_BattleNetCriticalSection for thread-safe global state access\n- Implicit register parameter in ECX (moved to ESI) for serverList string",
