      "comment": "Copies a 20-byte cipher block from the cipher data table to the destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if destination buffer pointer (ECX) is null using TEST ECX,ECX instruction\n2. If null flag is set, jump to function exit without copying data\n3. Calculate source array offset: nCipherBlockIndex * 0x5c (92 bytes per block)\n4. Load first dword from cipher data table at (base + offset), store to destination[0]\n5. Load second dword from cipher data table at (base + offset + 4), store to destination[1]\n6. Load third dword from cipher data table at (base + offset + 8), store to destination[2]\n7. Load fourth dword from cipher data table at (base + offset + 12), store to destination[3]\n8. Load fifth dword from cipher data table at (base + offset + 16), store to destination[4]\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nECX (pDestBuffer): Pointer to 20-byte destination buffer where cipher block will be copied\nIMPLICIT EAX (nCipherBlockIndex): Block index for array offset calculation (__fastcall: first param in EAX)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, result stored in destination buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL buffer protection: If pDestBuffer is NULL, function returns immediately without copying\n- Array stride: 0x5c (92 bytes per element) allows for multi-block array indexing\n- Data source: Five consecutive global DWORD constants at 0x6ff3e7c0 through 0x6ff3e7d0\n- Total bytes copied: 20 bytes (5 dwords \u00d7 4 bytes each) per function call",
