      "name": "SHA1ProcessBlock",
      "signature": "void SHA1ProcessBlock(uint * pHashState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes one 512-bit block of message data in SHA-1 cryptographic hash computation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Expand 16 input words into 80-word message schedule using XOR-based circular dependency\n2. Round 1 (0-19): Apply F function (IF) with constant 0x5a827999, 5 operations per iteration\n3. Round 2 (20-39): Apply G function (XOR) with constant 0x6ed9eba1, 5 operations per iteration\n4. Round 3 (40-59): Apply H function (majority) with constant 0x8f1bbcdc, 5 operations per iteration\n5. Round 4 (60-79): Apply I function (XOR) with constant 0xca62c1d6, 5 operations per iteration\n6. Update hash state (5 x 32-bit values) by adding computed round results\n\nParameters:\n- pHashState: Pointer to 5 x 32-bit hash state words (H0-H4) that get modified in place\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Modifies hash state array directly\n\nStructure Layout (pHashState):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type      Description\n0x00    0x04  H0          uint      Hash state word A (updated in place)\n0x04    0x04  H1          uint      Hash state word B (updated in place)\n0x08    0x04  H2          uint      Hash state word C (updated in place)\n0x0c    0x04  H3          uint      Hash state word D (updated in place)\n0x10    0x04  H4          uint      Hash state word E (updated in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message schedule expansion: W[i] = W[i-16] XOR W[i-14] XOR W[i-8] XOR W[i-3]\n- Left rotation via combined shift: (val << 5) | (val >> 27) for 5-bit rotation\n- Round functions applied in 5 operations per iteration for efficiency\n- Magic constants specific to each SHA-1 round function phase\n- All operations use unsigned 32-bit arithmetic with implicit wraparound on overflow",
