      "name": "InitializeSHA1Context",
      "signature": "void InitializeSHA1Context(int contextIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a SHA-1 cryptographic hash context with standard initial values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate context offset by multiplying contextIndex by 0x5c (92 bytes)\n2. Add base address 0x6ff3e7c0 to get target SHA1_CTX pointer\n3. Initialize h0 register to SHA-1 constant 0x67452301\n4. Initialize h1 register to SHA-1 constant 0xefcdab89\n5. Initialize h2 register to SHA-1 constant 0x98badcfe\n6. Initialize h3 register to SHA-1 constant 0x10325476\n7. Initialize h4 register to SHA-1 constant 0xc3d2e1f0\n8. Zero out bytesProcessedLow counter (offset +0x14)\n9. Zero out bytesProcessedHigh counter (offset +0x18)\n\nParameters:\n  contextIndex (int) - Index into SHA1_CTX array at 0x6ff3e7c0\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - SHA-1 initial values are FIPS 180-1 standard hash constants\n  - Structure size 0x5c (92 bytes) includes h0-h4 (20 bytes), counters (8 bytes), buffer (64 bytes)\n  - Array base at 0x6ff3e7c0 holds multiple SHA1_CTX structures\n\nStructure Layout (SHA1_CTX - 92 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type   Description\n  +0x00   4     h0                   uint   First hash register (0x67452301)\n  +0x04   4     h1                   uint   Second hash register (0xefcdab89)\n  +0x08   4     h2                   uint   Third hash register (0x98badcfe)\n  +0x0c   4     h3                   uint   Fourth hash register (0x10325476)\n  +0x10   4     h4                   uint   Fifth hash register (0xc3d2e1f0)\n  +0x14   4     bytesProcessedLow    uint   Low 32 bits of byte counter\n  +0x18   4     bytesProcessedHigh   uint   High 32 bits of byte counter\n  +0x1c   64    buffer               byte[] Input buffer for block processing",
