      "name": "ProcessSHA1DataBlock",
      "signature": "void ProcessSHA1DataBlock(int nScheduleIndex, uint * pDataBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes a 512-bit input data block through SHA-1 cryptographic hash algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate base address of schedule structure using nScheduleIndex multiplied by 0x5c bytes per entry\n2. Load current 32-bit block counter from schedule structure offset +0x14\n3. Add 0x200 (512 bytes) to counter to track processed blocks\n4. Check for overflow condition: if new counter < old counter, increment overflow counter at offset +0x18\n5. Store updated counter value back to schedule offset +0x14\n6. Copy 16 dwords (64 bytes) from pDataBlock into schedule message buffer at offset +0x1c using REP MOVSD\n7. Call SHA1ProcessBlock to process the message buffer and update hash state (H0-H4)\n8. Test if output pointer pOutputBuffer (EBX) is non-NULL\n9. If output pointer valid: copy 5 hash state words to output buffer at offsets 0x00, 0x04, 0x08, 0x0c, 0x10\n10. Restore registers and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- nScheduleIndex (int): Zero-based index selecting one of multiple SHA-1 schedule structures; multiplied by 0x5c to calculate offset from base 0x6ff3e7c0\n- pDataBlock (uint*): Pointer to 16-dword (64-byte) input buffer; contents are copied to internal message buffer for SHA-1 processing\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Modifies schedule structure in-place; optionally writes 5 hash state words (H0-H4) to pOutputBuffer if pointer is non-NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x200 (512 bytes): Standard SHA-1 block size for tracking processed data\n- Overflow handling: 32-bit counter wraps at 2^32; overflow counter tracks wrap events\n- Output routing: If pOutputBuffer is NULL (EBX == 0), hash output is not copied (internal processing mode)\n- Schedule base address: 0x6ff3e7c0 + (nScheduleIndex * 0x5c); each entry contains 5 hash words (H0-H4), counter, overflow counter, and 16-dword message buffer\n- Hash state words H0-H4 located at offsets +0x00, +0x04, +0x08, +0x0c, +0x10 within schedule structure\n- Note: pOutputBuffer is implicitly passed via EBX register (not a formal parameter), used for optional hash state output\n\nStructure Layout (SHA-1 Schedule Entry - 0x5c bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type      Description\n0x00    0x04  H0              uint      Hash state word A (160-bit hash word 0)\n0x04    0x04  H1              uint      Hash state word B (160-bit hash word 1)\n0x08    0x04  H2              uint      Hash state word C (160-bit hash word 2)\n0x0c    0x04  H3              uint      Hash state word D (160-bit hash word 3)\n0x10    0x04  H4              uint      Hash state word E (160-bit hash word 4)\n0x14    0x04  blockCounter    uint      512-byte block counter (incremented by 0x200 each call)\n0x18    0x04  overflowCount   uint      Overflow counter for 32-bit wrap detection\n0x1c    0x40  messageData     uint[16]  64-byte message buffer copied from pDataBlock input",
