      "name": "SelectConfigurationBuffer",
      "signature": "void * SelectConfigurationBuffer(int nSelector)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Selects one of two global configuration buffers based on input selector value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test selector parameter in EAX register (zero flag if zero)\n2. Load primary buffer pointer from g_pThirdConfigFileBuffer (0x6ff3e8e0)\n3. If selector is non-zero, return primary buffer\n4. If selector is zero, load and return alternate buffer from g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate (0x6ff3e8d8)\n\nParameters:\nnSelector (via EAX register): Selection flag\n  - Non-zero: Select primary buffer (g_pThirdConfigFileBuffer)\n  - Zero: Select alternate buffer (g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate)\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Pointer to selected configuration buffer\n  - Primary buffer (0x185801B0) when selector is non-zero\n  - Alternate buffer (0x00000000) when selector is zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses implicit register parameter (EAX) instead of stack parameter\n- Both buffers are global pointers initialized during game startup\n- Primary buffer contains valid heap pointer; alternate is typically NULL\n- Called by ValidateAndProcessEncodedStrings, LoadAndValidateGameConfigFiles, VerifyGameFilesAndInitializeCrypto",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a32bd78f2fa900054fc0983aa47d393b",
