      "name": "CalculateBoundedStringLength",
      "signature": "uint CalculateBoundedStringLength(char * szString, uint dwMaxLength1, uint dwMaxLength2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates the length of a null-terminated string with dual maximum length bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register for use as string pointer\n2. Compare two maximum length bounds (ECX vs EDX); use the smaller value as effective max\n3. Return 0 immediately if effective maximum length is 0\n4. Loop through string characters starting at string address:\n   a. Load current character from string buffer\n   b. Decrement remaining character counter\n   c. Increment total character count\n   d. Advance string pointer to next byte\n   e. Test character for null terminator; exit if found\n   f. Test remaining length counter; continue if more chars allowed\n5. Return character count if null terminator found, or 0 if max length exceeded\n\nParameters:\n- szString (EAX/ECX via fastcall): Pointer to null-terminated string to measure\n- dwMaxLength1 (ECX): First maximum length bound\n- dwMaxLength2 (EDX): Second maximum length bound\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Length of string (0 to min(dwMaxLength1, dwMaxLength2)), or 0 if no null terminator found within bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If either maximum bound is 0, returns 0 immediately without scanning string\n- If string exceeds both maximum bounds without null terminator, returns 0 (incomplete string)\n- String must be null-terminated; behavior undefined for non-terminated buffers",
