      "name": "ClearCipherBuffers",
      "signature": "void ClearCipherBuffers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clear cipher-related data buffers used in cryptographic operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize EAX to 0 for STOSD write operation\n2. Load count of 0x4e (78) DWORDs into ECX\n3. Load address of g_dwCipherKeyScheduleStart (0x6ff3ea18) into EDI\n4. Execute REP STOSD to zero first cipher buffer (312 bytes)\n5. Load count of 0x45 (69) DWORDs into ECX\n6. Load address of g_dwCipherBlockValues0 (0x6ff3e7c0) into EDI\n7. Execute REP STOSD to zero second cipher buffer (276 bytes)\n8. Restore EDI register and return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_dwCipherKeyScheduleStart (0x6ff3ea18): 312-byte buffer used in cipher key scheduling and block processing\n  - g_dwCipherBlockValues0 (0x6ff3e7c0): 276-byte buffer used in cipher operations and SHA1 processing\n  - Uses REP STOSD: repeats STOSD ECX times, writing EAX (0) to [EDI], EDI increments by 4 each iteration",
