      "name": "ReadAndValidateEncryptedFile",
      "signature": "void * ReadAndValidateEncryptedFile(void * pFileBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Reads and validates encrypted file data with automatic cleanup on failure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize buffer size field to 0x400 bytes (1KB default allocation size)\n2. Call ReadFileData to read file content into buffer with size constraint\n3. Check if buffer was successfully allocated (pointer must be non-null)\n4. Verify actual bytes were read from file (bytesRead > 0)\n5. Call ValidateEncryptedData to validate format and data integrity\n6. If validation succeeds (result == 0), return buffer pointer to caller\n7. If validation fails (result != 0), free allocated buffer automatically\n8. Return NULL pointer on any failure (allocation, read, or validation)\n\nParameters:\n  pFileBuffer (ECX, fastcall): Pointer to buffer structure or allocation target;\n    field at offset 0 receives size; field receives buffer pointer\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Pointer to validated encrypted data buffer if successful (non-zero)\n       NULL if allocation failed, no data read, or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic 0x400: Default allocation size of 1024 bytes\n  Validation codes: 0 = success, non-zero = failure with auto-cleanup\n  Memory ownership: Caller must free returned buffer when done\n  Error handling: Automatic memory cleanup prevents leaks on validation failure\n\nStructure Layout (caller-provided buffer structure):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name  | Type    | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | dwSize      | DWORD   | Buffer size or allocation limit\n  0x4    | 4    | pBuffer     | LPVOID  | Pointer to allocated data buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
