      "name": "LoadAndValidateGameConfigFiles",
      "signature": "void LoadAndValidateGameConfigFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Loads and validates three encrypted game configuration files with fallback mechanisms.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that no configuration files are already loaded (assert if true)\n2. Construct first filename using sprintf with format \"%s\\%s.gid\"\n3. Attempt to load first file via ReadAndValidateEncryptedFile()\n4. If first load fails, use XOR-based string decoding to generate alternate filename\n5. Initialize decoding tables from globals (szDecodeTable1-5) with sentinel 0x13\n6. Decode filename by indexing into tables based on string index array values\n7. Read decoded filename and validate encrypted data via ValidateEncryptedData()\n8. Store first file buffer in g_pFirstConfigFileBuffer\n9. Construct second filename using sprintf with format \"%s\\%s.clh\"\n10. Load and validate second file, storing in g_pSecondConfigFileBuffer\n11. If second file load failed, use fallback decoding (different index mapping)\n12. Call IndirectJumpThunk to determine if third file loading needed\n13. If third file required, copy config data to decode table (6 DWORD values)\n14. Decode third filename using different sentinel value 0x1a\n15. Load and validate third file, storing in g_pThirdConfigFileBuffer\n16. Zero out temporary filename buffer for security\n17. Set g_ConfigFilesLoadedFlag to 0 to indicate completion\n\nParameters:\n  Implicit Stack Parameters:\n    [ESP+0x54]: Decoded filename buffer (260 bytes)\n    [ESP+0x38-0x48]: Decoding table array (4 DWORD values)\n    [ESP+0x10-0x32]: String index array (39 byte values)\n    [ESP+0x48]: File buffer pointer\n    [ESP+0x4c]: File read size counter\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates global configuration file pointers on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic value 0x13: Sentinel marking end of first/second filename decoding sequences\n  Magic value 0x1a: Sentinel marking end of third filename decoding sequence\n  Magic value 0x400: Maximum buffer size for file reads (1024 bytes)\n  Assertion at entry: Validates no prior config files loaded (asserts if DAT_6ff3e8d8 or DAT_6ff3e8e4 non-NULL)\n  Fallback filenames: Constructed via XOR decoding if primary file read fails\n  Memory cleanup: All failed file buffers freed via FreeMemoryBlock()\n  Buffer zeroing: Filename buffer cleared byte-by-byte for security before return",
