      "name": "InitializeCryptoObjectBuffer",
      "signature": "void InitializeCryptoObjectBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a 32-byte global cryptographic object buffer by zeroing its contents.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ZeroMemory with address of global crypto object buffer (0x6ff3ecb8) and size 0x20 (32 bytes)\n2. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x20 (32): Exact size of the cryptographic object buffer structure\nGlobal address 0x6ff3ecb8: Static memory location for crypto object data\nThe zeroed buffer is subsequently populated by ExportAndHashObject during command processing\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function clears the CryptoObjectBuffer used for cryptographic operations. The buffer is 32 bytes total and serves as temporary storage for serialized cryptographic object data before hashing and random generation.",
