      "name": "GetDefaultUILanguage",
      "signature": "uint GetDefaultUILanguage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves the UI language identifier for the system with dynamic fallback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load kernel32.dll module into memory\n2. Attempt to get address of GetUILanguage function from kernel32\n3. If GetUILanguage is available, call it and return the UI language ID\n4. If GetUILanguage is unavailable, fall back to GetSystemDefaultLangID\n5. Free the kernel32.dll module handle\n6. Return the language ID as uint (LANGID)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses system APIs and hardcoded function names\n\nReturns:\nuint - Language identifier (LANGID) representing the system's default UI language\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- GetUILanguage is not available in all Windows versions; fallback ensures compatibility\n- Function dynamically loads kernel32.dll each time rather than caching\n- Language ID is zero-extended to uint for return in EAX",
