      "name": "InitializeCryptographicRNG",
      "signature": "int InitializeCryptographicRNG(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the cryptographic random number generator subsystem.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 288 bytes on stack for local buffers (32-byte seed + 256-byte hash output)\n2. Call SMemRandom to generate 32 bytes of random seed data from g_CryptoRandomSeed global\n3. Call MD5HashData to compute MD5 hash of 256-byte global data buffer g_CryptoHashBuffer1\n4. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData to initialize crypto RNG with seed buffer (83 bytes)\n5. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called during initialization when cryptographic services are first enabled\n- Uses global seed data from 0x6ff3ecf8 (32-byte seed buffer) and 0x6ff3eb58 (256-byte hash input)\n- Magic constant 0x53 (83 decimal) specifies the size of random data to generate\n- Stack allocation of 0x120 (288) bytes provides space for 32-byte seed + 256-byte hash output",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
