      "name": "InitializeAuthenticationSession",
      "signature": "uint InitializeAuthenticationSession(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net authentication session with cryptographic data and system environment information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize sessionMagicArray buffer with seed values [0, 0x49583836, calculated_magic_value, 0x0d]\n   - Magic value calculation: XOR 0x44324456 with language detection result\n   - Uses conditional negation (NEG/SBB) pattern for signed conversion\n2. Generate random seed bytes into randomSeedBytes array (3 bytes)\n3. Check authentication state via g_dwRNGInitEnabled flag\n4. If enabled, call GetSocketNameThreadSafe to retrieve cached magic value from socket\n5. Get current system UTC time using GetSystemTime() into localSystemTime\n6. Get local system time using GetLocalTime() into localSystemTime struct\n7. Convert both UTC and local SYSTEMTIME to FILETIME format (100-nanosecond intervals)\n8. Calculate timezone offset by subtracting local FILETIME from UTC FILETIME\n9. Divide timezone offset by 600000000 to convert from 100-nanosecond units to 60-second intervals\n   - Result is stored in timezoneOffsetMinutes for transmission to server\n10. Retrieve user default locale ID using GetUserDefaultLCID()\n11. Load kernel32.dll dynamically using LoadLibraryA()\n12. Attempt to get GetSystemDefaultUILanguage function pointer via GetProcAddress()\n13. If function exists, call it and mask result to 16-bit language ID value\n14. If not found, fall back to GetSystemDefaultLangID() function\n15. Query locale information for primary language group (LOCALE_IDEFAULTLANGUAGE, LOCALE_IGROUP: 0x400, 0x7)\n    - Mask result to 24-bit value and store in primaryLanguageGroup\n16. Query locale information for number format string (LOCALE_INUMBFORMAT: 0x400, 0x1002)\n    - Result stored in localeNumberFormatString buffer (up to 256 chars)\n17. Calculate cryptographic buffer size from locale string length plus 0x29 (41 bytes) padding\n18. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData to populate sessionMagicArray with cryptographic entropy (0x50 bytes)\n19. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n1 - Authentication session initialization successful\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value calculation uses NEG/SBB instruction pattern for signed integer conversion\n- If g_dwRNGInitEnabled is 0, magicValueResult defaults to 0 (no socket cache)\n- Language detection uses two-tier fallback: GetSystemDefaultUILanguage (modern) then GetSystemDefaultLangID (legacy)\n- Timezone calculation handles 64-bit subtraction with borrow propagation\n- Locale buffer sizes: primaryLanguageGroup=24bits, localeNumberFormatString=256 chars max\n- Cryptographic entropy generation adds 0x29 bytes overhead to locale string length\n\nStructure Layout:\nUsed structures: SYSTEMTIME (16 bytes for UTC/local), FILETIME (8 bytes for time conversion)\nsessionMagicArray: 74 DWORD elements (296 bytes total, seed initialization in first 4 elements)\nrandomSeedBytes: 4 bytes of random seed data\nlocalSystemTime: SYSTEMTIME structure (year, month, day, hour, minute, second, millisecond, day_of_week)",
