      "name": "InitializeEncryptionSeed",
      "signature": "void InitializeEncryptionSeed(uint dwSeedValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize cryptographic seed for encryption operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount() for time-based entropy\n2. MD5-hash 256 bytes of seed material from g_CryptoOutputBuffer\n3. Convert MD5 hash output to lowercase ASCII representation\n4. Call ComputeSHA1Hash() to process lowercase hash string through cipher\n5. Process tick count (0x1c bytes) through ComputeSHA1Hash() as second entropy source\n6. Generate 64 bytes of random data via SMemRandom from g_CryptoExportState\n7. Zero-fill g_CryptoExportState (0x40 bytes) to clear previous encryption state\n8. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData() to initialize cryptographic RNG with combined entropy\n9. Return void (function sets global crypto state)\n\nParameters:\nseedValue: uint - Initial seed parameter used to initialize encryption keys and derivation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function initializes global cryptographic state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack allocation: 0x174 (372) bytes for intermediate buffers\n- Uses fixed global addresses: g_CryptoOutputBuffer (0x6ff3ecb8, 256 bytes), g_CryptoExportState (0x6ff3ec58, 64 bytes)\n- Dual entropy sources: system time (GetTickCount) + random data (SMemRandom)\n- MD5 hash used as primary entropy source from seed material\n- __stdcall convention: caller cleans up parameter (RET 0x4)\n\nData Layout:\nStack buffers allocated for intermediate processing:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n------  ----  ---------------------   -----     ----------------------\n+0x00   0x100 md5HashBuffer           char[256] MD5 output of seed material\n+0x100  0x40  randomDataBuffer        byte[64]  Random data from SMemRandom\n+0x140  0x1c  tickCountBuffer         byte[28]  Tick count converted to buffer format\n+0x15c  0x18  processedHashArray      byte[24]  Hash processing workspace",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
