      "name": "VerifySha1Hash",
      "signature": "bool VerifySha1Hash(uint * pExpectedHash)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Verifies that a provided SHA-1 hash matches the computed hash of three cryptographic data regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 20-byte stack buffer for computed SHA-1 hash\n2. Call ComputeSha1Hash() to compute SHA-1 hash of three data regions (0x6ff3ecf8, 0x6ff3ed40, 0x6ff3ed18)\n3. Load expected hash pointer from stack parameter into EDI register\n4. Load computed hash address into ESI register\n5. Use REPE CMPSD instruction to compare computed hash vs expected hash (5 DWORDs = 20 bytes)\n6. Set AL = ZF flag result (1 if hashes match, 0 if differ)\n7. Return result as boolean (true=match, false=differ)\n\nParameters:\npExpectedHash (uint *): Pointer to expected SHA-1 hash array (5 DWORDs, 20 bytes total)\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if computed hash matches expected hash, false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number: 5 DWORDs = 20 bytes (standard SHA-1 hash output size)\n- Uses __stdcall convention: caller removes 4-byte parameter from stack (RET 0x4)\n- Hash comparison uses REPE CMPSD for efficient repeated DWORD comparison\n- Early exit: ZF flag set to 0 (false) immediately if any DWORD doesn't match\n\nStructure Layout:\nHash Array: 5 consecutive DWORDs (0x0 to 0x13)\n- Offset 0x0: DWORD 0 (bytes 0-3)\n- Offset 0x4: DWORD 1 (bytes 4-7)\n- Offset 0x8: DWORD 2 (bytes 8-11)\n- Offset 0xc: DWORD 3 (bytes 12-15)\n- Offset 0x10: DWORD 4 (bytes 16-19)",
