      "name": "GenerateEncryptionKeyWithHashing",
      "signature": "int GenerateEncryptionKeyWithHashing(void * pHashSource1, void * pHashSource2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Generates an encryption key through sequential MD5 hashing and cryptographic transformations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global crypto initialization flag (g_dwCryptoInitFlag) to 0\n2. Clear 0xBC bytes (188 bytes) of crypto cipher object structure at g_CryptoCipherObject using ZeroMemory\n3. MD5 hash the first source buffer (pHashSource1, 256 bytes) into hashBuffer1\n4. Apply TransformHashData to transform hashBuffer1\n5. MD5 hash the second source buffer (pHashSource2, 256 bytes) into hashBuffer2\n6. Apply TransformHashData to transform hashBuffer2\n7. MD5 hash implicit EDI parameter (256 bytes) into objectDataStructure\n8. Apply TransformHashData to transform objectDataStructure\n9. Export and hash object at g_dwCryptoContextState with combined hashBuffer1 and objectDataStructure\n10. Process crypto object at g_CryptoCipherObject with exported state and hashBuffer2\n11. Generate 32 bytes of random data into randomDataBuffer using g_CryptoRandomSeed\n12. MD5 hash pHashSource1 again (256 bytes) into hashBuffer3, result length returned in EAX\n13. Generate cryptographic random data at [EAX + 0x21] with size 0x55 bytes using randomFlag\n14. Return 0 (success status)\n\nParameters:\npHashSource1: void* - Pointer to first 256-byte hash source data buffer\npHashSource2: void* - Pointer to second 256-byte hash source data buffer\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 0 (success/initialization status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses implicit parameters in ESI and EDI registers beyond calling convention\n- All hash operations process 256 bytes (0x100) of input data\n- Random data buffer is 32 bytes (0x20) generated from cryptographic seed\n- Final generated cryptographic data size is 0x55 bytes (85 decimal)\n- Multiple global crypto state objects are initialized and modified:\n  g_dwCryptoInitFlag, g_CryptoCipherObject, g_CryptoRandomSeed, g_dwCryptoContextState\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function operates on several crypto state structures with 188-byte (0xBC) minimum size for cipher operations.",
