      "name": "PerformCryptographicOperations",
      "signature": "int PerformCryptographicOperations(void * pInputData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs cryptographic operations on input data including MD5 hashing, hash transformation, and secure random data generation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 832 bytes stack space for three hash buffers (256 bytes each) and working areas\n2. MD5 hash implicit ESI source buffer (256 bytes) into sourceBufferHash buffer\n3. Transform sourceBufferHash using cryptographic transformation function\n4. MD5 hash pInputData parameter buffer (256 bytes) into inputDataHash buffer\n5. Transform inputDataHash using cryptographic transformation function\n6. Export and combine both hashes with global crypto context state (g_dwCryptoContextState) using implicit EBX context\n7. MD5 hash implicit ESI buffer again (0x7fffffff size) into randomDataBuffer\n8. Extract randomFlag from implicit EDI parameter and generate cryptographic random data (0x52 bytes) into cryptoRandomOutput buffer\n9. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\n- pInputData (void*): Input data buffer to process with MD5 hashing and transformation\n- [implicit ESI]: Source buffer pointer (256 bytes) used for initial and secondary MD5 hashing\n- [implicit EDI]: Random flag/seed parameter passed to cryptographic functions\n- [implicit EBX]: Object context pointer used in export and hash operations\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Cryptographic operations completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses implicit register parameters (ESI, EDI, EBX) that are managed by caller\n- Three sequential MD5 operations: source buffer (256 bytes), input data (256 bytes), source buffer again (0x7fffffff)\n- Random data generation size fixed at 0x52 (82) bytes\n- All hash operations use 256-byte aligned buffers for cryptographic processing\n- Global state g_dwCryptoContextState is modified during export/hash operation",
