      "name": "InitializeRandomNumberGenerator",
      "signature": "void InitializeRandomNumberGenerator(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the cryptographic random number generator using SHA-1 hash with seed data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global seed data pointers and size from memory (0x6ff3e0f8, 0x6ff3e0f4, 0x6ff3e11c, 0x6ff3e0fc)\n2. Call InitializeObjectWithData to set up RNG object structure with imported seed data\n3. Call GetTickCount to obtain current system tick count for timestamp entropy\n4. Call InitializeSha1RandomHash to initialize SHA-1 based random hash generator\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses global data at 0x6ff3e0f8 (seed pointer 1)\n  - Uses global data at 0x6ff3e0f4 (seed pointer 2)  \n  - Uses global data at 0x6ff3e11c (seed data size = 0x20 bytes)\n  - Uses global data at 0x6ff3e0fc (seed data buffer)\n  - GetTickCount provides timestamp entropy for random seed\n  - SHA-1 hash algorithm used for cryptographic random generation",
