      "name": "InitializeCryptographicState",
      "signature": "uint InitializeCryptographicState(ObjectData * pCryptoObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize cryptographic state and generate random data for security operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate the crypto object using ValidateAndProcessCryptoObject with crypto config pointer\n2. Zero the memory region at DAT_6ff3ecb8 (32 bytes)\n3. If validation fails (ESI == 0), jump to validation_failed branch and return 0\n4. If validation succeeds:\n   a. Generate 20 bytes of random data into stack buffer (ESP+0x10)\n   b. Generate 64 bytes of random data into another stack buffer (ESP+0x24)\n   c. Zero the DAT_6ff3ec58 memory region (64 bytes)\n   d. Generate cryptographic random data with size 0x56 (86 bytes) and offset 0x54 (84 bytes)\n5. Return 1 on successful initialization, return 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npCryptoObject (ECX via __fastcall): Pointer to ObjectData structure for crypto validation\n- ObjectData.status: Validation status\n- ObjectData.pObject1: Primary crypto object pointer\n- ObjectData.pObject2: Secondary crypto object pointer\n\nReturns:\n- EAX = 1: Cryptographic state initialized successfully\n- EAX = 0: Validation of crypto object failed, initialization aborted\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __fastcall convention with first parameter in ECX register\n- Stack frame size: 0x54 bytes (84 bytes) for local random buffers\n- Magic values: 0x20 (32), 0x14 (20), 0x40 (64), 0x56 (86), 0x54 (84)\n- Memory regions DAT_6ff3f8e4, DAT_6ff3ecb8, DAT_6ff3ec58, DAT_6ff3ed40 are crypto configuration\n- Uses unaffected register EDI for possible state flags\n- All random buffers are stack-allocated for security (automatic cleanup on return)",
