      "name": "VerifyGameFilesAndInitializeCrypto",
      "signature": "int VerifyGameFilesAndInitializeCrypto(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Verifies game file integrity using MD5 hashing and initializes cryptographic state for client session\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 368-byte local verification data array by zeroing all DWORDs\n2. Obtain current Unix timestamp and system tick count as entropy sources for RNG\n3. Update global RNG seed (g_dwRngSeed at 0x6ff3f930) with combined time values\n4. Wait for verification file string (s_ver_IX86_1_mpq at 0x6ff3f510) to be loaded\n5. Check abort flag (g_SystemInitialized at 0x6ff3f644); exit if set\n6. Call VerifyGameFilesWithRevisionCheck() to validate game binaries with version data\n7. If verification fails, lock g_BattleNetCriticalSection, set failure flag g_dwGameStateVar3, unlock, return 0\n8. Call LoadAndValidateGameConfigFiles() for internal crypto state initialization\n9. Call MD5Init to initialize MD5 context\n10. Based on verification sub-parameter from thunk call:\n    - Path A (param=0): Hash binary buffer (0x200 bytes at esp+0x268) into first output\n    - Path B (param!=0): Hash binary into second output, decode primary and secondary strings\n11. Compute final MD5 hash of concatenated decoded string data\n12. Free previously allocated memory blocks (g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate, g_pSecondGridBufferTemplate)\n13. Get length of hash output string result\n14. Generate 0x51 (81) bytes of cryptographic random data appended after hash using GenerateCryptographicRandomData()\n15. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n1 = Success: Game files verified and cryptographic state initialized\n0 = Failure: File verification failed or aborted by system flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Abort flag check: If g_SystemInitialized is set at any point, immediately return 0\n- File loading wait: Function enters sleep loop (10ms intervals) waiting for verification file string\n- Concurrent access protection: Critical section lock (g_BattleNetCriticalSection) protects failure flag\n- Two verification paths: Behavior differs based on thunk sub-parameter (param value 0 vs non-zero)\n- Memory cleanup: Deallocates grid buffers before setting them to NULL\n- Magic values: 0x200 bytes = binary buffer size, 0x97 = 151 DWORDs (604 bytes local array)\n- RNG entropy: Combines Unix time, tick count, and previous seed for better randomness\n\nGlobal Data Items:\ng_SystemInitialized (0x6ff3f644) - Abort/initialization flag\ng_BattleNetCriticalSection (0x6ff3f1dc) - Thread synchronization lock\ng_dwGameStateVar3 (0x6ff3f1f4) - Verification failure flag\ng_dwRngSeed (0x6ff3f930) - RNG seed accumulator\ns_ver_IX86_1_mpq (0x6ff3f510) - Verification file string\ng_pFirstGridBufferTemplate (0x6ff3e8d8) - First allocated hash buffer\ng_pSecondGridBufferTemplate (0x6ff3e8e4) - Second allocated hash buffer\ng_pThirdConfigFileBuffer (0x6ff3e8e0) - Config file buffer for decoding",
