      "name": "ProcessSHA1Block",
      "signature": "void ProcessSHA1Block(SHA1_CTX_Context * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes one 512-bit SHA-1 message block and updates digest state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize message schedule array W[0..15] by loading 16 values from input block\n   at pContext->state[5..20], with byte-swapping\n2. Expand message schedule to W[16..79]: For each position i=16..79, compute\n   W[i] = ROTL(W[i-3] XOR W[i-8] XOR W[i-14] XOR W[i-16], rotate_amount)\n   where rotate_amount is masked from XOR to 5 bits\n3. Load current digest state values (A,B,C,D,E) from pContext->state[0..4]\n4. Execute Round 1 (indices 0..19, constant=0x5a827999):\n   F(B,C,D) = (B & C) | (~B & D)\n5. Execute Round 2 (indices 20..39, constant=0x6ed9eba1):\n   F(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D\n6. Execute Round 3 (indices 40..59, constant=0x8f1bbcdc):\n   F(B,C,D) = (B & C) | (B & D) | (C & D) [majority function]\n7. Execute Round 4 (indices 60..79, constant=0xca62c1d6):\n   F(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D\n8. Each iteration: Compute T = ROTL(A, 5) + F(B,C,D) + W[i] + constant + E\n   Update: E=D, D=C, C=ROTL(B, 30), B=A, A=T\n9. Add final state values back to pContext->state[0..4]\n\nParameters:\n  pContext: Pointer to SHA1_CTX_Context structure containing:\n            [0..4]: Current digest state (A,B,C,D,E)\n            [5..20]: Input message block (16 values, 64 bytes total)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies pContext->state[0..4] in-place with updated digest)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    4     state[0]      uint    Digest state A\n  0x04    4     state[1]      uint    Digest state B\n  0x08    4     state[2]      uint    Digest state C\n  0x0c    4     state[3]      uint    Digest state D\n  0x10    4     state[4]      uint    Digest state E\n  0x14    4     state[5..20]  uint[]  Input message block (16 DWORDS)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message schedule expansion uses 5-bit rotation amount from XOR result\n- State rotation after each step is 30-bit left rotation\n- Constants are round-specific: 0x5a827999, 0x6ed9eba1, 0x8f1bbcdc, 0xca62c1d6\n- Function is called by SHA1_Update to process each 512-bit block\n- All operations use 32-bit arithmetic with implicit overflow wrapping",
