      "name": "ComputeSHA1Hash",
      "signature": "void ComputeSHA1Hash(uint * pHashOutput, void * pInputData, uint dwInputLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes SHA-1 cryptographic hash of input data using standard SHA-1 algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SHA-1 state variables with standard constants (A=0x67452301, B=0xefcdab89, C=0x98badcfe, D=0x10325476, E=0xc3d2e1f0)\n2. If input length is zero, skip processing and return initial hash values\n3. For each 64-byte block of input data:\n   - Copy up to 64 bytes from input buffer to local block buffer\n   - Pad block with zeros if less than 64 bytes (64-byte alignment requirement)\n   - Call SHA1ProcessBlock to update hash state through 80 SHA-1 rounds\n   - Increment processed byte counter by 64\n4. Store final 5 SHA-1 hash words (A, B, C, D, E) to output buffer (20 bytes total)\n\nParameters:\n  pHashOutput: Pointer to 20-byte output buffer for SHA-1 hash (5 dwords)\n  pInputData: Pointer to input data to hash\n  inputLength: Length of input data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void (results written to pHashOutput)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero length input: Returns unmodified initial SHA-1 constants without processing\n  - Partial final block: Padded with zeros before processing\n  - Block alignment: Processes exactly 64-byte blocks; final block always padded",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
