      "name": "BuildBNCachePath",
      "signature": "void BuildBNCachePath(char * szBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Constructs the full path to bncache.dat file in the module directory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get module handle for current process using GetModuleHandleA(NULL)\n2. Retrieve full module file path using GetModuleFileNameA() into pBuffer\n3. Search for backslash separators in the path to locate directory portion\n4. Find the last backslash separator by repeatedly searching forward\n5. Truncate path at last separator to keep only directory portion\n6. Scan from beginning to null terminator to find append position\n7. Copy filename \"\\bncache.dat\" (13 bytes) from szBNCacheFileName to end of directory path\n8. Return with complete cache file path in pBuffer\n\nParameters:\npBuffer - char* - Pre-allocated buffer (260 bytes) to receive full cache file path\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Cache file path is returned in pBuffer parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size is fixed at 0x104 (260 bytes - MAX_PATH)\n- Filename constant \"\\bncache.dat\" includes leading backslash separator\n- If path contains no backslash, entire path serves as directory base\n- Scans path character-by-character to find null terminator position",
