      "name": "FillRandomNumberBuffer",
      "signature": "void FillRandomNumberBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Fills random number buffer using Linear Congruential Generator (LCG) algorithm\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load buffer base address from g_pHashLookupTable global variable\n2. If buffer address is null, exit early without generating random numbers\n3. Initialize LCG state to 0x100001\n4. Iterate 256 times (0x100) to generate random numbers:\n   a. Apply LCG transformation: state = (state * 0x7d + 3) mod 0x2aaaab\n   b. Extract remainder from division as intermediate random value\n   c. Apply LCG transformation again on intermediate value\n   d. Combine two 16-bit values into 32-bit DWORD\n   e. Write generated DWORD to buffer at calculated offsets\n5. Increment buffer write pointer and continue to next iteration\n6. Return to caller\nParameters: None\nReturns: void\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pHashLookupTable is NULL, function returns immediately without doing work\n- LCG modulus 0x2aaaab ensures good distribution across range\n- Four DWORDs are generated per iteration (0x800 - 0xfffffc00 offset calculations)\n- Buffer base offset adjustments: -0x800, 0x0, +0x400, +0x800",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
