      "name": "GetCachedSystemTimeAdjusted",
      "signature": "void * GetCachedSystemTimeAdjusted(DWORD timeContextSeconds)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4 *",
      "comment": "Retrieves cached system time adjusted by a context value in seconds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load cached context value from g_dwCachedTimeContext\n2. Compare with current timeContextSeconds parameter\n3. If context unchanged, call GetTickCount and check if tick count matches g_dwCachedTickCount\n4. If both context and tick match, return cached result (early exit optimization)\n5. Otherwise, allocate 16-byte SYSTEMTIME structure on stack\n6. Call GetSystemTime() to fetch current system time into local SYSTEMTIME\n7. Call SystemTimeToFileTime() to convert SYSTEMTIME to 64-bit FILETIME format\n8. Load FILETIME result into g_dwCachedTimeValueLow/High (cache addresses passed to function)\n9. Perform 64-bit multiplication: timeContextSeconds * 10000000 (magic constant for 100-nanosecond ticks)\n10. Add multiplication result to cached FILETIME (64-bit addition using ADC for carry)\n11. Store adjusted result back to g_dwCachedTimeValueLow/High\n12. Update g_dwCachedTimeContext with current timeContextSeconds parameter\n13. Call GetTickCount() and store in g_dwCachedTickCount for cache validation\n14. Return pointer to g_dwCachedTimeValueLow as the cached adjusted time\n\nParameters:\n- timeContextSeconds (DWORD, __stdcall stack param): Time adjustment in seconds, multiplied by 10M to convert to 100-nanosecond intervals\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Pointer to 64-bit cached FILETIME value containing adjusted system time\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x989680 (10,000,000): Converts seconds to 100-nanosecond intervals in FILETIME format\n- Early return optimization: If same context and GetTickCount matches, skip expensive system time fetch\n- 64-bit arithmetic: Uses EDX:EAX pair for multiplication result, ADC instruction for carry propagation when adding to 64-bit time\n\nGlobal Data Structure:\nCache maintains 4 DWORD values consecutively in memory:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name                | Type   | Purpose\n  ------ | ---- | ----------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------\n  +0x00  | 4    | g_dwCachedTickCount     | DWORD  | GetTickCount value from last update\n  +0x04  | 4    | g_dwCachedTimeContext   | DWORD  | Context value from last update\n  +0x08  | 4    | g_dwCachedTimeValueLow  | DWORD  | Low DWORD of adjusted FILETIME\n  +0x0C  | 4    | g_dwCachedTimeValueHigh | DWORD  | High DWORD of adjusted FILETIME (complete 64-bit value)",
