      "name": "ComputeDataHash",
      "signature": "void ComputeDataHash(uint * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Computes a cryptographic hash over input data using a lookup table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert input byte count to 4-byte chunks (dwByteCount >> 2)\n2. If chunk count is zero, skip loop and return\n3. Load hash table base pointer from g_pCacheIoBuffer at 0x6ff3f62c\n4. Initialize hash accumulator to 0xeeeeeeee\n5. For each 4-byte chunk of input data:\n   a. Load current 32-bit chunk from pData\n   b. Extract low byte of current offset and look up value in hash table\n   c. Add lookup value (from offset 0x1000 in table) to hash accumulator\n   d. Multiply accumulator by magic constant 0x21 and add 0x3\n   e. XOR the result with the loaded data chunk\n   f. Compute bit rotation via NOT, left shift by 0x15, add 0x11111111\n   g. Apply right shift by 0xb on current offset\n   h. Combine via OR operation\n   i. Store result back to data location (in-place modification)\n6. Continue until all chunks processed\n7. Return with processed data in place\n\nParameters:\n  pData (ECX) : Pointer to 4-byte aligned data buffer to hash\n  dwByteCount (EDX) : Total byte count (truncated to multiple of 4)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function modifies data in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Byte count is truncated to multiple of 4 (dwByteCount >> 2)\n  - If dwByteCount < 4, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Hash table offset 0x1000 bytes past g_pCacheIoBuffer base\n  - Magic constants: 0x21 (multiply), 0x3 (add), 0x11111111 (rotate)\n  - Output overwrites input buffer (in-place transformation)",
