      "name": "CleanupBNCacheFile",
      "signature": "void CleanupBNCacheFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Closes and deletes the game cache file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load cached file handle from g_hCacheFileHandle global variable\n2. Compare handle against INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (0xFFFFFFFF / -1)\n3. If handle is valid, call CloseHandle Windows API to close it\n4. Reset g_hCacheFileHandle to INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE marker\n5. Allocate 260 bytes (MAX_PATH) on stack for cache file path\n6. Initialize path buffer with null terminator at start\n7. Call BuildBNCachePath to construct full cache file path\n8. Call DeleteFileA Windows API to remove cache file from disk\n9. Clean up 260-byte stack allocation and return\n\nParameters:\nNone - function is parameterless, operates on global g_hCacheFileHandle\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value, performs cleanup operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\nINVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (0xFFFFFFFF) indicates no open file handle and skips close\n260-byte stack buffer (0x104) is Windows MAX_PATH constant for file paths\nFunction uses __stdcall calling convention with callee stack cleanup",
