      "name": "FindHashTableEntryByKey",
      "signature": "int FindHashTableEntryByKey(char * pKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Performs linear probing hash table lookup for cache entry matching a string key.\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute three independent hash values for the input key using different hash functions (indices 0, 1, 2)\n2. Load hash table metadata: size (cached at 0x6ff3f624) and table base address (0x6ff3f630)\n3. Calculate initial probe index by masking first hash value with (size - 1)\n4. Load hash table entry at probe index: check status field (offset +0xC)\n5. If entry status is -1 (empty), return -1 (not found)\n6. For occupied entries, compare both stored hash values at offsets +0x0 and +0x4\n7. If hashes match, verify entry status is not -2 (deleted marker)\n8. If all checks pass, load data field at offset +0x8 and compare with search key\n9. If data field is null (0), save index as fallback and continue probing\n10. If data matches the search key exactly, return current index immediately\n11. Increment index with wraparound mask and repeat from step 4 until full table probed\n12. Return saved fallback index (entry with matching hashes but null data) or -1\nParameters:\npKey (char *): Pointer to null-terminated string key to search for in cache\nReturns:\nint: Index of matching cache entry (0+), or -1 if no matching entry found\nSpecial Cases:\nEntry status -1 indicates empty slot; -2 indicates deleted slot previously removed",
