      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeGameCache",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitializeGameCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes game cache file with CRC32 integrity checks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 5KB temporary I/O buffer\n2. Generate random number seed for hash operations\n3. Allocate 44-byte cache header buffer\n4. Attempt to open existing cache file and validate:\n   a. Read 44-byte header and verify file size >= 44 bytes\n   b. Check magic number is 0x1a334e42 (reject old format 0x1a324e42)\n   c. Compute CRC32 of header bytes 0-31 using lookup table polynomial\n   d. Compare computed CRC with stored checksum at offset 0x20\n   e. Verify all table offset and size fields are non-zero\n   f. For first table: clamp min entry count to 0x400, multiply by 16 bytes, verify file contains data\n   g. Allocate memory for first table and read from file\n   h. Compute CRC32 of first table data and compare with stored CRC\n   i. Decode first table using hash-based key transformation (ComputeStringHashForTable + ComputeDataHashWithKeyTable)\n   j. Repeat steps f-i for second table with separate offsets and CRC values\n5. If file missing or any validation fails:\n   a. Delete any temp buffers allocated during failed attempt\n   b. Create new cache file (truncate existing file)\n   c. Initialize header with magic 0x1a334e42\n   d. Set first table offset to 0x2c (end of header), minimum 0x400 entries\n   e. Allocate 0x4000 bytes for first index buffer (1024 entries * 16 bytes)\n   f. Initialize all entries with 0xffffffff sentinel values\n   g. Set second table offset to 0x402c, minimum 0x800 entries\n   h. Allocate 0x4000 bytes for second index buffer\n6. Mark g_dwCacheClearFlag = 1 to indicate cache is ready\n7. Leave critical section (LeaveCriticalSection on g_CacheLock)\n8. Return 1 for success, 0 for failure (only on file creation error)\n\nParameters: void\n\nReturns: int - 1 on success (file valid or new file created), 0 on failure (file creation failed)\n\nCACHE FILE HEADER (44 bytes):\nOffset 0x00-0x03: Magic number (0x1a334e42 for valid cache, 0x1a324e42 for old format to reject)\nOffset 0x04-0x07: First table data offset from EOF (typically 0x2c for post-header)\nOffset 0x08-0x0B: First table max entry count (minimum 0x400 = 1024 entries)\nOffset 0x0C-0x0F: Second table data offset from EOF (typically 0x402c)\nOffset 0x10-0x13: Second table max entry count (minimum 0x800 = 2048 entries)\nOffset 0x14-0x1F: Reserved (12 bytes, zeroed)\nOffset 0x20-0x23: CRC32 checksum of bytes 0-31 (computed with 0xffffffff initial value, inverted final)\nOffset 0x24-0x27: Reserved/future use (8 bytes)\n\nVALIDATION ERROR CODES:\n0x01: File size is zero or exceeds 10MB limit\n0x02: File read incomplete (less than 44 bytes read)\n0x03: Invalid magic number (not 0x1a334e42)\n0x04: Header CRC32 mismatch\n0x05: First table offset or size is zero\n0x06: Second table offset or size is zero\n0x07: First table data extends beyond file size\n0x08: First table read incomplete\n0x09: First table CRC32 mismatch\n0x0A: Second table data extends beyond file size\n0x0B: Second table read incomplete\n0x0C: Second table CRC32 mismatch",
