      "name": "ClearHashTableEntries",
      "signature": "void ClearHashTableEntries(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears all entries in a hash table by marking them invalid and resetting their state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop by calling FindHashTableEntryByKey(0) to get first entry index\n2. Check if entry index equals 0xffffffff (no entries sentinel) - exit if true\n3. Enter main processing loop:\n   a. Load cache hash table base (g_pCacheHashTable)\n   b. Load cache control block base (g_pCacheControlBlock)\n   c. Load max entry count from control block + 0x1c\n   d. Calculate pointer to entry's next field: (index * 16) + 0xc + hash_table_base\n   e. Load next entry index from current entry's next field\n   f. Compare next index against max entry count\n   g. If within bounds: calculate entry offset (index * 16 + g_pCacheEntries) and clear bytes at offset+8 and offset+0xc\n   h. Mark current entry as invalid by setting its next field to 0xfffffffe\n   i. Call FindHashTableEntryByKey(0) to get next entry\n   j. Compare result - if not 0xffffffff, repeat from step 3\n4. Exit function\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters. Operates on global cache hash table structures.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic values: 0xffffffff = iteration end sentinel, 0xfffffffe = invalid entry marker\nIteration uses linked-list pattern via entry's next field at offset+0xc\nOnly clears state fields (offset+8 and offset+0xc) for valid entries within bounds\nCalled during cache initialization and reset operations",
