      "name": "ValidateAndUpdateCacheFile",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndUpdateCacheFile(char * pCacheIdentifier, byte * pCacheData, char * pDataBuffer, FILETIME * pSystemTimestamp, int reserved, int flags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates input parameters and updates Battle.net cache file with new cache entry\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate all input parameters (non-null pointers, cache identifier non-empty, data buffer size <= 0x1000000)\n2. Enter critical section to serialize cache access\n3. Clear hash table entries for current operation\n4. Scan available slots in cache entry table:\n   - Check each slot: if unused (marked 0) or data address exceeds buffer boundary, use it\n   - Loop through slots until valid slot found or limit reached\n5. If no valid slot in initial scan, perform full scan with file validation:\n   - For each slot: verify data address within buffer bounds\n   - Read 4-byte file header and validate checksum (0x144 bytes)\n   - Read 0x140 bytes of cached data from file\n   - Get system time and compare with cached timestamp using CompareFileTime\n   - Continue until valid slot found or all slots exhausted\n6. If valid slot found (slotIndex < slotCount):\n   - Clear invalidated hash table references (set to 0xfffffffe)\n   - Compute three hash functions for cache lookup\n   - Find empty hash table slot using linear probing\n   - Store entry: hash values, data size, slot index, flags\n   - Initialize 0x144-byte header structure with version 0x0144\n   - Get system time from 5 separate calls (captures 5 different timestamps)\n   - Copy cache identifier string to header\n   - Calculate CRC32 of data buffer\n   - Calculate CRC32 of header structure\n7. Write cache entry to file:\n   - Seek to slot file offset\n   - Write 0x144-byte header\n   - Write serialized data buffer\n8. Write hash and data tables:\n   - Allocate temporary buffer (max of table sizes)\n   - Copy hash table and calculate CRC32\n   - Write hash table to file\n   - Copy data table and calculate CRC32\n   - Write data table to file\n   - Free temporary buffer\n9. Write cache file header (0x2c bytes):\n   - Calculate CRC32 of header\n   - Seek to file start\n   - Write header and verify write success\n10. If slot exhausted (>= 0x400) or hash table full, set error and rebuild cache\n11. Leave critical section\n12. Return true if errorStatus == 0, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pCacheIdentifier: String identifier for cache entry (char*, ECX)\n- pCacheData: Pointer to data buffer to cache (byte*, EDX)\n- pDataBuffer: Pointer to serialized buffer with embedded length (char*, [ESP+8])\n- pSystemTimestamp: FILETIME structure with current system time (FILETIME*, [ESP+C])\n- reserved: Reserved parameter (undefined4, [ESP+10])\n- flags: Control flags for cache operation (int, [ESP+14])\n\nReturns:\n- true (1): Cache file updated successfully\n- false (0): Validation failed, parameter error, slot allocation error, or file write error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error 0xb: No valid cache slot available (>= 0x400), rebuilds cache\n- Error 0xc: Hash table insertion failure (slot exhausted)\n- Error 0xd-0x10: Cache data or table write failures\n- Error 0x11: Final header write failure\n- Magic numbers: 0x144 = header size, 0x140 = data read size, 0x2c = file header size, 0x400 = max slots\n- CRC32 precomputed table at g_pCrc32LookupTable\n- Cache synchronization via g_CacheLock critical section",
