      "name": "ReallocateGlobalSendBuffer",
      "signature": "void ReallocateGlobalSendBuffer(byte * pSourceBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Reallocates the global send buffer with new data from source.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current global buffer pointer from g_pGlobalSendBuffer\n2. If buffer exists (non-null), delete it using DeleteObjectTrampoline with source file metadata\n3. Allocate new memory block sized to actualBufferSize using AllocateMemory\n4. Store new allocated pointer back into g_pGlobalSendBuffer global\n5. Copy actualBufferSize bytes from pSourceBuffer to new buffer using optimized memory copy:\n   a. Divide size by 4 to get DWORD count, copy DWORD-aligned chunks using REP MOVSD\n   b. Extract remainder (size & 3), copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually using REP MOVSB\n6. Return void (new buffer pointer stored in global)\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceBuffer - Pointer to source data buffer to copy (stack parameter at ESP+0x4)\n  bufferSize - Unused stack parameter (actual size passed via EAX register implicitly)\n  [IMPLICIT] actualBufferSize - Size in bytes to allocate and copy (passed via EAX register)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function updates global g_pGlobalSendBuffer with pointer to new allocated buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null buffer check: If g_pGlobalSendBuffer is null, skips deletion and only allocates\n  - Optimized copy: Uses REP MOVSD for DWORD-aligned data (up to size-3), then REP MOVSB for remainder\n  - Source file metadata: Passes source file string szBnSendSourcePath and line numbers (0x1bd=445, 0x1be=446)\n\nStructure Layout: g_pGlobalSendBuffer points to untyped buffer (byte array)",
