      "name": "InitializeThreadSafeMD5Hash",
      "signature": "uint InitializeThreadSafeMD5Hash(uint dwContextHandle, void * pInitializationData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes thread-safe MD5 hash context with critical section protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire BattleNet critical section lock via EnterCriticalSection() for thread-safe access\n2. Load g_dwMD5ContextHandle from 0x6ff3f1f4 to check initialization flag (0=uninitialized)\n3. Test if context already initialized; if yes, skip initialization and jump to leave_critical_section\n4. If uninitialized, load dwContextHandle parameter from stack offset ESP+0x4\n5. Load pInitializationData parameter pointer from stack offset ESP+0x8\n6. Store dwContextHandle value in g_dwMD5ContextHandle global to mark as initialized\n7. Call MD5HashData() with g_MD5HashContext address, pInitializationData pointer, and 0x80 (128) byte size\n8. Jump to leave_critical_section label to exit critical section\n9. Release critical section lock via LeaveCriticalSection() at 0x6ff3f1dc\n10. Return 1 in EAX to indicate successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n  dwContextHandle (uint): Hash context identifier/handle to store as initialization flag in global state\n  pInitializationData (void*): Pointer to 128-byte data buffer for MD5 hash state initialization\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success indicator)",
