      "name": "DestroyLinkedListItems",
      "signature": "uint DestroyLinkedListItems(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Destroys all items in a global linked list by iterating and calling destructors.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Acquire critical section lock for thread-safe list access\\n2. Load first node from global linked list head (g_dwGameStateVar1)\\n3. If list is empty (null), skip loop and jump to cleanup\\n4. Loop: Load next node pointer from current node at offset +0x128\\n5. Call destructor function via function pointer (free-like operation)\\n6. Update global list head to next node\\n7. Test if next node is valid; if so, repeat loop\\n8. Release critical section lock\\n9. Return 1 (success status)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - Operates on global game state variables\\n\\nReturns:\\nuint - Returns 1 to indicate successful completion of list destruction\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty list: If g_dwGameStateVar1 is null, function skips processing and returns 1\\n- Critical section: Synchronizes access across multiple threads to prevent race conditions\\n- Node structure: Each node has a next pointer at offset +0x128\\n- Destructor call: Invokes cleanup routine for each node before removing from list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:7fa676f12170a4152c5871925310d481",
