      "name": "CreateAndAddHashEntry",
      "signature": "uint CreateAndAddHashEntry(uint dwHashId, HashDataBuffer * pDataToHash)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Creates a new hash entry node with MD5 hash of input data and adds it to a thread-safe global linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x5f (95) bytes for hash entry node structure\n2. Calls MD5HashData to compute hash of 0x120 (288) bytes starting at node offset +0x4\n3. Scans hash output from offset +0x4 to find null terminator (string length)\n4. Calculates actual hash string length in bytes including null terminator\n5. Stores hash length at node offset +0x124, hash ID at offset +0, NULL at offset +0x128\n6. Validates hash length constraint: length must be <= 0x120 bytes\n7. If validation fails: calls assertion handler with line number 0x65 and exits with -1\n8. Enters critical section protecting g_dwGameStateVar1 (list head) and g_dwGameStateVar2 (list tail)\n9. If list is empty (head is NULL): sets both head and tail pointers to new node\n10. If list has items: retrieves current tail, links its next pointer (+0x128) to new node\n11. Updates tail pointer to new node\n12. Leaves critical section and returns 1 (success)\n\nHash Entry Structure Layout (95 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type     Description\n0x0     4     dwHashId           uint     Hash entry identifier/type from parameter\n0x4     0x120 szHashData         char[288] MD5 hash output (null-terminated string)\n0x124   4     dwHashLength       uint     Length of hash string in bytes\n0x128   4     pNextEntry         void*    Pointer to next node in linked list (NULL for tail)\n\nParameters:\n  dwHashId: uint - Identifier/type for this hash entry, stored at offset +0\n  pDataToHash: HashDataBuffer* - Pointer to 288-byte data buffer to hash\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Returns 1 on success; triggers assertion failure and exit(-1) on invalid hash length\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x5f: allocated node size (95 bytes)\n  - Magic number 0x120: fixed input data size for MD5 (288 bytes)\n  - Magic number 0x124: offset in node storing hash output length\n  - Magic number 0x128: offset in node for next pointer (linked list linkage)\n  - Offset +0x4: where MD5 hash output is stored (288-byte buffer)\n  - Assertion at line 0x65: triggers if computed hash length > 0x120 bytes\n  - Thread-safe: uses g_BattleNetCriticalSection for list head/tail access\n  - Linked list is singly-linked via next pointers at offset +0x128 in each node",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
