      "name": "CreateNetworkOperationEntry",
      "signature": "uint CreateNetworkOperationEntry(uint dwOperationType, uint * pOperationData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Creates and registers a new network operation entry in a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate a buffer (58 bytes) via AllocateBuffer(0x3a, 0)\n2. Validate data size: cap to 0x120 bytes if exceeds limit\n3. If data size is 0, initialize first byte to null and jump to size check\n4. Copy operation data to allocated buffer via DWORD-aligned copy loop\n5. Copy remaining bytes (0-3 bytes) via byte copy loop\n6. Store data size at offset +0x124 (0x49 * 4) in allocated buffer\n7. Store operation type at offset +0x0 in allocated buffer\n8. Store next pointer at offset +0x128 (0x4a * 4) = 0\n9. If data size <= 0x120:\n   - Enter critical section at 0x6ff3f1dc\n   - Check if head pointer (0x6ff3f64c) is non-null\n   - If non-null, link current entry to last entry's next pointer at +0x128\n   - Update head pointer to current entry (first insert)\n   - Update tail pointer (0x6ff3f650) to current entry\n   - Leave critical section\n   - Return 1 (success)\n10. If data size > 0x120: trigger assertion and exit with code -1\n\nParameters:\n- operationType: uint - Type identifier for the network operation\n- pOperationData: uint* - Pointer to operation data to copy\n\nReturns:\n- uint - 1 on success, or calls _exit(-1) on size violation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Size limit: 0x121 bytes (289 bytes) - enforced via assertion\n- Buffer allocation size: 0x3a bytes (58 bytes) - fixed allocation\n- Structure offsets: 0x0=type, 0x4=data start, 0x124=size, 0x128=next pointer\n- Zero-size data is valid - initializes first byte to null\n- Linked list uses doubly-linked structure via critical section protection\n- Magic numbers: 0x120 (288), 0x121 (289), 0x3a (58), 0x124 (292 offset), 0x128 (296 offset)\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe allocated entry structure (58+ bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | type       | uint | Operation type identifier\n4      | 288  | data       | byte[288] | Operation data payload (variable length)\n292    | 4    | size       | uint | Size of data copied (0-0x120)\n296    | 4    | next       | ptr  | Pointer to next entry in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
