      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that copies data to global buffer and returns success status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Move source data pointer from EDX to EAX per __fastcall calling convention\n2. Push ECX register to preserve it across the function call\n3. Call CopyDataToGlobalBuffer to perform the actual copy operation\n4. Set return value in EAX to 1 (success indicator)\n5. Return to caller with success status\n\nParameters:\npSourceData (void *) - Pointer to source data buffer to be copied\n  Passed in EDX per __fastcall convention, moved to EAX for callee\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating successful copy operation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function always returns success (1) regardless of copy outcome\n- Acts as a simple wrapper around CopyDataToGlobalBuffer with hardcoded success indicator\n- Uses __fastcall convention: parameter in EDX, first local in ECX\n- Function pointer likely stored in callback table at 0x6ff3e228 for indirect invocation",
