      "name": "ClearPacketDispatchStatus",
      "signature": "void ClearPacketDispatchStatus(byte byPacketType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears packet dispatch status and auxiliary state for a specific packet type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-extend byPacketType from AL to EAX (ensure byte range 0x00-0x5D)\n2. Multiply index by 4 bytes via left shift (SHL EAX, 2) for DWORD array offset\n3. Zero ECX register to prepare zero value for array writes\n4. Write zero to g_dwPacketDispatchStatus[index] to clear packet dispatch state\n5. Write zero to g_dwPacketAuxState[index] to clear packet auxiliary state\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nbyPacketType (byte): Packet type identifier (valid range 0x00-0x5D, 94 types)\n  Caller responsible for bounds checking; out-of-range values write beyond array\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nArray bounds: Each table is 376 bytes (94 DWORD entries \u00d7 4 bytes each)\nValid range: Packet types 0x00 through 0x5D (0 through 93 decimal)\nParallel arrays: Both tables cleared simultaneously to maintain state consistency\nInitialization: Called from InitializeGameData to reset packet state on startup\nArray addresses: g_dwPacketDispatchStatus (0x6ff3ed58), g_dwPacketAuxState (0x6ff3eed8)",
