      "name": "CachePacketBufferWrapper",
      "signature": "uint CachePacketBufferWrapper(void * pSourceBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that caches packet buffer data with network byte order conversion\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Accept packet buffer pointer in ECX and size in EDX (__fastcall convention)\\n2. Transfer size from EDX to EBX for custom calling convention\\n3. Call CopyAndCachePacketBuffer with IMPLICIT bufferSize in EBX\\n4. Return fixed success code 1\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pSourceBuffer (void* in ECX) - Pointer to network packet buffer to cache\\n  dwBufferSize (uint in EDX) - Size of packet buffer in bytes\\n\\nReturns:\\n  uint - Always returns 1 indicating operation initiated (not completion status)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Wrapper adapts __fastcall (ECX, EDX) to custom convention (ECX, EBX)\\n  - Callee (CopyAndCachePacketBuffer) expects size as IMPLICIT parameter in EBX\\n  - Network byte order conversion of packet header handled by callee at offset +0x18\\n  - Always returns success regardless of allocation success in underlying function\\n  - Function is referenced through packet handling callbacks",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
