      "name": "Generate37ByteRandomKey",
      "signature": "int Generate37ByteRandomKey(void * pUnused, void * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Generate a 37-byte cryptographic random key by delegating to random data generator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI register (required by __fastcall convention)\n2. Preserve first parameter (pUnused) in EDI for potential later use\n3. Move second parameter (pOutputBuffer) to ECX for function call\n4. Push constant 0x25 (37 bytes) as size parameter\n5. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData to fill buffer with random bytes\n6. Set return value EAX to 1 (success indicator)\n7. Restore EDI register and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void *) - First parameter passed in ECX, preserved but unused\n  pOutputBuffer (void *) - Second parameter passed in EDX, pointer to output buffer\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 indicating successful random key generation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fixed size: Generates exactly 37 bytes (0x25), no variable length support\n  - Success only: No error handling, always returns success (1)\n  - Buffer safety: Caller responsible for ensuring pOutputBuffer has at least 37 bytes",
