      "name": "WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout",
      "signature": "int WaitForResourceReadyWithTimeout(byte byResourceIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Waits for a resource at the given index to become available with 45-second timeout and cancellation support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetTickCount() to establish baseline timestamp in EBX\n2. Load resource state from array g_dwResourceStates[resourceIndex]\n3. If resource state is non-zero (available), return success (EAX=1)\n4. Check g_dwCancellationFlag - if set, jump to cancellation handler\n5. Call GetTickCount() to get current time, calculate elapsed duration\n6. Compare elapsed time against 45000ms threshold (0xafc8)\n7. If elapsed exceeds threshold, jump to timeout handler\n8. Call Sleep(10ms) to prevent CPU busy-waiting\n9. Reload resource state and loop back to step 3\n10. Timeout path: Enter critical section, set g_dwGameErrorCode=0x11 if not already set, exit critical section, return 0\n11. Cancellation path: Enter critical section, set g_dwGameErrorCode=0x12 if not already set, exit critical section, return 0\n\nParameters:\n  resourceIndex (byte) - Array index (0-255) for resource state lookup in g_dwResourceStates\n\nReturns:\n  1 (EAX) if resource became available before timeout or cancellation\n  0 (EAX) if timeout occurred (45 seconds elapsed) or cancellation flag was set\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Timeout threshold: 45000ms (0xafc8 in hex)\n  - Sleep interval: 10ms (0xa) per retry to prevent CPU spin-waiting\n  - Error codes: 0x11 for timeout, 0x12 for cancellation\n  - Critical section g_BattleNetCriticalSection protects g_dwGameErrorCode updates\n  - Error code is only set if not already set (allows first error to persist)\n  - Resource array indexed via scaled addressing: [ESI*4 + 0x6ff3ed58] for 32-bit DWORD elements\n\nStructure Layout (g_dwResourceStates array):\n  Offset  Size  Description\n  ------  ----  -----------\n  +0      4     Resource state DWORD (0=not ready, non-zero=available)",
