      "name": "ProcessAuthenticationCommand",
      "signature": "uint ProcessAuthenticationCommand(CommandRequest * pRequest, uint dwRequestSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes authentication commands with SHA-1 hash verification and state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that request size is at least 24 bytes (minimum CommandRequest structure size)\n2. Extract command type from offset +0 of request structure into nCommandType variable\n3. Zero 32-byte global crypto output buffer (g_CryptoOutputBuffer at 0x6ff3ecb8) for security\n4. Check if command type equals 0 for hash verification path\n5. If command type is 0: call VerifySha1Hash with SHA-1 hash data at offset +4\n   - If hash verification returns non-zero: set success flag and return 1\n   - If hash verification fails: call InitializeGlobalStateOnce with error 0x12 and return 0\n6. Check if command type equals 2 for immediate success path\n7. If command type is 2: enter critical section, set success flag, set error code 0xe, leave section, return 1\n8. For other command types: enter critical section, set error code 0x12, leave section, return 0\n9. Use critical section (g_BattleNetCriticalSection at 0x6ff3f1dc) to protect error state\n\nParameters:\npRequest (CommandRequest *): Pointer to command request structure, minimum 24 bytes\n  - Field at +0: nCommandType (uint) - command identifier (0=verify hash, 2=success, other=error)\n  - Field at +4: sha1Hash data (20 bytes) - SHA-1 hash for verification\ndwRequestSize (uint): Size of request buffer in bytes, must be at least 24\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 on successful command processing (hash valid or command type 2), 0 on any error condition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Request size < 24 bytes: immediate return 0 without processing\n- Command type 0: SHA-1 hash must pass verification\n- Command type 2: sets success flag without requiring hash verification\n- Error codes: 0x12 for invalid command type, 0xe for command type 2\n- Thread safety: critical section protects error state at g_dw_GameStateVar3",
