      "name": "ProcessNewsBuffer",
      "signature": "void ProcessNewsBuffer(byte * pNewsBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that invokes news entry buffer processor\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cast char* parameter to byte* pointer type\n2. Invoke ProcessNewsEntryBuffer with byte pointer parameter\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pNewsBuffer - Pointer to packed news buffer with format:\n                [+0] byte: entry count (max 256)\n                [+5] DWORD: timestamp\n                [+9] DWORD: line number for assertion\n                [+13] variable-length entries (DWORD timestamp + null-terminated text)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a simple type-casting wrapper function\n  - Actual processing performed by ProcessNewsEntryBuffer at 0x6ff32c30\n  - Uses fastcall convention with ECX parameter passed via stack manipulation",
