      "name": "ProcessProtocolMessage",
      "signature": "uint ProcessProtocolMessage(byte * pMessageBuffer, uint dwMessageSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes Battle.net protocol messages and executes command-specific logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate message buffer: check minimum size (>= 5 bytes), verify null termination at messageSize-1, scan for embedded nulls in range [4, messageSize-1)\n2. Extract command code from first DWORD at pMessageBuffer offset 0x0\n3. Mask command code with 0xff0f to obtain base command type (ignoring flag bits 4-7)\n4. For commands 0x0/0x100/0x102: allocate memory and generate 0x5d bytes of cryptographic random data\n5. Initialize global state flags: g_dw_ProtocolStateFlags = 0, g_dw_GlobalStateInitialized = 0\n6. Apply patches to file download stub using szPatchDirectoryName and szPatchesDirectoryName\n7. Execute command-specific handler:\n   - Command 0x0: Set g_dw_GlobalStateInitialized=1 and g_dw_InitializationComplete=1\n   - Command 0x100: MD5 hash 0xfe bytes of payload, initialize RNG, patch download stub, initiate file download with flags 0x80000002\n   - Commands 0x101/0x102: Call InitializeGlobalStateOnce(1), clear g_dw_InitializationComplete\n   - Command 0x200: Enter critical section at g_BattleNetCriticalSection, compute connection state ((commandCode & 0xf0) != 0 ? 7 : 3), update g_dw_GameStateVar3, leave critical section\n   - Command 0x201: Set connection state ((commandCode & 0xf0) != 0 ? 10 : 6), MD5 hash 0x100 bytes of payload to g_dw_ProtocolStateFlags, call SetGlobalValue\n   - Command 0x202: Set connection state ((commandCode & 0xf0) != 0 ? 8 : 4)\n   - Command 0x203: Set connection state ((commandCode & 0xf0) != 0 ? 9 : 5)\n8. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\npMessageBuffer - Pointer to message buffer containing command DWORD at offset 0x0 and payload at offset 0x4. Buffer must be null-terminated.\nmessageSize - Total size of message buffer in bytes (must be >= 5)\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if command processed successfully, 0 if validation fails (invalid size, missing null terminator, or embedded nulls)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFlag bits extraction: (commandCode & 0xf0) determines connection state offset (adds 4 when flag bits set)\nMemory allocation: Only performed for initialization commands (0x0, 0x100, 0x102) to prepare RNG seed buffer\nCritical section: Command 0x200 uses g_BattleNetCriticalSection for thread-safe state updates\nHash operations: Command 0x100 processes 0xfe bytes, command 0x201 processes 0x100 bytes of payload data\nNull termination: Message must be explicitly null-terminated; embedded nulls in payload cause validation failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
