      "name": "ManageLoggingState",
      "signature": "int ManageLoggingState(int command, uint param)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Manages logging operations with thread synchronization using critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup structured exception handling (SEH) frame for guaranteed cleanup\n2. Enter critical section to synchronize logging access (g_GameCriticalSection)\n3. Test command parameter:\n   - If command == 1: Initialize logging buffer via InitializeLoggingBuffer, write header via WriteLogFile to szBnetLogFile, set return value to 1\n   - If command == 2: Write log entry data via WriteLogDataThunk with param data\n   - Otherwise: Skip logging operations\n4. Exit critical section to release synchronization lock\n5. Restore SEH frame pointer and return\n6. Return: 1 if command 1 was executed, 0 for command 2 or other values\n\nParameters:\ncommand (int): Logging operation command code (1=initialize logging, 2=write data entry)\nparam (uint): Data parameter for command 2 (write operation), unused for command 1\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 if command 1 (initialize) was executed; 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses Windows structured exception handling to guarantee critical section cleanup even if exception occurs\n- Protects access to g_pDefaultLoggingBuffer (logging buffer state) with critical section\n- Command 1 initializes buffer and writes header to szBnetLogFile\n- Command 2 appends data entry to log file\n- All other command values are silently ignored (no operation performed)",
