      "name": "ExecuteMultipleProcesses",
      "signature": "DWORD ExecuteMultipleProcesses(LPSTR pCommandLines, LPSTR pWorkingDirectory)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Executes multiple processes from a null-delimited string of command lines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize STARTUPINFOA structure with cb=0x44 (68 bytes)\n2. Load the first command pointer from EAX\n3. Check if first character is null terminator (empty command list)\n4. If null, return 1 (success) - all commands processed\n5. Loop for each command in the delimited string:\n   a. Zero-initialize STARTUPINFOA structure using ZeroMemory\n   b. Set STARTUPINFOA.cb field to 0x44 (68 bytes)\n   c. Call CreateProcessA with:\n      - lpApplicationName = NULL (command line parsing enabled)\n      - lpCommandLine = current command pointer\n      - dwCreationFlags = 0x20 (CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP)\n      - lpCurrentDirectory = working directory (from EBX parameter)\n      - lpStartupInfo = pointer to STARTUPINFOA\n      - lpProcessInformation = pointer to PROCESS_INFORMATION output\n   d. Test CreateProcessA return value (EAX)\n   e. If CreateProcessA returns 0 (failure), jump to failure_return_path\n   f. Close hThread handle via CloseHandle function pointer (stored in EBP)\n   g. Close hProcess handle via CloseHandle function pointer\n   h. Calculate current command length using strlen function\n   i. Advance pCurrentCommand by (length + 1) to point to next command\n   j. Load next command's first character\n   k. Check if it's null terminator - if not, loop back to step 5a\n6. On successful completion of all commands: return EAX=1\n7. On CreateProcessA failure: return EAX=0\n\nParameters:\n- pCommandLines: Pointer to null-delimited command line strings (each command is null-terminated,\n  entire block ends with additional null byte indicating end of all commands)\n- pWorkingDirectory: Working directory for all created processes, passed to CreateProcessA\n  as lpCurrentDirectory parameter\n\nReturns:\n- EAX=1: All processes were created successfully\n- EAX=0: CreateProcessA failed for at least one command\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses non-standard stack-based parameter passing with __stdcall calling convention\n- Each created process runs in a new process group (CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP flag 0x20)\n- CreateProcessA lpApplicationName parameter is NULL, allowing command line shell parsing\n- Process and thread handles are immediately closed after creation - no synchronization with process lifetime\n- Empty command list (first character is null) returns success (1)\n- Function pointers for CreateProcessA and CloseHandle are loaded from global variables\n  at 0x6ff39080 (CreateProcessA) and 0x6ff39174 (CloseHandle)",
