      "name": "DuplicateFileData",
      "signature": "void DuplicateFileData(HANDLE hSourceFile, void * pUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Duplicates file data from a source file to a new destination file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize file system state via InitializeFileOperations()\n2. If initialization fails (result == 0), skip all operations and return\n3. Get the size of the source file via GetFileSize()\n4. Allocate a memory buffer with size matching the source file (magic: 0x57a)\n5. Read entire source file contents into the allocated buffer via ReadFileData()\n6. If read operation fails (returns 0), jump to cleanup without writing\n7. Create/open destination file with CreateFileWrapper using flags: access=0x3, share=0x0, create=0x2, attributes=0x80, special=0x40000000\n8. If destination file creation fails (returns -1), skip write operation\n9. Write the entire buffer contents to destination file via WriteFileDataBuffer()\n10. Close the destination file handle via CloseFileHandle_Thunk()\n11. Free the allocated buffer via DeleteObjectTrampoline() (magic: 0x589)\n12. Close the source file handle via CloseFileHandle()\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- hSourceFile: Source file HANDLE to read data from (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n- pUnused: Unused parameter, never referenced (passed in EDX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if InitializeFileOperations() returns 0 (failure)\n- Skips write if ReadFileData() returns 0 (read failure)\n- Skips write if CreateFileWrapper() returns -1 (file creation failure)\n- Magic constants 0x57a and 0x589 appear to be module/zone identifiers passed to memory allocator\n- Destination file is created with specific flags indicating create-always behavior with attributes 0x80",
