      "name": "GetFileSizeIfRecent",
      "signature": "DWORD GetFileSizeIfRecent(FILETIME * pTargetTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Retrieves file size if modification time is within recent threshold.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create/open file with read-write access flags (dwDesiredAccess=3, dwCreationDisposition=3)\n2. Validate file handle against invalid marker (0xFFFFFFFF)\n3. Call GetFileTime to retrieve file's last modification time into stack-local FILETIME\n4. Calculate 64-bit time difference: timeDiff = fileModTime - pTargetTime\n5. Perform signed comparison: if timeDiff < 0 (file older than target), negate both parts\n6. Validate high 32-bits equals 0 (difference within 32-bit range)\n7. Compare low 32-bits against threshold 0x2625a00 (~10 seconds in 100ns units)\n8. If validation passes: call GetFileSize, close handle, return file size in EAX\n9. If any validation fails: close handle and return 0\n\nParameters:\n- pTargetTime: Pointer to FILETIME structure containing reference timestamp (dwLowDateTime at +0x0, dwHighDateTime at +0x4)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: File size in bytes if file handle valid and file modification time recent (within ~10 seconds)\n- 0: If CreateFileWrapper fails, file time validation fails, or file is older than threshold\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Time threshold constant: 0x2625a00 = 630000000 decimal = ~10 seconds in 100-nanosecond intervals\n- Invalid handle constant: 0xFFFFFFFF indicates CreateFileWrapper failure\n- 64-bit subtraction uses SBB (Subtract with Borrow) for proper carry chain across high/low parts\n- Two exit paths: success at 0x6ff2cf84 returns file size, error paths return 0\n- File handle closed on all paths to prevent resource leaks",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
