      "name": "WriteDataToFileWithTimestamp",
      "signature": "void WriteDataToFileWithTimestamp(void * pData, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes data to a file with timestamp information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push registers (ECX, ESI) and local variables to stack\n2. Prepare 5 parameters for CreateOrOpenFileHandle: (0, 0, 2, 0x80, 0)\n3. Load address 0x40000000 into EDX (file access flags)\n4. Call CreateOrOpenFileHandle to create or open a file and obtain handle\n5. Move returned handle to ESI and compare against -1 (INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)\n6. If handle is invalid (-1), jump to cleanup and return without writing\n7. Load pData pointer from ESP+0x10 into ECX\n8. Load dwSize size from ESP+0xc into EDX\n9. Prepare 3 parameters for WriteFileDataBuffer: (0, abFileTimeBuffer, dwSize)\n10. Load file handle from ESI into ECX and call WriteFileDataBuffer to write data\n11. Push pFileTime three times (FILETIME pointer for creation, access, and write times)\n12. Push file handle ESI as first parameter\n13. Call SetFileTime via function pointer at g_pSetFileTimeFunction to set timestamps\n14. Move file handle ESI to ECX and call CloseFileHandle_Thunk to close file\n15. Pop ESI and ECX registers, return with 8-byte __stdcall cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  pData (void *): Pointer to data buffer containing data to write to file\n  dwSize (uint): Size in bytes of the data buffer to write\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value, uses __stdcall with 8-byte callee cleanup)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If file handle creation fails (returns -1), function returns immediately without error\n  - Uses same FILETIME value for all three timestamp fields (creation, access, write)\n  - pFileTime register preserved across call (used for FILETIME pointer)\n  - File handle obtained from CreateOrOpenFileHandle is always closed before return",
