      "name": "InitializeMPQState",
      "signature": "void InitializeMPQState(uchar stateCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes MPQ processing state by clearing flags and storing a state code in protected memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock on g_CriticalSectionForExit to prevent concurrent access\n2. Clear byte at 0x6ff3f670 (first MPQ state flag)\n3. Clear byte at 0x6ff3f671 (second MPQ state flag)\n4. Load stateCode parameter from stack (offset +0x4 from ESP)\n5. Store stateCode value in DWORD at 0x6ff3f508 (state storage)\n6. Perform tail call to LeaveCriticalSection with critical section object on stack\n\nParameters:\n  stateCode (uchar): State code value to store (typically 0x65 for MPQ processing)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns via tail call to LeaveCriticalSection\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic value 0x65 indicates MPQ file processing state\n  - Critical section synchronization ensures atomic state update without race conditions\n  - Tail call optimization: LeaveCriticalSection return address replaces InitializeMPQState return\n  - Called only from DispatchNetworkFileOperation during MPQ protocol handling",
