      "name": "ProcessPatchFile",
      "signature": "int ProcessPatchFile(int * pResultCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes patch files for binary updates. Reads patch list from MPQ file, parses patch commands (delete, extract, execute), manages MD5 hashes for file verification, and orchestrates patch application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate parameter not null, exit with error if null\n2. Get executable directory path by finding last backslash in module path\n3. Load patch list from patch directory (szPatchDirectoryName) containing patch file names\n4. Iterate through each patch file name from the list:\n   a. Open patch file as MPQ archive\n   b. Read patch version from MPQ metadata\n   c. Validate version is 0 or >= 5, delete patch if invalid\n   d. Open data file within MPQ archive\n   e. Read all file data into memory buffer\n   f. Parse patch file line by line:\n      - Skip empty lines and line endings (CR/LF)\n      - Extract command and filename from each line\n      - Calculate MD5 hash of filename\n      - Build output file path using base directory + filename\n      - Process command: DELETE, EXTRACT, or EXECUTE\n      - For EXECUTE: calculate MD5 hash of output file and queue command\n   g. Close file and MPQ archive\n   h. Move to next patch file\n5. After all patches processed, dispatch final patch operations:\n   a. Copy launcher (Launcher) to destination\n   b. Copy game files (d2exp.mpq, d2data.mpq, d2sfx.mpq)\n   c. Copy patch file (patch_d2.mpq)\n   d. Add bnupdate.exe to execution queue\n6. Save engine state and unload before patching\n7. Execute all queued operations via external processes\n8. Return status: -1 for success, 2 for execution failure, 0 for patch load failure\n\nParameters:\n- pResultCode: Pointer to int receiving result code (-1=success, 0=patch_error, 2=exec_error)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: int status (0 or 1 for success/failure from perspective of caller)\n- Sets *pResultCode: -1 (success), 0 (patch load failed), 2 (patch execution failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pResultCode triggers assertion and exit with code -1\n- Invalid patch versions (not 0 and not >= 5) cause patch to be deleted\n- Malformed command lines are silently skipped\n- Empty patch list (no files) returns success with pResultCode=0\n- File read failures during patch processing cause early exit\n- MD5 verification is performed for both filenames and executable file data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
