      "name": "CreateNetworkOperationWithType0",
      "signature": "uint CreateNetworkOperationWithType0(uint * pOperationData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Creates a network operation entry with operation type 0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX register (fastcall implicit parameter)\n2. Move pOperationData pointer from EDX to EAX\n3. Push operation type 0 onto stack\n4. Call CreateNetworkOperationEntry(0, pOperationData)\n5. Set return value to 1 (success indicator)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pOperationData: uint* - Pointer to operation data structure to be queued\n\nReturns:\n- uint - Always returns 1 to indicate successful operation queueing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Operation Type: Hardcoded to 0, distinguishing this from CreateNetworkOperation1, etc.\n- This is a convenience wrapper for the most common network operation type (type 0)\n- Return value is constant and does not indicate actual operation success, only queueing success",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
