      "name": "ConvertHexCharToValue",
      "signature": "int ConvertHexCharToValue(char chHexChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts a hexadecimal character digit to its numeric value 0-15.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert input character to lowercase via _tolower to handle both 'A'-'F' and 'a'-'f'\n2. Compare lowercase result against 0x61 ('a') to distinguish letters from digits\n3. If character >= 'a' (letters 'a'-'f'): subtract 0x57 (87) to get 10-15\n4. If character < 'a' (digits '0'-'9'): subtract 0x30 (48) to get 0-9\n5. Return computed value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  hexChar (char) - Single hexadecimal character: '0'-'9', 'A'-'F', or 'a'-'f'\n\nReturns:\n  int - Numeric value 0-15 where:\n        0-9 for input '0'-'9'\n        10-15 for input 'a'-'f' or 'A'-'F'\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No input validation; assumes caller passes valid hex character\n  - Uses 0x61 ('a') as comparison threshold\n  - Subtraction values: 0x57 for letters, 0x30 for digits\n  - Case-insensitive via _tolower preprocessing",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
