      "name": "ConvertNibbleToHexChar",
      "signature": "char ConvertNibbleToHexChar(uint dwNibble)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts a 4-bit nibble value to its ASCII hexadecimal character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Mask input value to lower 4 bits (0x0-0xF range)\n2. Compare masked value to 10 (0xA) to determine digit type\n3. If value >= 10, add 0x37 to produce 'A'-'F' (ASCII 65-70)\n4. If value < 10, add 0x30 to produce '0'-'9' (ASCII 48-57)\n5. Return ASCII character code in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  dwNibble (uint) - Input nibble value in EAX, uses lower 4 bits only\n\nReturns:\n  char - ASCII hex digit: '0'-'9' or 'A'-'F'",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
