      "name": "ValidateAndDecodeHash",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndDecodeHash(ulong * pResultValue1, ulong * pResultValue2, ulong * pResultValue3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and decodes an MD5-based cryptographic hash structure extracting three components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize all output parameters to zero\n2. Validate hash data pointer (return 0 if null)\n3. Compute MD5 hash of 32-byte input data into md5Buffer\n4. Convert computed MD5 to hexadecimal string representation\n5. Calculate rolling checksum iterating first 16 MD5 bytes:\n   - Convert byte to lowercase via _tolower\n   - Compute offset value: -0x57 if char >= 'a', else -0x30\n   - Update checksum: EDI = EDI + (EDI*2 XOR offset)\n6. Validate checksum matches pResultValue3 low byte (EDI & 0xFF)\n7. If checksum fails, return 0 (validation failed)\n8. Shuffle hash bytes using calculated stride pattern (modulo 16)\n9. Transform shuffled bytes with magic constant 0x13ac9741:\n   - Convert to uppercase via _toupper\n   - For chars < '8': XOR with (magic & 0x7), shift magic >>3\n   - For chars '8' to 'A': XOR with (index & 0x1)\n10. Parse three segments from transformed hash using _strtoul (base 16)\n11. Store parsed values into output parameters\n12. Return 1 (validation successful)\n\nParameters:\n  pResultValue1: Pointer to receive first 32-bit parsed value\n  pResultValue2: Pointer to receive second 32-bit parsed value\n  pResultValue3: Pointer to receive third 32-bit parsed value\n\nReturns:\n  1 = Hash validation and decoding successful\n  0 = Hash validation failed (null pointer or checksum mismatch)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic constant 0x13ac9741 is reused as temporary storage during byte transformation\n  - Checksum uses only low byte (8-bit) comparison\n  - Hash shuffle operates on 16-byte hash with modulo indexing\n  - Three parsing segments have variable lengths: 3, 7, 9 bytes",
