      "name": "ExceptionCleanupAndExit",
      "signature": "void ExceptionCleanupAndExit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exception handler cleanup and process termination routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Display error message via WriteErrorMessage(0x0A=10 decimal) for SEH/exception notification\n2. Call FUN_6fba3179(0x16) to perform exception handler cleanup and resource deallocation\n   - 0x16 parameter indicates cleanup-specific handler variant\n   - Acquires/releases critical section locks as needed\n   - Deallocates exception-related thread-local state\n3. Call __exit(3) to terminate process with exit code 3\n   - Bypass normal cleanup (no atexit handlers)\n   - Indicates abnormal termination due to unhandled exception\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  No return - terminates process via __exit(3)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Always invoked from SetupStructuredExceptionHandler after exception dispatch\n  - Exit code 3 signals SEH/exception handler termination (vs. normal exit 0)\n  - WriteErrorMessage call indicates fatal error condition requiring user notification\n  - Used for both caught exceptions and cleanup-on-error paths\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0A (10) - Error code for WriteErrorMessage (generic exception/SEH error)\n  0x16 (22) - Parameter to FUN_6fba3179 triggering exception cleanup variant\n  3 - Exit code indicating exception-triggered abnormal termination\n\nRelated Functions:\n- SetupStructuredExceptionHandler() - Calls this function after exception dispatch\n- WriteErrorMessage() - Logs fatal error before exit\n- FUN_6fba3179() - Performs actual exception handler cleanup\n- __exit() - Windows API for process termination",
