      "name": "InitializeGlobalGameObject",
      "signature": "void InitializeGlobalGameObject(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes global game object and registers automatic cleanup handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push EDI register to stack for preservation (1 byte pushed)\n2. Load global game object address (0x6ff3f8e4) into EDI register\n3. Call AllocateAndInitializeStructure() to allocate memory and initialize global object fields\n4. Push DeleteGlobalObject function pointer (0x6ff38700) as parameter for atexit()\n5. Call _atexit() C runtime function to register cleanup handler\n6. Add 4 bytes to ESP to clean up stack (remove function parameter)\n7. Restore EDI register from stack\n8. Return to caller via RET instruction\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters; uses global state at 0x6ff3f8e4\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global game object stored at fixed address 0x6ff3f8e4 (g_pGlobalGameObject)\n- DeleteGlobalObject function is guaranteed to execute at program exit via _atexit()\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleans stack with RET 0)\n- EDI register preserved across function call per x86 calling convention\n- Typical initialization sequence: allocate resources, then register cleanup",
