      "name": "ValidateAndProcessDownloadPacket",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndProcessDownloadPacket(DownloadPacket * pPacket, uint dwPacketSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and processes a network download packet.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if packet size meets minimum requirement (0x11 bytes / 17 bytes)\n2. Extract magic value from packet offset +0x0 (first DWORD)\n3. Compare magic value with cached value at g_dwLastProcessedMagic to detect duplicates\n4. Return 1 immediately if packet too small or magic matches cached (duplicate packet)\n5. Calculate source path pointer at packet offset +0x10 (after 16-byte header)\n6. Scan source path string byte-by-byte to locate null terminator\n7. Calculate destination path pointer as location after source path null terminator\n8. Store current magic value to g_dwLastProcessedMagic cache for duplicate detection\n9. Validate that both source and destination paths are non-empty (not null strings)\n10. Call InitiateFileDownload with magic, param at +0x4, source path, and destination path\n11. Return 1 to indicate packet was processed\n\nParameters:\npPacket (DownloadPacket*): Pointer to network packet structure containing:\n  +0x0: magicValue (uint) - Unique identifier for this download request\n  +0x4: callbackParam (uint) - Custom parameter passed to download callback\n  +0x8: reserved (byte[8]) - Unused padding bytes\n  +0x10: sourcePath (char[]) - Null-terminated source file path\n  +0x10+len: destPath (char[]) - Null-terminated destination path after source\ndwPacketSize (uint): Total packet size in bytes, must be at least 0x11 (17 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 regardless of success or failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Packets smaller than 0x11 bytes are silently rejected\n- Magic value cache prevents reprocessing of duplicate download requests\n- Empty source or destination paths cause silent skip without calling InitiateFileDownload\n- Packet structure is variable-length due to null-terminated strings\n- Magic value must be unique per download request to be processed",
