      "name": "MultiplyAccumulate32",
      "signature": "uint MultiplyAccumulate32(uint elementCount, uint multiplier, uint * sourceArray, uint * destArray, uint carryIn)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Multiply-Accumulate 32-bit Elements for Multiprecision Arithmetic\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte offset from element count: offset = (elementCount - 1) * 4\n2. Initialize source and destination pointers to end of arrays using offset\n3. Enter loop to process all elements in reverse order (from end to start)\n4. For each element:\n   - Load 32-bit unsigned element from source array\n   - Multiply element by multiplier (produces 64-bit result in EDX:EAX)\n   - Add carry-in value to 64-bit product\n   - Store lower 32 bits to destination array\n   - Extract upper 32 bits as carry for next iteration\n   - Decrement both source and destination pointers by 4 bytes\n   - Decrement element count\n5. Repeat loop until all elements processed (elementCount reaches 0)\n6. Return final carry value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- elementCount (ECX): Number of 32-bit elements to process\n- multiplier (EDX): Value to multiply each element by\n- sourceArray (stack +0x14): Pointer to array of 32-bit unsigned values\n- destArray (stack +0x18): Pointer to array where results are stored\n- carryIn (stack +0x1c): Initial carry value (typically 0)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Final carry value (upper 32 bits from last multiplication)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Processes arrays in reverse order (high to low indices) to handle carries properly\n- Handles 64-bit intermediate values using MUL EDX, ADC EDX sequence\n- Returns carry-out for chaining multiple multiply-accumulate operations\n- Used in bigint multiplication where each array element represents part of a large number\n- __fastcall convention: first two parameters in ECX/EDX, remaining on stack, caller cleanup",
