      "name": "DecodeLookupTableBytes",
      "signature": "void DecodeLookupTableBytes(byte * pInputBuffer, byte * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes 26 input bytes using a lookup table, producing 52 output bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize firstOutputIndex to 0x21 and byteIndex to 0\n2. Enter loop (loop_start_decode):\n   a. Calculate first position: (firstOutputIndex + 0x7b5) mod 0x34\n   b. Calculate second position: (first position + 0x7b5) mod 0x34\n   c. Load input byte at [inputBuffer + byteIndex]\n   d. Lookup transformation value in g_LookupTableDecodeBytes table\n   e. Divide lookup value by 5: quotient stored at first position, remainder at second position\n   f. Increment byteIndex\n3. Compare byteIndex with 0x1a (26 iterations)\n4. Jump back to loop if carry flag set, otherwise continue\n5. Pop saved registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  inputBuffer (byte *) - 26-byte input buffer to decode\n  outputBuffer (byte *) - 52-byte output buffer for decoded values\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to outputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic constant 0x7b5 (1973 decimal) used for pseudo-random index calculation\n  - Magic constant 0x34 (52 decimal) is both modulus for index wrapping and output buffer size\n  - Each input byte generates exactly 2 output bytes via division by 5\n  - Lookup table g_LookupTableDecodeBytes at 0x6ff3a5d0 contains 260 bytes of transformation values\n  - Loop uses carry flag (JC) for iteration control based on CMP EDI, 0x1a\n\nStructure Layout:\nOutput buffer layout for single input byte:\n  outputBuffer[firstPosition] = lookupValue / 5\n  outputBuffer[secondPosition] = lookupValue % 5\n\nWhere positions are calculated as:\n  firstPosition = (firstOutputIndex + 0x7b5) % 0x34\n  secondPosition = (firstPosition + 0x7b5) % 0x34",
