      "name": "TransformDiagonalCoordinates",
      "signature": "void TransformDiagonalCoordinates(int * pCoordBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Transforms diagonal isometric coordinates using bit-level operations on packed arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize source position (sourcePosition) to 0 and destination stride (destStridePosition) to 2\n2. Enter main loop processing 6 destination positions per iteration\n3. For each destination position from (stride-2) to (stride+3):\n   a. Calculate source bit offset from sourcePosition (mod 32) and source array index (sourcePosition >> 5)\n   b. Calculate destination bit offset from stride variant (mod 32) and array index (3 - (stride >> 5))\n   c. Extract source bit using bit shift and mask (1 << sourceBitOffset)\n   d. Replace destination bit by clearing mask and setting new bit value\n   e. Increment sourcePosition by 0xB (11 positions)\n   f. Apply position wrapping: if sourcePosition > 0x77, subtract 0x6D; if still negative, subtract 0x62\n4. Increment destination stride by 6 and repeat until stride-2 >= 0x78\n5. Return with pCoordBuffer modified in place\n\nParameters:\n   pCoordBuffer : int * - Array of 4 DWORDs (indices 0-2 destination, 3 is source)\n\nReturns:\n   void - Modifies pCoordBuffer in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Processes exactly 120 positions (0x78) using wrapping arithmetic\n   - Source positions wrap using custom logic: positions > 0x77 subtract 0x6D or 0x62\n   - Each bit in source coordinate array maps to one bit in destination array\n   - Stride increments by 6 per loop iteration, processes 6 bits per iteration\n\nStructure Layout:\n   pCoordBuffer is an array of 4 DWORDs, each storing packed bits:\n   [0] = bits 96-127 (32 bits)\n   [1] = bits 64-95 (32 bits)\n   [2] = bits 32-63 (32 bits)\n   [3] = bits 0-31 source data (32 bits)",
