      "name": "ProcessCryptographicRound",
      "signature": "void ProcessCryptographicRound(uint * pDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Applies cryptographic round transformation using substitution-permutation network on 128-bit block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize roundCounter to 0x1d0 (464 total substitution-permutation rounds)\n2. Initialize currentNibble to 0x1d (29 nibbles to process per iteration)\n3. For each round iteration:\n   a. Extract 4-bit value from pDataBuffer using bit position calculations\n   b. If not first iteration (roundCounter < 0x1d0):\n      - Execute inner_loop: Process all 30 nibbles for substitution mixing\n      - For each nibble: Extract value, XOR with accumulated result, perform S-box lookup\n      - Lookup in g_szCryptographicSubstitutionTable at offset (roundCounter + XOR_result)\n   c. Execute second mixing loop: Repeat S-box operations for all nibbles\n   d. Extract final result byte from S-box lookup\n   e. Write 4-bit result back to pDataBuffer at calculated nibble position\n   f. Decrement roundCounter by 0x10 (advance to next round)\n4. Continue outer_loop while roundCounter >= 0 (16 total rounds)\n\nParameters:\n  pDataBuffer: uint* - Pointer to 16-byte block (4 dwords) to transform in-place\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies pDataBuffer in-place, returns nothing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  S-box table address: 0x6ff3a3f0 (256-byte lookup table with permutation values)\n  Processes data as little-endian: dword index = (3 - nibbleIndex/8)\n  Nibble extraction: uses ((nibbleIndex & 7) * 4) bit shift\n  Total operations: 30 nibbles * 16 rounds * 2 loops = 960 S-box lookups",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
