      "name": "DecodeAndExtractCoordinates",
      "signature": "void DecodeAndExtractCoordinates(byte * pEncodedData, uint * pX, uint * pY, uint16 * pResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes a 26-byte encoded string and extracts coordinate and state data through cryptographic transformations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (pEncodedData and pResult must be non-NULL)\n2. Decode lookup table bytes from the 26-byte encoded string into abDecodedBytes array\n3. Initialize accumulators (dwAccumulatorLow=0, dwAccumulatorHigh=0, dwReserved1=0, dwReserved2=0)\n4. Process decoded bytes in reverse order (52 down to 1):\n   - Call MultiplyAccumulate32(4, 5, accumulators, currentByte) for each byte\n5. Apply cryptographic round transformation via ProcessCryptographicRound\n6. Apply diagonal coordinate transformation via TransformDiagonalCoordinates\n7. Extract and store results:\n   - pX = dwAccumulatorLow >> 10 (top 22 bits)\n   - pY = ((dwAccumulatorLow & 0x3FF) << 16) | (dwAccumulatorHigh >> 16)\n   - pResult[0] = dwAccumulatorHigh (lower 16 bits as word)\n   - pResult[1] = dwReserved1\n   - pResult[3] = dwReserved2\n\nParameters:\n  pEncodedData (in): Pointer to 26-byte encoded data string\n  pX (out): Pointer to extracted X coordinate (uint)\n  pY (out): Pointer to extracted Y coordinate (uint)\n  pResult (out): Pointer to 6-word result array for additional decoded values\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to output pointers via dereferenced pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function exits silently if pEncodedData is NULL or pResult is NULL\n  - Cryptographic functions are called in specific order for correct decoding\n  - Bit field extraction uses magic values 0x3FF (10-bit mask) and 0xA (10-bit shift)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b33f42f78030aa6326679bc78608a1a3",
