      "name": "DownloadFileFromSocketThread",
      "signature": "uint DownloadFileFromSocketThread(FileDownloadRequest * pDownloadRequest)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Threaded function that downloads file data from a Battle.net socket connection\n\nThis function runs as a worker thread to handle downloading file data from a remote\nBattle.net server. It manages the complete lifecycle of socket communication including\nconnection establishment, authentication, data reception, and cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize variables and check RNG initialization status (g_dwRNGInitEnabled)\n2. Load BNet gateway configuration and server list into buffers\n3. Parse first hostname from server list using szServerListDelimiter\n4. Configure socket address structure with AF_INET (IPv4) and port 0x17e0 (6112)\n5. Enter retry loop (max 3 attempts) to create AF_INET TCP socket\n6. Attempt connection to server using connect() syscall\n7. If connection fails, handle retries or exit based on retry counter and cancel flag\n8. On successful connection, configure socket options (SO_KEEPALIVE, SO_RCVTIMEO=15000ms)\n9. Send protocol marker byte (0x02) to server\n10. Get download parameter block size from pDownloadRequest[0]\n11. Copy parameter block (282 words) to local buffer using DWORD loop\n12. Send parameter block to server via send()\n13. Receive 4-byte response header in loop until all bytes received\n14. Validate header size does not exceed 0xFF bytes (256 max)\n15. Allocate memory buffer of size headerDataSize using AllocateMemory()\n16. Receive remaining file data bytes in loop with error checking\n17. Check g_dwReceiveThreadCancelFlag for early termination request\n18. Determine transfer type from pDownloadRequest[0x22C] (offset 556 = type field)\n19. If transfer type is 2: check file modification timestamp via GetFileSizeIfRecent()\n20. For matching timestamps, skip transfer and set result=0x312\n21. For type 1 transfer: call ReceiveFileFromSocket() with socket and file buffer\n22. For type 2 transfer: call ReceiveFileDataFromSocket() with alternate parameters\n23. On transfer error, call HandleNetworkOperationDispatch() with response metadata\n24. Call DeleteObjectTrampoline() to deallocate file buffer with error code\n25. On connection failure after retries, exit retry loop\n26. Cleanup phase: close socket if valid, deallocate error buffer, deallocate file buffer\n27. Delete download request parameter object\n28. Special cleanup: if status=0x80000002 and progress<100%, enter critical section\n29. Reset gateway list data (g_GatewayListData=0), patch random data (g_byPatchRandomData=0)\n30. Set file receive progress to 100% (0x65), leave critical section\n31. Decrement active thread counter using InterlockedDecrement()\n32. Exit thread with status 0 using __endthreadex(0)\n\nParameters:\n- pDownloadRequest [FileDownloadRequest *] - Download request structure containing:\n  Offset 0x0: wParamBlockSize (param block size in bytes)\n  Offset 0x14: dwTimestamp (file modification time for type 2 transfers)\n  Offset 0x114: nDownloadMode (download mode flag, 0x80000002=retry, other=normal)\n  Offset 0x228: dwTransferType (1=ReceiveFileFromSocket, 2=ReceiveFileDataFromSocket)\n  Offset 0x22C: dwTransferType2 (alternate transfer type field)\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Always returns 0 (thread return value via __endthreadex)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic values: 0x17e0=port 6112 in host byte order, 0x3a98=15000ms timeout\n- Magic values: 0x80000002=retry mode flag, 0x100=max header size (255 bytes)\n- Transfer type 2 with matching timestamp skips transfer (result=0x312)\n- Retry counter limits reconnection attempts to maximum of 3\n- Cancel flag g_dwReceiveThreadCancelFlag allows early termination at any point\n- Progress threshold (g_dwFileReceiveProgress<100) triggers special cleanup section\n\nStructure Layout - FileDownloadRequest (offset 0x0):\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type     | Purpose\n0x000  | 2    | wParamBlockSize     | ushort   | Parameter block size in words\n0x014  | 4    | dwTimestamp         | DWORD    | File time for validation\n0x114  | 4    | dwDownloadMode      | DWORD    | Retry mode flag (0x80000002)\n0x228  | 4    | dwTransferType      | DWORD    | Primary transfer type selector\n0x22C  | 4    | dwTransferType2     | DWORD    | Secondary transfer type",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
