      "name": "CheckCryptoProviderAndCall",
      "signature": "uint CheckCryptoProviderAndCall(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if cryptographic provider is initialized and invokes external crypto function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load cryptographic provider initialization flag from global variable g_dwRNGInitEnabled at 0x6ff3f654\n2. Test if the flag value is non-zero to determine if crypto provider is initialized\n3. If initialized (flag != 0), preserve value in EAX register by pushing it onto stack\n4. Call external cryptographic provider function at 0x6ff2810e (ordinal 10262)\n5. If not initialized (flag == 0), skip the call and jump to provider_not_initialized label\n6. Return result from external crypto function if provider initialized, otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\n(None) - Function takes no explicit parameters, operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nuint - Result value from external crypto function if provider initialized\n       0 - If cryptographic provider is not initialized or unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global g_dwRNGInitEnabled at memory address 0x6ff3f654 stores provider initialization state\n- Function is referenced 42 times throughout codebase, all in cryptographic operations\n- External crypto function call passes control to ordinal 10262 routine\n- EAX register is preserved during call using PUSH/POP pattern",
