      "name": "ValidateAndDecodeCoordinates",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndDecodeCoordinates(byte * pEncodedData, uint16 * pResult, uint * pY, uint * pX)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates an encoded data pointer and orchestrates coordinate extraction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pEncodedData pointer is NULL\n2. Return 0 (failure) if pointer is invalid\n3. Call DecodeAndExtractCoordinates to decode and extract coordinate values\n4. Return 1 (success) after decoding completes\n\nParameters:\npEncodedData - Pointer to 26-byte encoded coordinate data string (must not be NULL)\npResult - Pointer to 6-element uint16 array for decoded intermediate values\npY - Pointer to uint for decoded Y coordinate output\npX - Pointer to uint for decoded X coordinate output\n\nReturns:\n0 - Validation failed (pEncodedData is NULL)\n1 - Validation and decoding successful\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return path for NULL pointer validation prevents crashes\n- Stack cleanup of 4 bytes (RET 0x4) compensates for one stack-passed parameter in __cdecl",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
