      "name": "ConvertBinaryDataToHexString",
      "signature": "void ConvertBinaryDataToHexString(byte * pBinaryData, uint * pOverflowFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts binary data to hexadecimal ASCII string representation with overflow tracking\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize overflow flags output to zero\n2. Set up iteration counter to 2 (process 16 bytes in 2 passes of 8 bytes each)\n3. Initialize overflow mask to 0x1 (will rotate left 4 bits per byte pair)\n4. For each of 4 byte pairs in current 8-byte chunk:\n   a. Load two consecutive bytes as indices into lookup table g_HexEncodingLookupTable\n   b. Combine values: (table[byte[0]] * 0x18) + table[byte[1]] using LEA instruction\n   c. Compare combined value to 0x100 (256)\n   d. If overflow (>= 0x100): subtract 0x100, set corresponding bit in overflow flags using mask\n   e. Extract high nibble: (combined >> 4) & 0xF\n   f. Convert high nibble to ASCII: add 0x30 if value < 10, else add 0x37 (0-9 or A-F)\n   g. Store ASCII high nibble at byte[index-1]\n   h. Extract low nibble: combined & 0xF\n   i. Convert low nibble to ASCII using same rules\n   j. Store ASCII low nibble at byte[index]\n   k. Rotate overflow mask left by 1 bit for next pair (SHL ESI, 1)\n5. After processing all 4 pairs (8 bytes): rotate mask left by 4 bits total, advance pointer by 8\n6. Decrement iteration counter and repeat until all 16 bytes converted\n\nParameters:\n- pBinaryData: pointer to 16-byte binary buffer (EAX register) - input and output buffer\n- pOverflowFlags: pointer to DWORD output buffer (EDI register) - receives overflow bits\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value in EAX)\n- Modifies pBinaryData in-place, converting each byte to two ASCII hex digits\n- Sets bits in *pOverflowFlags: bits 0-3 represent overflow for bytes 0-3, bits 4-7 for bytes 4-7, etc.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Lookup table g_HexEncodingLookupTable at 0x6ff3a6f0 contains 256-byte mapping table\n- Magic values: 0x100 (overflow threshold), 0x30 (ASCII '0'), 0x37 (ASCII 'A' - 10)\n- Overflow occurs when scaled byte pair sum exceeds 255 (0xFF)\n- Function assumes exactly 16-byte input buffer (2 iterations \u00d7 8 bytes)\n- Calling convention: __stdcall (parameters in ECX/EDX by convention, passed via registers)",
