      "name": "ProcessAndDecodeEncodedString",
      "signature": "uint ProcessAndDecodeEncodedString(void * pOutputBuffer, uint dwUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and decodes either a 16-byte hash string or a 26-byte coordinate string into a structured output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Obtain the length of the input string using strlen()\n2. If length == 0x10 (16 bytes): Process as encoded hash string\n   - Decode the hash string using ValidateAndDecodeHash()\n   - If validation succeeds, populate output structure and return 1\n   - Hash path calls ComputeSHA1Hash() to derive final hash at output+0x10\n3. If length == 0x1a (26 bytes): Process as coordinate string  \n   - Verify input string pointer is not NULL\n   - Decode X/Y coordinates using DecodeAndExtractCoordinates()\n   - Populate output structure with decoded coordinates and return 1\n   - Coordinate path calls SHA1_Final() to store hash at output+0x10\n4. For any other length, return 0 (failure/invalid format)\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer: Pointer to 0x28-byte output structure (caller allocates)\n  nUnused: Reserved parameter (passed by caller, not used)\n  [EDI implicit]: Pointer to null-terminated encoded input string\n\nReturns:\n  1 if string was successfully decoded and output populated\n  0 if string length is invalid or processing failed\n\nOutput Structure Layout (0x28 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    0x04  stringLength    Length of input string (16 or 26)\n  0x04    0x04  hashOrX         Hash low bits OR coordinate X\n  0x08    0x04  hashOrY         Hash high bits OR coordinate Y\n  0x0C    0x04  zeroPadding     Always zero (padding)\n  0x10    0x18  hashData        Final hash data (24 bytes for hash path, 26 for coords)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Input pointer can be NULL for coordinate case (returns 0)\n  - 16-byte hash path: Calls ComputeSHA1Hash() for hash derivation\n  - 26-byte coordinate path: Calls SHA1_Final() for SHA1 computation\n  - Output buffer offset +0x10 holds different data based on input type",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
