      "name": "ValidateAndProcessEncodedStrings",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndProcessEncodedStrings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Validates and processes encoded game configuration strings (hash or coordinate formats).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call LoadAndValidateGameConfigFiles() to initialize processing state\n2. Load first encoded data pointer from global g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate\n3. Calculate string length using strlen()\n4. Validate length: must be 0x10 (16 bytes) for hash or 0x1a (26 bytes) for coordinates\n5. If hash format (0x10), call ValidateAndDecodeHash() to validate and decode\n6. If coordinate format (0x1a), call DecodeAndExtractCoordinates() to process data\n7. Call indirect function at 0x6ff28126 to check secondary processing condition\n8. If secondary condition is true, repeat steps 2-6 for second buffer (g_pThirdConfigFileBuffer)\n9. Execute cleanup: free both allocated buffers (g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate, g_pSecondGridBufferTemplate) and nullify pointers\n10. Return processing result in EAX: 1 (0x1) for success, 0 (0x0) for validation failure\n\nParameters:\nNone (function uses global pointers)\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 if both encoded strings validated and decoded successfully, 0 if validation fails or memory errors occur\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x10: Hash format requires exactly 16-byte encoded string\nMagic number 0x1a: Coordinate format requires exactly 26-byte encoded string\nNull pointer validation: Both global data pointers checked before processing\nMemory cleanup: Always executes at cleanup_and_return, freeing both buffers regardless of success",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:84ac9117ccd6c827f700ba3588d6b346",
