      "name": "ValidatePatchVersionAndInitiateDownload",
      "signature": "uint ValidatePatchVersionAndInitiateDownload(uint * pPatchVersionData, int nPathOrHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates patch version code and initiates appropriate patch download or state management workflow.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract patch version code from pPatchVersionData[0] (valid range: 1-3, 0 or 4+ is invalid)\n2. Validate version range; if valid (1-3), call ValidateAndInitializePatchData to initialize patch data structures\n3. Call PatchFileDownloadStub with patch directory paths (szPatchPathPrefix, szPatchesDirectory) and magic value 0x82\n4. Branch on version code:\n   - Version 1 (requires_download): Acquire lock on g_CriticalSectionPatchData, generate random data via SMemRandom into pPatchVersionData[1], clear g_dwPatchInitializationFlag, release lock, initiate async download via InitiateFileDownload(handle=0x80000002, flags=2), set status message to szDownloadingUpgrade\n   - Version 2 (current_version): Set g_dwDownloadProgressFlag to 1, set status message to szUserHasLatestVersion\n   - Version 3 (requires_reinstall): Call InitializeGlobalStateOnce(1) to reset game state, set status message to szUserMustReinstallAndPatch\n   - Default (version_unknown): Call InitializeGlobalStateOnce(1), set status message to szUserHasUnknownVersion\n5. Clear g_dwDownloadProgressFlag to 0 before displaying final message\n6. Log final status message via LogFormattedDebugMessage with descriptive text indicating patch state\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npPatchVersionData (ECX): Pointer to patch version data structure. Offset +0 contains version code (1=needs_download, 2=current, 3=needs_reinstall). Offset +1 (byte) stores random initialization data generated during version 1 processing. Used to verify patch integrity.\npathOrHandle (EDX): File path or handle parameter passed to patch download functions. Adjusted by offset -4 for random data generation length calculation.\n\nReturns:\nuint: Always returns 1 indicating successful patch version validation and download initiation (does not indicate download completion, only that handling completed).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Version code range validation: Only 1-3 are valid versions; 0 and 4+ treated as invalid and trigger default error state\n- Critical section synchronization: Random data generation (version 1) is protected by g_CriticalSectionPatchData lock to prevent concurrent modification of game state\n- Magic constant 0x82: Appears to be patch file version or chunk size identifier used in download operations\n- Download handle 0x80000002: Special system handle used for async patch download operations via InitiateFileDownload\n- State reset: Versions 3 and default trigger InitializeGlobalStateOnce(1) to reset game state before reinstall/unknown scenarios\n- Flag management: g_dwDownloadProgressFlag is set during version 2 (no-op) and cleared before message display; g_dwPatchInitializationFlag is cleared during version 1 random data generation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
