      "name": "InitializeSHA1Context",
      "signature": "void InitializeSHA1Context(SHA1_CTX * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize SHA-1 hashing context with standard initial hash values\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize byte counters (h0 and h1 fields at offsets +0x0 and +0x4)\n2. Set h0 to SHA-1 initial value A: 0x67452301 (offset +0x8)\n3. Set h1 to SHA-1 initial value B: 0xEFCDAB89 (offset +0xC)\n4. Set h2 to SHA-1 initial value C: 0x98BADCFE (offset +0x10)\n5. Set h3 to SHA-1 initial value D: 0x10325476 (offset +0x14)\n6. Set h4 to SHA-1 initial value E: 0xC3D2E1F0 (offset +0x18)\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Pointer to SHA1_CTX structure passed in EAX register\n\nReturns:\n  void - Initializes the context structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic constants are the standard SHA-1 initialization vectors defined in RFC 3174\n  - First two fields (offsets +0x0, +0x4) are zeroed for byte counter initialization\n  - Context must be allocated by caller before calling this function\n  - Uses __fastcall convention with implicit EAX parameter\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type   | Description\n-------|------|---------------------|--------|----------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | bytesProcessedLow   | uint   | Low 32-bits of bytes processed (zeroed)\n+0x04  |  4   | bytesProcessedHigh  | uint   | High 32-bits of bytes processed (zeroed)\n+0x08  |  4   | h0                  | uint   | SHA-1 state A (0x67452301)\n+0x0C  |  4   | h1                  | uint   | SHA-1 state B (0xEFCDAB89)\n+0x10  |  4   | h2                  | uint   | SHA-1 state C (0x98BADCFE)\n+0x14  |  4   | h3                  | uint   | SHA-1 state D (0x10325476)\n+0x18  |  4   | h4                  | uint   | SHA-1 state E (0xC3D2E1F0)\nTotal: 28 bytes initialized",
