      "name": "UpdateSHA1Context",
      "signature": "void UpdateSHA1Context(SHA1_CTX * pContext, byte * pData, uint dwDataLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Updates SHA1 hash context with input data bytes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert byte count to bit count (multiply by 8)\n2. Add bits to low 32-bit counter with carry propagation to high counter\n3. Calculate current buffer offset: (bitCount_low >> 3) & 0x3F\n4. If partial block exists (offset > 0), fill remaining buffer to 64 bytes with input data\n5. If buffer becomes full, call SHA1Transform to process the block and reset offset\n6. While remaining input >= 64 bytes, process complete 64-byte blocks via SHA1Transform\n7. Copy any remaining bytes (< 64) into buffer for next update or finalization\n\nParameters:\npContext (EDI): Pointer to SHA1_CTX structure containing:\n  - bit counters (low/high 32-bit words for 64-bit total bit count)\n  - hash state (5 DWORDs for A,B,C,D,E hash values)\n  - buffer (64-byte input buffer)\npData (EAX): Pointer to input byte data to process\nnDataLength (Stack): Number of input bytes to process\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no explicit return; updates context in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Partial block handling: If buffer contains < 64 bytes, new data fills the buffer\n- Carry propagation: ADC instruction handles carry from low to high bit counter\n- Block alignment: Processes data in 64-byte SHA1 blocks only\n- Remaining bytes: Bytes not forming a complete block are copied to buffer\n- Bit precision: Maintains dual 32-bit counters for bit-level counting\n\nStructure Layout:\nSHA1_CTX at [EDI]:\nOffset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n0x00    0x4   bit_count_low   uint      Lower 32 bits of total input bits\n0x04    0x4   bit_count_high  uint      Upper 32 bits of total input bits\n0x08    0x14  hash_state      uint[5]   Hash values A,B,C,D,E (5 DWORDs)\n0x1C    0x40  buffer          byte[64]  Input buffer for block processing\nTotal:  0x5C",
