      "name": "SHA1_ProcessFinalBlock",
      "signature": "void SHA1_ProcessFinalBlock(SHA1_CTX * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Finalize SHA-1 message digest and produce 20-byte output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract message length from context (8 bytes total: 64-bit big-endian)\n2. Store length bytes on stack via bit-shifting (SHRD/SHR operations)\n3. Calculate padding block size: -(msgLen >> 3) - 9 AND 0x3F + 1\n4. Call SHA1_Update with padding block (variable length, 1-64 bytes)\n5. Call SHA1_Update with message length block (8 bytes constant)\n6. Load output pointer at context + 8 bytes\n7. Loop 5 iterations for each state DWORD (A, B, C, D, E):\n   - Load 32-bit value from context\n   - Convert to big-endian byte order via SHR shifts\n   - Write 4 bytes to output buffer in sequence\n   - Advance both pointers by 4 bytes\n   - Decrement counter and repeat\n8. Return via __stdcall (callee cleanup)\n\nParameters:\n- pContext: SHA1_CTX pointer containing message length and state\n\nReturns:\n- void (output written to context structure)\n\nStructure Layout (SHA1_CTX):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type   Description\n0       4     msgLen_Lo     uint   Message length bits (low 32)\n4       4     msgLen_Hi     uint   Message length bits (high 32)\n8       4     state_A       uint   SHA-1 state A\n12      4     state_B       uint   SHA-1 state B\n16      4     state_C       uint   SHA-1 state C\n20      4     state_D       uint   SHA-1 state D\n24      4     state_E       uint   SHA-1 state E\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0xFFFFFFF7: implements -(x >> 3) - 9 for padding calc\n- Output is 20 bytes (5 DWORDs in big-endian byte order)\n- SHRD instruction extracts byte atomically with shift\n- Big-endian conversion required for SHA-1 standard compliance",
