      "name": "ValidateAndInitializePatchData",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndInitializePatchData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes patch data for the patch/update system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x5e0 (1504) bytes on stack as temporary buffer\n2. Load size value (0x5dc) and call JumpTableEntry_AllocateMemory() \n3. Test allocation result - if NULL, return false\n4. At allocation success, load size into ECX register\n5. Push EDI register to preserve it across function call\n6. Push validation size parameter (0x5d = 93 bytes of patch metadata)\n7. Load buffer address (ESP+0xc) into EDI register\n8. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData() to validate and initialize patch data\n9. Clear ECX register for boolean conversion\n10. Test validation result in EAX register\n11. Set CL byte to 1 if result >= 0 (success), else 0 (failure)\n12. Move boolean result to EAX register and clean up stack\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses implicit local stack buffer and global allocator function\n\nReturns:\nbool - true (1) if patch data validated and initialized successfully, false (0) if memory allocation failed or validation returned negative value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack allocation is 0x5e0 (1504) bytes for temporary patch processing buffer\n- Validation size is 0x5d (93) bytes of patch metadata or header\n- Early return path at offset 0x6ff2b9cd if allocation fails\n- Validation path begins at offset 0x6ff2b9d4 on allocation success\n- EDI register is unaffected across function calls (preserved by PUSH/POP)\n- SETGE instruction converts signed comparison to boolean (>= 0 success)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:1ccce5b149e26631fdc6e0926b0b624b",
