      "name": "BNGatewayAccessAssignmentOperator",
      "signature": "BNGatewayAccess * BNGatewayAccessAssignmentOperator(BNGatewayAccess * this, BNGatewayAccess * pThis, BNGatewayAccess * pSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Assignment operator for BNGatewayAccess class. Copies all 36 bytes from source object to destination using efficient MOVSD.REP instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register (caller-saved general purpose register)\n2. Load source object pointer from stack parameter [ESP+8] into ESI\n3. Save EDI register (caller-saved general purpose register)\n4. Copy this pointer from ECX register into EAX and EDI\n5. Set counter to 9 to copy 9 consecutive 4-byte chunks\n6. Execute MOVSD.REP to bulk copy 36 bytes from source to destination\n7. Restore EDI register from stack\n8. Restore ESI register from stack\n9. Return this pointer in EAX with RET 0x4 (callee cleanup of 1 parameter)\n\nParameters:\npThis - IMPLICIT in ECX register, pointer to BNGatewayAccess destination object\npSource - Reference to source BNGatewayAccess object, passed at [ESP+8]\n\nReturns:\nEAX - Pointer to this object after assignment, enables chained assignments (a = b = c)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Copies exactly 36 bytes (9 DWORDs), assumes BNGatewayAccess structure is 36 bytes\n- Uses MOVSD.REP for maximum performance vs loop instruction\n- Thiscall calling convention with callee cleanup (RET 0x4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cd0285e9441f5e782995c62b7f40a547",
