      "name": "WriteFileWithTextModeConversion",
      "signature": "int WriteFileWithTextModeConversion(uint dwFileDescriptor, char * szBuffer, uint dwBytesToWrite)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes data to a file descriptor with text mode CRLF conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize canary value for stack overflow detection\n2. Return 0 if bytesToWrite is 0\n3. Locate file entry in global descriptor table using descriptor index\n4. Check EOF mode flag (0x20): seek to end of file if set\n5. Check binary mode flag (0x80):\n   a. If binary mode (flag clear): call WriteFile directly and return result\n   b. If text mode (flag set): convert LF to CRLF before writing\n6. Text mode conversion loop:\n   a. Initialize input position and conversion buffer\n   b. For each byte in input buffer:\n      - If byte is LF (0x0a): insert CR (0x0d) and increment newline count\n      - Store byte in conversion buffer\n   c. When buffer reaches 1024 bytes or input exhausted: call WriteFile\n   d. Verify all converted data was written\n   e. Continue until entire input buffer processed\n7. Handle WriteFile errors: map Windows error codes to DOS error numbers\n8. Final validation: check special flags and Ctrl-Z marker (0x1a)\n9. Return total bytes written minus newline count for text mode\n\nParameters:\n  fileDescriptor (ECX): Index into global file descriptor table\n  pBuffer (EDI): Pointer to data to write\n  bytesToWrite (ESP+0x3b4): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: On success, returns bytes written (excluding inserted CRs)\n       On error, returns -1 (0xffffffff)\n       Special case: returns bytes_written - newline_count for text mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Text mode: Each LF becomes CRLF, increasing byte count written by newline count\n  - File mode 0x80: Indicates text mode conversion needed\n  - File mode 0x20: Indicates EOF mode, triggers seek to end\n  - File mode 0x40: Special flag affecting final validation\n  - Error code 5: Mapped to special handling with errno 9 and 5\n  - Ctrl-Z (0x1a) with 0x40 flag: Suppresses error reporting\n  - Chunking: 1024-byte (0x400) conversion buffer for efficient processing\n\nStructure Layout:\nFile descriptor entry structure (36 bytes per entry):\n  Offset Size Field Name         Type        Description\n  +0x00   4    hFileHandle        HANDLE      Windows file handle\n  +0x04   1    dwFileMode         byte        File mode flags (0x20=EOF, 0x40=special, 0x80=text)\n  +0x05+  31   reserved           byte[31]    Reserved fields",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
