      "comment": "Flushes all open file streams and closes critical sections for high-index handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize structured exception handling frame and acquire global lock for thread safety\n2. Initialize processed file counter to 0 and set initial stream index to 3 (skip stdin/stdout/stderr)\n3. Loop through file pointer table from index 3 up to g_dwStreamTableSize:\n   a. Calculate byte offset as streamIndex * 4 to index into g_pStreamTableBase\n   b. Load FILE* pointer from table entry; skip if NULL\n   c. Test FILE._flag bits 0x83 (EOF | ERROR | WRITEABLE flags) for processing eligibility\n   d. If flags set, call CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked to flush the stream\n   e. If flush returns non-(-1), increment processed file counter\n   f. For indices greater than 20 (0x14):\n      - Delete critical section at FILE+0x20 offset to prevent deadlocks\n      - Free the FILE structure memory\n      - Clear the file pointer table entry to NULL\n   g. Increment index and loop back to loop_start_stream_index\n4. Exit loop after processing all indices; call final cleanup routine\n5. Return count of successfully processed files in EAX\n\nParameters:\n(void) - Function takes no parameters; operates on global file stream table\n\nReturns:\nint - Number of file streams successfully flushed (0 if none processed, incremented for each successful flush)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Standard I/O streams (indices 0-2) are skipped by starting loop at index 3\n- File handles at indices > 20 are unconditionally freed after flush attempt regardless of success\n- Critical sections protect concurrent access to FILE structures and must be deleted before freeing\n- Function uses structured exception handling (SEH) via __SEH_prolog/__SEH_epilog for safe cleanup\n- CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked returns -1 on flush failure; counter only incremented on success (EAX != -1)\n- If g_dwStreamTableSize is 0 or less than 3, loop exits immediately without processing\n- If g_pStreamTableBase is NULL, indexed access will cause access violation (assumed valid by caller)",
