      "name": "FlushFileAndCheckFlags",
      "signature": "int FlushFileAndCheckFlags(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes a file buffer and checks for special file flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __flush(pFile) to flush the file's output buffer to disk\n2. Test the flush result - if non-zero, the flush failed\n3. If flush fails, return -1 immediately to signal error\n4. If flush succeeds, test the 0x4000 flag bit in pFile->_flag field\n5. If the 0x4000 flag is not set, return 0 to indicate success\n6. If the 0x4000 flag is set, call FlushFileDescriptor(pFile->_file)\n7. Convert the descriptor check result: return -1 if check failed, else 0\n\nParameters:\n  pFile (FILE*): Pointer to the FILE stream structure to flush and check\n    - Contains _flag field at offset +0xd (byte) for status flags\n    - Contains _file field at offset +0x10 (dword) for the file descriptor\n\nReturns:\n  int: 0 if file flushed successfully and no special flags set\n       -1 if flush fails or descriptor check fails\n       Encodes boolean result via NEG/SBB: converts non-zero to 0xffffffff\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The 0x4000 flag indicates special file state requiring descriptor check\n  - NEG followed by SBB converts non-zero to 0xffffffff (-1), zero stays 0\n  - Called by FlushStreamsByMode in dual locations (0x6fbfe45c, 0x6fbfe477)\n  - Used in file stream management for error checking and synchronization",
