      "name": "ProcessSha1Block",
      "signature": "void ProcessSha1Block(uint * pHashState)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "SHA-1 Block Processing Function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load hash state (h0-h4) from pHashState[0-4] and 512-bit message block from pHashState[5-20]\n2. Byte-swap 16 32-bit message words from big-endian to little-endian format\n3. Expand message words W[16-79] using XOR and left rotate-by-1 expansion formula\n4. Initialize working variables A-E from current hash state values\n5. Execute Round 1 (iterations 0-19): F(B,C,D) = (B AND C) OR (NOT B AND D), constant 0x5a827999\n6. Execute Round 2 (iterations 20-39): F(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D, constant 0x6ed9eba1\n7. Execute Round 3 (iterations 40-59): F(B,C,D) = (B AND C) OR (B AND D) OR (C AND D), constant 0x8f1bbcdc\n8. Execute Round 4 (iterations 60-79): F(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D, constant 0xca62c1d6\n9. In each iteration: temp = (A<<5 | A>>27) + F(B,C,D) + E + constant + W[i]\n10. Rotate state: E=D, D=C, C=(B<<30|B>>2), B=A, A=temp\n11. Add final hash state values back to original pHashState array\n\nParameters:\n- pHashState: Pointer to hash state array containing 21 DWORDS\n  [0] = h0 (hash digest word 0)\n  [1] = h1 (hash digest word 1)\n  [2] = h2 (hash digest word 2)\n  [3] = h3 (hash digest word 3)\n  [4] = h4 (hash digest word 4)\n  [5-20] = 16 DWORD message block (512 bits in big-endian format)\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies pHashState in-place with updated hash state values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message bytes must be in big-endian format; little-endian systems require byte-swapping\n- Rotate-left operations: (value << N) | (value >> (32-N))\n- Constants are official FIPS 180-1 SHA-1 round constants\n- No input validation; caller must provide valid 512-bit block\n\nStructure Layout:\nHash State and Message Block (21 DWORDS):\nOffset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n0x0     4     h0           uint      Hash state word 0\n0x4     4     h1           uint      Hash state word 1\n0x8     4     h2           uint      Hash state word 2\n0xc     4     h3           uint      Hash state word 3\n0x10    4     h4           uint      Hash state word 4\n0x14    64    msg_block    uint[16]  512-bit message block (16 DWORDs)",
