      "signature": "void Sha1_Finalize(SHA1_CTX * pSha1Context, void * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Finalizes SHA1 hash computation and extracts the 20-byte message digest.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Extract 8 bytes from SHA1 context hash state words at offsets 0x18 and 0x14 via bit shifting\\n2. Call Sha1_UpdateBuffer with message block marker byte (0x80) to mark message end\\n3. While padding bit count [pSha1Context+0x14] masked by 0x1f8 does not equal 0x1c0 (448 bits for 512-bit blocks), repeatedly call Sha1_UpdateBuffer with padding byte (0x00) to reach exactly 448 bits\\n4. Call Sha1_UpdateBuffer with the 8-byte buffer containing extracted hash state bytes to update final block\\n5. Loop through 20 hash bytes: calculate shift amount as (3 - (byteIndex & 3)) * 8 to extract each byte in correct endian order from [pSha1Context + (byteIndex >> 2) * 4] using bit shifting\\n6. Store each extracted byte to pOutputBuffer[byteIndex]\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pSha1Context: Pointer to SHA1_CTX structure containing hash state words and bit count register\\n  - [offset+0x14]: Bit count register (32-bit) with bits 3-8 tracking padding state\\n  - [offset+0x18]: First hash state word (32-bit)\\n  - [offset+0x1c], [offset+0x20], [offset+0x24]: Additional hash state words for byte extraction\\n- pOutputBuffer: Pointer to 20-byte output buffer for final message digest\\n\\nReturns:\\n- void: Hash digest bytes extracted and written to pOutputBuffer\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Padding validation ensures exactly 448 bits (56 bytes) of padding before final 512-bit block\\n- Byte extraction uses little-endian style extraction with (3 - (index & 3)) shift calculation\\n- Loop counter uses carry flag (JC) for unsigned 32-bit comparison to detect when byteIndex reaches 0x14 (20)\\n- Each byte is extracted from a 32-bit word using calculated bit shift\\n- Message termination marked by 0x80 byte (MSB set) followed by zero padding bytes",
