      "name": "ProcessObjectDataWithTempCopy",
      "signature": "void ProcessObjectDataWithTempCopy(ObjectData * pDestination, ObjectData * pSource, ObjectData * pTemplate)",
      "calling_convention": "__d2call",
      "comment": "Creates a temporary object, initializes it from a template, processes data between source and destination objects using the temporary copy as an intermediate buffer, then destroys the temporary object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate temporary ObjectData structure on stack (PUSH ECX creates 4-byte slot)\n2. Get address of temporary object on stack (LEA EAX, [ESP])\n3. Call ResolveImportedFunction_Ordinal624 to initialize temporary buffer\n4. Load pTemplate parameter from stack offset +0x10 into ECX\n5. Load temporary object pointer from [ESP] into EDX\n6. Call InitializeObjectWithValue to initialize temporary object with template data\n7. Load temporary object pointer from [ESP] into EAX\n8. Load pSource parameter from stack offset +0xc into ECX\n9. Load pDestination parameter from stack offset +0x8 into EDX\n10. Call ProcessOrCopyObjectData to process data from source to destination via temporary\n11. Load temporary object pointer and call DestroyObject to release resources\n12. Restore stack with POP ECX and return to caller, cleaning 12 bytes from stack\n\nParameters:\nEBX (implicit) - pDestination (ObjectData *) - Target object to receive processed data\nStack +0x4 - pSource (ObjectData *) - Source object to read data from\nStack +0x8 - pTemplate (ObjectData *) - Template object used for initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Temporary object is allocated on stack with PUSH ECX (4-byte allocation)\n- Uses __d2call calling convention: implicit parameter in EBX, others on stack\n- Function callee cleans 12 bytes from stack (RET 0xc)\n- Acts as a safe wrapper ensuring temporary object cleanup via exception-safe pattern\n- Used for transforming object data safely without corrupting source or destination\n\nObjectData Structure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type      | Description\n-------|------|-------------|-----------|----------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | status      | UINT      | Object status/type identifier\n+0x04  |  4   | pObject1    | pointer   | First object pointer reference\n+0x08  |  4   | pObject2    | pointer   | Second object pointer reference\nTotal: 12 bytes (0xc)",
