      "name": "VerifyMD5HashWithBuffers",
      "signature": "bool VerifyMD5HashWithBuffers(uint * pBuffer1, uint * pBuffer2, uint * pBuffer3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Verifies cryptographic integrity using MD5 hashing with triple-buffer validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute MD5 hash of input data (from EAX) and store at context offset +0x40\n2. Copy 32 bytes from pBuffer1 to context base (offset +0x0 to +0x1F)\n3. Copy 32 bytes from pBuffer2 to context offset +0x20 (offset +0x20 to +0x3F)\n4. Copy 32 bytes from pBuffer3 to context offset +0x60 (offset +0x60 to +0x7F)\n5. Call ordinal 624 import function (initialization/setup)\n6. Import object data from pBuffer1 and pBuffer3 (32 bytes)\n7. Call ordinal 624 import function again (second phase)\n8. Initialize pBuffer3 object with value 0\n9. Compare object size between pBuffer1 and pBuffer3\n10. Destroy temporary objects pBuffer3 and pBuffer1\n11. Return true if comparison result equals 1, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EBX: ebx_contextPtr - Pointer to crypto context structure (128+ bytes)\nIMPLICIT EAX: eax_hashInputPtr - Pointer to input data for MD5 hashing\npBuffer1 - Pointer to first 32-byte verification buffer\npBuffer2 - Pointer to second 32-byte verification buffer\npBuffer3 - Pointer to third 32-byte verification buffer\n\nReturns:\ntrue (1) if MD5 verification succeeds and object sizes match\nfalse (0) if verification fails or size comparison != 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic value 0x7FFFFFFF used as hash length parameter (maximum signed int)\nMagic value 0x20 (32 bytes) used for object data import size\nComparison result must equal exactly 1 for success\nContext structure uses EBX register (non-standard calling convention)\n\nStructure Layout - Crypto Context (EBX):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n------  ----  ---------------  ------  -----------\n+0x00   32    buffer1Copy      uint[8] First verification buffer copy\n+0x20   32    buffer2Copy      uint[8] Second verification buffer copy\n+0x40   ?     md5HashOutput    byte[]  MD5 hash result storage\n+0x60   32    buffer3Copy      uint[8] Third verification buffer copy\n------  ----\nTotal:  128+  bytes (minimum)",
