      "name": "ExportObjectDataPair",
      "signature": "uint ExportObjectDataPair(uint * pOutputSize1, uint * pOutputSize2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Serializes two objects from an ObjectData structure to separate buffers with size tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load ObjectData pointer from ESI register (implicit parameter)\n2. Check if status field at offset +0x0 is valid (non-zero)\n3. If status is zero, return failure code (0)\n4. Call ExportObjectData to serialize first object from offset +0x4 to EDI buffer\n5. Track bytes written for first object export in local variable\n6. Zero-fill any unused space in first buffer if export size < 32 bytes\n7. Store actual bytes written to first output parameter (pOutputSize1)\n8. Call ExportObjectData to serialize second object from offset +0x8 to EBX buffer\n9. Track bytes written for second object export in local variable\n10. Zero-fill any unused space in second buffer if export size < 32 bytes\n11. Store actual bytes written to second output parameter (pOutputSize2)\n12. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI - Pointer to ObjectData structure (offset +0x0 status, +0x4 pObject1, +0x8 pObject2)\nIMPLICIT EDI - Destination buffer for first object export (32 bytes fixed size)\nIMPLICIT EBX - Destination buffer for second object export (32 bytes fixed size)\npOutputSize1 - Pointer to uint receiving actual bytes written for first export\npOutputSize2 - Pointer to uint receiving actual bytes written for second export\n\nReturns:\n0 - ObjectData status field is zero (invalid or uninitialized)\n1 - Successfully exported both objects with sizes written to output parameters",
