      "name": "MarshalParametersForOrdinal628",
      "signature": "void MarshalParametersForOrdinal628(void * pStructA, void * pStructB, void * pStackParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Marshals parameters from mixed calling convention to standard calling convention for external ordinal 628.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load dword from pStructA at offset +0x8 via EAX register\\n2. Load dword from pStructB at offset +0x0 via EDX register\\n3. Load dword from pStructA at offset +0x4 via EAX register\\n4. Load pStackParam from stack at [ESP+0x8]\\n5. Load dword from pStackParam at offset +0x0\\n6. Push all four extracted dwords onto stack in reverse order\\n7. Call external ordinal 628 handler via thunk at 0x6ff286fe\\n8. Return with stack cleanup of 0x4 bytes (one parameter)\\n\\nParameters:\\npStructA - Implicit in EAX: Pointer to structure with fields at offsets +0x4 and +0x8\\npStructB - Implicit in EDX: Pointer to structure with field at offset +0x0\\npStackParam - Explicit stack parameter at [ESP+0x8]: Pointer to structure with field at offset +0x0\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Return value from external ordinal 628 returned in EAX to caller\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nNon-standard calling convention: First two parameters passed implicitly in EAX and EDX registers,\\nthird parameter on stack. Parameter extraction order: Stack param field first, then pStructA fields,\\nthen pStructB field. Stack cleanup (RET 0x4) indicates one 4-byte parameter cleaned by callee.",
