      "name": "ValidateAndCompareStringPairs",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndCompareStringPairs(char * szSourceStr, char * szPatternStr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates and compares two strings by copying them to a combined stack buffer and running cryptographic validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSourceStr is non-NULL and non-empty, else return false\n2. Validate pPatternStr is non-NULL and non-empty, else return false\n3. Get length of pSourceStr using strlen(), verify length + 1 <= 256 bytes\n4. Copy pSourceStr to stack buffer using optimized DWORD copies for speed\n5. Get length of pPatternStr using strlen(), verify length + 1 <= 256 bytes\n6. Copy pPatternStr to stack buffer at offset (pSourceStr length)\n7. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData with combined buffer and magic 0x5a\n8. Return true if validation result >= 0 (success), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npSourceStr: char* - Pointer to source string (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\npPatternStr: char* - Pointer to pattern string (passed in EDX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if string validation succeeds, false if validation fails or strings are invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Both strings must be non-NULL and non-empty\n- Each string must fit in 256 bytes including null terminator\n- Combined buffer allocated on stack: 512 bytes (0x200)\n- String validation function called with magic number 0x5a (90 decimal)\n- Assertion failure (line 0x5a6-0x5b9) indicates invalid parameters\n- Calls _exit(-1) on buffer overflow or invalid parameters",
