      "name": "ValidateBufferAndGenerateRandomData",
      "signature": "bool ValidateBufferAndGenerateRandomData(LPCSTR pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates buffer constraints and generates cryptographic random data for network gateway operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if buffer pointer (ECX) is null - if null, trigger assertion at line 0x58d\n2. Call strlen() to calculate buffer length from input buffer\n3. Increment length by 1 to account for null terminator\n4. Compare (length + 1) against maximum 0x100 (256 bytes) constraint\n5. If length check passes, jump to random data generation at offset 0x6ff2bc5b\n6. If length check fails or buffer null, call GetLineNumberForAssertion() to obtain decorated line number\n7. Push source file path string pointer (g_szObfuscatedVerificationData) and line number\n8. Call AssertFailed() to report assertion with file and line information\n9. Call _exit(-1) to terminate process with error code -1\n10. Generate cryptographic random data by calling GenerateCryptographicRandomData() with magic seed 0x59\n11. Check if result >= 0 using TEST and SETGE instructions\n12. Return bool: true if random generation succeeded, false if failed\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer (LPCSTR): Pointer to buffer that will receive cryptographic random data.\n                    Must be non-null and have length <= 255 bytes (0x100 - 1).\n\nReturns:\n  bool: true if GenerateCryptographicRandomData() returned value >= 0 (success)\n        false if GenerateCryptographicRandomData() returned value < 0 (failure)\n        Function may not return if assertion triggered (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null buffer pointer: triggers assertion at line 0x58d (decimal 1421)\n  - Buffer length > 255: triggers assertion at line 0x593 (decimal 1427)\n  - Assertion failure: calls _exit(-1) for immediate process termination\n  - Magic constant 0x59 (89 decimal): seed value passed to random generator\n  - Uses __fastcall convention: buffer pointer in ECX, returns result in EAX as bool",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:bf36b697ce337671c87a88ebd8749cff",
