      "name": "ValidateAndHashObjects",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndHashObjects(LPCSTR pBaseData, uint nItemCount, int nOffsetDelta, void * * ppItemArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates multiple data items and computes composite MD5 hash for cryptographic verification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate string length of pBaseData\n2. If nItemCount > 0, validate all item array pointers (call strlen on both offset-adjusted and direct pointers)\n3. Allocate 0x4F4 byte hash context buffer\n4. Initialize hash header with count=1 and nItemCount value\n5. Hash base data string into buffer starting at offset +8\n6. If nItemCount > 0, hash each item from first array (offset-adjusted via nOffsetDelta)\n7. If nItemCount > 0, hash each item from second array (direct ppItemArray pointers)\n8. Clear global flags at 0x6ff3edf4 and 0x6ff3ef74 before finalization\n9. Execute finalization computation with hash size parameter (0x27)\n10. Convert result to bool (return true if >= 0) and free hash buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pBaseData (ECX): LPCSTR - Base data string to hash first\n- nItemCount (EDX): uint - Number of items in both arrays\n- nOffsetDelta (Stack +4): int - Offset difference between array bases\n- ppItemArray (Stack +8): void ** - First array pointer, second at +nOffsetDelta\n\nReturns:\n- bool: true if finalization succeeded (result >= 0), false otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty arrays (nItemCount==0): validation and item hashing loops skipped\n- Fixed buffer: always allocates 0x4F4 (1268) bytes for hash context\n- Dual arrays: uses nOffsetDelta offset to access alternate array base\n- Global state: clears g_dwHashContextFlag1 and g_dwHashContextFlag2 before finalization",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:578c54d6ec6302c57916ac88630d614d",
