      "name": "ComputeMD5HashValue",
      "signature": "uint ComputeMD5HashValue(char * pInputString, int nRandomDataMode, int nAdditionalParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes MD5 hash of input string with optional random data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 264-byte hash buffer by clearing with REP STOSD (0x41 dwords)\n2. Check if input string is NULL or empty\n3. If invalid input, use default \"Diablo II\" identifier and set hashFlags=1\n4. Call MD5Init to prepare hash context for computation\n5. Check system flags and conditionally set flag 0x4 based on nAdditionalParam\n6. If valid input, set hashFlags with flag 0x2 if random data mode is enabled\n7. Call MD5HashData to compute hash with 0x100-byte length limit\n8. Scan hash buffer to locate null terminator and calculate string length\n9. Add 5 bytes to computed length for padding calculation\n10. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData with padded length and randomness seed\n11. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\n- pInputString: Input string to hash; NULL or empty uses default identifier\n- bUseRandomData: Boolean flag enabling random data appending mode\n- nAdditionalParam: Parameter affecting flag computation in system check\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Always returns 1 indicating successful computation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
