      "name": "InitializeRandomNumberGenerator",
      "signature": "int InitializeRandomNumberGenerator(void * pSeed, uint dwSeedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize random number generator with seed data in thread-safe manner.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access to shared RNG state\n2. Call SMemRandom with seed buffer pointer and size to initialize RNG\n3. Clear global verification flag DAT_6ff3f508 to 0\n4. Leave critical section to release lock\n5. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nParameters:\npSeed (void*) - Pointer to seed data buffer used to initialize random number generator\ndwSeedSize (uint) - Size in bytes of the seed data buffer\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses critical section DAT_6ff3f8e8 to protect RNG state from concurrent access\n- Called with seed address DAT_6ff3b010 and size parameter 2 from InitializeVerificationSystem\n- The verification flag DAT_6ff3f508 is set to 0x66 before this call and cleared here\n- Part of security verification initialization sequence",
