      "name": "InitiateFileDownload",
      "signature": "void InitiateFileDownload(void * pCallbackContext, uint dwOptions, uint dwCallbackParam1, uint dwCallbackParam2, char * szSourcePath, char * szDestinationPath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initiates an asynchronous file download with caching and validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that source path is non-null and non-empty\n2. Use default destination path (0x6ff3a813) if parameter is null\n3. Read source file metadata and modification time via LoadCacheFileFromDisk\n4. Compare cached file time with source file time using CompareFileTime\n5. If timestamps match and WRITE_CACHE flag (0x2) is set, write cached data to destination\n6. Call HandleNetworkOperationDispatch to process download with path hashes\n7. Free cached buffer on success/error path\n8. If timestamps differ, allocate FileDownloadRequest structure (0x230 bytes)\n9. Initialize structure with magic values (0x49583836, 0x44324456) for validation\n10. Calculate source path length and store in size field (length + 0x21 base)\n11. Generate MD5 hashes for both source and destination paths\n12. Increment global download counter (g_dwFileDownloadThreadRunning)\n13. Spawn worker thread (DownloadFileFromSocketThread) with fire-and-forget pattern\n14. Close thread handle immediately after spawn\n\nParameters:\npCallbackContext (void*): User-supplied context pointer passed to callbacks\ndwOptions (uint): Option flags - bit 1 (0x2) enables WRITE_CACHE behavior\nnCallbackParam1 (uint): First parameter passed to callback function\nnCallbackParam2 (uint): Second parameter passed to callback function\npSourcePath (char*): Null-terminated source file path to download (must not be null)\npDestinationPath (char*): Null-terminated destination path for hash calculation, or null for default\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function provides no return value; side effects include thread creation and file operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Default destination path (0x6ff3a813) used when pDestinationPath is null\n- WRITE_CACHE flag (0x2) only takes effect if timestamps match\n- FileDownloadRequest must be exactly 0x230 bytes for worker thread compatibility\n- Magic values 0x49583836 and 0x44324456 validate structure format in worker thread\n- Source path length calculation uses null-terminator scan (strlen+1 pattern)\n- MD5 hashes placed at fixed offsets (0x20 and 0x124) within structure\n- Global counter at 0x6ff3f66c incremented atomically before thread spawn\n- Thread handle is closed immediately (fire-and-forget pattern, worker owns structure)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type         Description\n0x0     2     wDataSize            word         Source path length + 0x21 (base offset)\n0x2     1     bReserved            byte         Unused, set to 0\n0x3     1     bFlags               byte         Flags, set to 0x1\n0x4     4     dwMagic1             dword        0x49583836 (validation magic)\n0x8     4     dwMagic2             dword        0x44324456 (validation magic)\n0xc     4     nParam1              dword        Callback parameter 1\n0x10    4     nParam2              dword        Callback parameter 2\n0x18    4     dwFileTimeLow        dword        FILETIME.dwLowDateTime\n0x1c    4     dwFileTimeHigh       dword        FILETIME.dwHighDateTime\n0x20    256   szSourcePathHash     char[256]    MD5 hash of source path\n0x120   256   szDestPathHash       char[256]    MD5 hash of destination path\n0x220   4     dwOptions            dword        Option flags from dwOptions parameter\n0x224   4     pCallback            void*        Callback context pointer\nTotal: 0x230 bytes",
