      "name": "InitializeAndStartFileDownload",
      "signature": "uintptr_t InitializeAndStartFileDownload(char * szPatchPath, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes patches and starts a file download thread\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify that required imported ordinals are available\n2. Initialize patch seed data using SMemRandom and synchronized access\n3. Patch the file download stub entry point with parameters\n4. Validate patch path parameter is not NULL or empty string\n5. Load existing cache file from disk and retrieve file timestamps\n6. Compare file modification times to determine if update is needed\n7. If file exists (uVar2 != 0), write file data and dispatch network operation\n8. If timestamps don't match (LVar3 == 0), clean up and return 0\n9. Allocate 560-byte download request structure (0x230 bytes)\n10. Zero-initialize structure using REP STOSD (0x8c dwords = 0x230 bytes)\n11. Calculate patch path length (strlen(patchPath) + 0x21)\n12. Store calculated path length at offset +0x00\n13. Set magic signature \"IX86\" (0x49583836) and version signatures\n14. Set D2DV signature (0x44324456) in version fields\n15. Store FILETIME values at structure offsets +0x18 (low) and +0x1c (high)\n16. Compute MD5 hash of patch path string, store at offset +0x20\n17. Compute MD5 hash of global assertion data, store at offset +0x124\n18. Increment thread counter (InterlockedIncrement)\n19. Create worker thread using __beginthreadex with DownloadFileFromSocketThread\n20. Return thread handle (HANDLE) or 0 on validation/allocation failure\n\nParameters:\n- patchPath (ECX): Pointer to patch directory path string, cannot be NULL\n- flags (EDX): Additional initialization flags (passed to SMemRandom)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Thread handle (HANDLE) from __beginthreadex, or 0 on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL or empty patch path immediately returns 0\n- Failed LoadCacheFileFromDisk returns 0\n- Memory allocation failure (pDownloadStruct == NULL) returns 0\n- CompareFileTime == 0 means timestamps match, proceed with update\n- Structure is 560 bytes (0x230) with specific binary format for download protocol\n- Magic values appear to encode protocol version: \"IX86\" (x86) + \"D2DV\" (Diablo II DV)\n- FILETIME fields store 64-bit Windows file timestamps\n- MD5 hashes at offsets +0x20 and +0x124 are 256-byte regions each\n\nStructure Layout (DownloadRequest at pDownloadStruct):\nOffset Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n0x00   2     pathLength              word        Calculated path length + 0x21\n0x02   1     reserved1               byte        Always 0\n0x03   1     version                 byte        Always 1\n0x04   4     magicSignature          dword       0x49583836 (\"IX86\")\n0x08   4     versionSignature        dword       0x44324456 (\"D2DV\")\n0x0c   8     reserved2               dword[2]    Always 0\n0x14   4     reserved3               dword       Always 0\n0x18   4     fileTimeLow             dword       File timestamp low dword\n0x1c   4     fileTimeHigh            dword       File timestamp high dword\n0x20   0x104 pathMD5Hash             byte[260]   MD5 hash of patchPath string\n0x124  0x104 dataMD5Hash             byte[260]   MD5 hash of global assertion data\n0x228  4     flags                   dword       0x80000002 (protocol flags)\n0x22c  4     reserved5               dword       Always 2\nTotal: 0x230 (560 bytes)",
