      "name": "GetSystemModeValue",
      "signature": "uint GetSystemModeValue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns the system mode value based on initialization state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system is NOT initialized (g_dwCancellationFlag == 0)\n2. If not initialized, check download mode (g_dwDownloadMode):\n   - If mode == 0: Load and return value from g_ValidationState1 (0x6ff3ee40)\n   - If mode == 1: Load and return value from g_InitializationState1 (0x6ff3eea8)\n   - Otherwise: Return 0\n3. If system IS initialized, enter critical section\n4. Load current mode value from g_dwConnectionState (0x6ff3f1f4)\n5. If mode value is zero, initialize it to 0x12 (18 decimal - default mode)\n6. Leave critical section\n7. Return 0 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Mode value or status code\n  - When not initialized with downloadMode==0: Returns g_ValidationState1\n  - When not initialized with downloadMode==1: Returns g_InitializationState1\n  - When initialized: Returns 0 (success indicator)\n  - Otherwise: Returns 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x12 (18): Default mode value assigned during initialization\nCritical section g_BattleNetCriticalSection: Ensures thread-safe access to g_dwConnectionState\nDownload modes: Valid values are 0 and 1 during pre-initialization state\nFunction pointer tables: EnterCriticalSection and LeaveCriticalSection called via g_pEnterCriticalSectionFunc and g_pLeaveCriticalSectionFunc",
