      "name": "GetBattleNetConnectionStateThreadSafe",
      "signature": "int GetBattleNetConnectionStateThreadSafe(BattleNetStateInfo * pStateInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current Battle.net connection state and associated data in a thread-safe manner using a critical section lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section (g_BattleNetCriticalSection at 0x6ff3f1dc) to protect global state access\n2. Read current Battle.net state value from g_dwConnectionState (0x6ff3f1f4)\n3. Read associated data/value pointer from g_dwDataPointerOrValue (0x6ff3f1d8) into local variable\n4. Compare state value against special state indicator 0x1b\n5. Store state value to output structure at offset +0x00\n6. Store data pointer to output structure at offset +0x04\n7. If state equals 0x1b (special state), replace data pointer with g_MD5HashContext (0x6ff3f158)\n8. Leave critical section (g_BattleNetCriticalSection) to release lock\n9. Return 1 to indicate successful completion\n\nParameters:\npStateInfo - Pointer to BattleNetStateInfo output structure (8 bytes: 4-byte state + 4-byte data pointer)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns success indicator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State value 0x1b triggers special handling: the data pointer field is replaced with address of g_MD5HashContext buffer (0x6ff3f158, 128 bytes)\n- Thread-safe: Uses g_BattleNetCriticalSection to serialize access to global state variables\n- Atomic operation: Critical section ensures state and data are read/stored as atomic pair\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_BattleNetCriticalSection (0x6ff3f1dc) - RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION structure for synchronization\ng_dwConnectionState (0x6ff3f1f4) - Current Battle.net connection state value\ng_dwDataPointerOrValue (0x6ff3f1d8) - Associated data pointer or integer value\ng_MD5HashContext (0x6ff3f158) - 128-byte buffer used for state 0x1b special case\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|-------|----------------------------------\n+0x00  |  4   | dwStateValue      | DWORD | Current Battle.net state value\n+0x04  |  4   | pDataOrValue      | DWORD | Associated data pointer or value\n-------|------|-------------------|-------|----------------------------------\nTotal: 8 bytes",
