      "name": "InitializeGlobalStateOnce",
      "signature": "DWORD InitializeGlobalStateOnce(DWORD dwInitialValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Thread-safe one-time initialization of global error code state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock (g_BattleNetCriticalSection) for thread-safe access\n2. Load current value of g_dwGameErrorCode from memory address 0x6ff3f1f4\n3. Test if g_dwGameErrorCode is zero (not yet initialized)\n4. If already initialized (non-zero), skip to step 6\n5. If not initialized, load dwInitialValue from stack and write to g_dwGameErrorCode\n6. Release critical section lock to allow other threads\n7. Return 1 (success indicator) in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- dwInitialValue: DWORD - The value to write to g_dwGameErrorCode on first call. On subsequent calls, this parameter is ignored and the existing g_dwGameErrorCode value is preserved.\n\nReturns:\n- DWORD: Always returns 1 (success status code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function implements a \"write-once\" pattern where g_dwGameErrorCode can only be set once\n- If g_dwGameErrorCode is already non-zero, the provided dwInitialValue is discarded\n- The critical section ensures only one thread can modify g_dwGameErrorCode at a time\n- Multiple calls to this function from different threads will serialize through the critical section lock",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
