      "name": "DequeueAndFreeBNetEntry",
      "signature": "uint DequeueAndFreeBNetEntry(uint * pEntryId, byte * pDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Dequeues and frees the first Battle.net message entry from the global queue, copying its payload data to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire g_BattleNetCriticalSection lock for thread-safe queue access\n2. Load queue head pointer from g_dwGameStateVar1 (global queue head)\n3. Test if queue head is null; if empty jump to queue_empty_handler\n4. Load entry data size from current entry offset +0x124 (dataSize field)\n5. Calculate DWORD count for aligned copy: size >> 2\n6. Copy full DWORDs from entry data (offset +0x4) to pDataBuffer via REP MOVSD\n7. Calculate remaining bytes: size & 3 (0-3 bytes for tail)\n8. Copy remaining bytes to pDataBuffer via REP MOVSB\n9. Load entry ID from current entry offset +0x0 and store to *pEntryId output\n10. Load data size from offset +0x124 for return value\n11. Load next entry pointer from offset +0x128 (pNext field)\n12. Call destructor at 0x6ff280f0 passing entry pointer in ECX\n13. Update g_dwGameStateVar1 queue head to next entry pointer\n14. Release g_BattleNetCriticalSection lock\n15. Return data size (0-0x120) as success indicator\n16. On empty queue: release lock and return 0 immediately\n\nParameters:\npEntryId: uint* - Output pointer to store the dequeued entry ID from offset +0x0\npDataBuffer: byte* - Output buffer receiving entry payload data (max 0x120 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Size of data copied (0-0x120 bytes), or 0 if queue was empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty queue returns 0 without modifying output parameters. Maximum entry data size is 288 bytes (0x120). Entry structure layout: ID at +0x0, data at +0x4-0x123, dataSize at +0x124, next pointer at +0x128. Destructor freeing is handled at 0x6ff280f0 via vtable call.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6b051200df70700a50910290e6f0b8ee",
