      "name": "ProcessCryptographicCommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessCryptographicCommand(CommandRequest * pRequest)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Dispatches cryptographic provider initialization commands based on command type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read command type from pRequest->commandType and store in g_dwCryptProviderValid\n2. Validate command type is in range 0-6, dispatch to default handler if out of range\n3. Switch on command type using jump table dispatch:\n   Case 0: No-op, return success (1)\n   Case 1: Initialize SHA/MD5 provider (ordinal 0xD)\n   Case 2: Initialize broken SHA/MD5 provider (ordinal 0xE)\n   Case 3: Initialize lockdown SHA/MD5 provider (ordinal 0xF)\n   Case 6: Initialize thread-safe MD5 hash with pRequest->sha1Hash (+4 offset, ordinal 0x1B)\n   Default: Thread-safe initialization of g_dwGameErrorCode with fallback value 0x12\n4. All paths return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npRequest - CommandRequest * - Pointer to command request structure\n  +0x0: commandType - Command type selector (0-6)\n  +0x4: sha1Hash - Hash data for command type 6 (20 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success status code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command type 0: No-op dispatch path through default case\n- Command type 6: Passes pRequest+4 (sha1Hash pointer) to thread-safe MD5 initializer\n- Default/Out-of-range: Enters critical section, checks if g_dwGameErrorCode is zero, sets to 0x12 if uninitialized\n- g_dwCryptProviderValid (0x6ff3e120): Stores command type globally for reference\n- g_BattleNetCriticalSection (0x6ff3f1dc): Protects g_dwGameErrorCode initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4eae409d642579f34890ef335f4b23df",
