      "name": "InitializeGameData",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game data structures and synchronization objects at startup\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear first memory region (0x6ff3eed8) by writing 94 dwords of zeros via REP STOSD\n2. Clear second memory region (0x6ff3ed58) by writing 94 dwords of zeros via REP STOSD  \n3. Set initialization completion marker at 0x6ff3e120 to 0xff\n4. Clear game state counter at 0x6ff3f644 to 0\n5. Push critical section address (0x6ff3f1dc) and call EnterCriticalSection\n6. Clear game error code at 0x6ff3f1f4 to 0 (thread-safe within critical section)\n7. Push critical section address and call LeaveCriticalSection to release lock\n8. Load return value EAX with 1 (success indicator)\n\nParameters:\n(none - no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Total memory cleared: 188 dwords (752 bytes) across two separate data regions\n- Critical section protects g_dwGameErrorCode from concurrent thread access\n- Marker value 0xff signals initialization completion to other subsystems\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (function cleans stack with RET)\n- No error handling implemented - assumes all operations succeed",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
