      "name": "SetCryptographicProvider",
      "signature": "int SetCryptographicProvider(int * pProviderType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the cryptographic provider type for Battle.net authentication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load provider type value from input parameter pointer (stored in ECX via __fastcall convention)\n2. Store provider type to global variable g_dwCryptoModeState at address 0x6ff3eed0\n3. Set cryptographic provider initialization flag to 1 at address 0x6ff3ef9c\n4. Test if provider type equals 0 (indicating default/null provider)\n5. If provider type is non-zero, skip default initialization and jump to return\n6. If provider type is zero, enter critical section at 0x6ff3f1dc for thread-safe access\n7. Load current default provider value from address 0x6ff3f1f4\n8. Test if default provider is already initialized (non-zero)\n9. If already initialized, jump to critical section exit\n10. If not initialized, write default value 0xe (14 decimal) to address 0x6ff3f1f4\n11. Leave critical section by calling LeaveCriticalSection via function pointer at 0x6ff391b0\n12. Set return value in EAX to 1 (success code)\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pProviderType - Pointer to cryptographic provider type constant (int*). Value is loaded from [ECX] and stored to global g_dwCryptoModeState for use by authentication routines. Provider type 0 triggers default initialization.\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 indicating success. No error conditions are handled; this function always succeeds even if default initialization was already performed.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Provider type 0 (null/default): Triggers thread-safe initialization with critical section lock to prevent race conditions\n  - Default provider constant 0xe (14): Represents the default cryptographic provider algorithm for Battle.net\n  - Critical section 0x6ff3f1dc: Protects concurrent access to default provider during multi-threaded initialization\n  - Initialization flag 0x6ff3ef9c: Marks provider as configured to prevent redundant initialization\n  - Thread safety: Critical section ensures consistent provider state across all authentication threads\n  - Magic number 0xe: Default crypto provider value hard-coded for Battle.net compatibility\n\nStructure Layout:\n  RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION at 0x6ff3f1dc (24 bytes total):\n    Offset  Size  Field               Description\n    0x00    4     DebugInfo           Pointer to critical section debug info\n    0x04    4     LockCount           Lock counter (-1 = unlocked, 0+ = locked)\n    0x08    4     RecursionCount      Recursion depth counter\n    0x0c    4     OwningThread        Thread ID that owns the lock\n    0x10    4     LockSemaphore       Semaphore for thread synchronization\n    0x14    4     SpinCount           Spin count before blocking on semaphore",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
