      "name": "ProcessHashCommand",
      "signature": "uint ProcessHashCommand(CommandRequest * pCommand, uint dwCommandBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Process hash verification command with thread-safe state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer size is at least 0x18 bytes (24 bytes minimum)\n2. Extract command type from pCommand->commandType at offset +0\n3. Branch on command type:\n   - Type 0: SHA1 hash verification mode - verify hash at offset +4, set state to 0 on success\n   - Type 2: Set initialization state to 2 with error code 0xe (14), thread-safe via critical section\n   - Other types: Invalid command - set error code to 0x12 (18), thread-safe via critical section\n4. Enter/leave critical section to protect global state modifications\n5. Return 1 on successful processing, 0 on validation failure or invalid command\n\nParameters:\n- pCommand: Pointer to CommandRequest structure with type at offset +0 and hash data at offset +4\n- commandBufferSize: Size of command buffer in bytes (minimum 0x18 = 24 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (TRUE) if command processed successfully (hash verified OR state set to 2)\n- 0 (FALSE) if buffer too small, invalid command type, or hash verification failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Minimum buffer size 0x18 bytes enforced\n- Critical section g_BattleNetCriticalSection used for thread-safe state updates\n- Global error code g_dw_GameStateVar3 only set if previously 0 (idempotent)\n- Global crypto state g_hCryptProvider set to 0 on hash success or 2 on type-2 command\n- Error codes: 0x12 (18) for invalid commands, 0xe (14) for type-2 commands\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dw_GameStateVar3 @ 0x6ff3f1f4: Error code (0x12 or 0xe)\n- g_hCryptProvider @ 0x6ff3e120: Crypto state (0 or 2)\n- g_BattleNetCriticalSection @ 0x6ff3f1dc: Thread synchronization",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
