      "name": "ValidateAndInitiateDownload",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitiateDownload(void * pDownloadBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates a structured download request buffer and initiates file download if validation passes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates buffer size is at least 0x16 (22 bytes)\n2. Verifies the last byte of buffer is null terminator (0x00)\n3. Scans buffer from offset 0x14 to bufferSize-2 counting null terminators\n4. Confirms exactly one null terminator exists in the scanned range\n5. If validation fails at any step, returns 0\n6. If validation passes, extracts four DWORD fields from buffer structure:\n   - Offset +0x00: Download mode value (stored to g_downloadMode)\n   - Offset +0x04: Crypt context handle (stored to g_hCryptContext)\n   - Offset +0x0c: Reserved field 1\n   - Offset +0x10: Reserved field 2\n7. Extracts null-terminated string from offset +0x14 using strlen()\n8. Computes MD5 hash of string + 1 byte offset with 0x104-byte buffer\n9. Computes MD5 hash of szObfuscatedVerificationData with 0x7fffffff size\n10. Calls InitiateFileDownload with handle 0x80000001, operation code 3\n11. Returns 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer - Pointer to structured buffer containing download request data\n  bufferSize - Total size of buffer in bytes (validated >= 0x16)\n\nReturns:\n  1 if validation passed and download initiated successfully\n  0 if validation failed (incorrect size, missing null terminator, or null count mismatch)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic constant 0x16: Minimum buffer size required (22 bytes)\n  Magic constant 0x14: Offset where string data begins in buffer\n  Magic constant 0x104: Hash buffer size for first MD5 operation\n  Magic constant 0x7fffffff: Size parameter for second MD5 operation\n  Magic constant 0x80000001: Special file download handle\n  Magic constant 3: File download operation code\n  \n  The function expects exactly ONE null terminator in the range [0x14, bufferSize-2).\n  String must be null-terminated at buffer end (bufferSize-1).\n  \nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name               | Type      | Description\n-------|------|--------------------------|-----------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwDownloadMode           | DWORD     | Mode flags for download operation\n0x04   | 4    | hCryptContext            | HANDLE    | Cryptographic context handle\n0x0c   | 4    | reserved1                | DWORD     | Reserved field 1\n0x10   | 4    | reserved2                | DWORD     | Reserved field 2\n0x14   | var  | szDownloadPath           | char[N]   | Null-terminated download path string\nTotal: 0x14 + string_length + 1 (null terminator)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
