      "name": "ProcessFileDownloadWithHash",
      "signature": "uint ProcessFileDownloadWithHash(FileDownloadRequest * pRequest, char * pszBoundary)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes a file download request by validating bounds and computing MD5 hash of source path.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load source path pointer from FileDownloadRequest structure at offset +8 (sourcePath field)\n2. Scan source path string to find null terminator using first strlen loop (loop_check_source_strlen)\n3. Calculate required space: strlen(sourcePath) + 9 bytes for hash computation\n4. Compare required space against pszBoundary pointer to validate sufficient buffer space\n5. If space is insufficient (JNC jump to call_initiate_download), skip MD5 computation entirely\n6. If space is sufficient, recalculate strlen to determine hash output buffer offset (loop_check_hash_strlen)\n7. Call MD5HashData with szMD5HashBuffer address (0x6ff3f770), hash source offset, size 0x104 (260 bytes)\n8. Call InitiateFileDownload with flags 0x80000001 (high priority), mode 3 (operation type)\n9. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pRequest (ECX) - Pointer to FileDownloadRequest structure:\n    +0x08: sourcePath (UINT) - Start address of source path string (extracted at 0x6ff31724)\n    +0x20: buffer area (260+ bytes for MD5 output storage)\n  pszBoundary (EDX) - Upper boundary pointer for bounds validation of hash buffer space\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - MD5 hash computation only occurs if (strlen(sourcePath) + 9) < pszBoundary offset\n  - Hash buffer stored at global address szMD5HashBuffer (0x6ff3f770)\n  - Download priority flag 0x80000001 indicates high-priority operation with special handling bit\n  - Hash computation size parameter is 0x104 (260 decimal bytes)\n  - Mode 3 specifies the download operation type for InitiateFileDownload\n  - Second strlen loop required to calculate correct offset for hash data within buffer",
