      "name": "InitializeCryptographicState",
      "signature": "int InitializeCryptographicState(void * pDataBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the cryptographic state by hashing input data and generating random values for cipher initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero the crypto initialization flag (g_dwCryptoInitFlag)\n2. Hash sourceData1 (256 bytes) with MD5 into g_CryptoHashBuffer1\n3. Clear cipher object buffer at g_CryptoCipherObject (0xbc bytes)\n4. Hash sourceData1 again with MD5 into hash1Buffer (256 bytes)\n5. Apply crypto transformation to hash1Buffer using TransformHashData\n6. Hash input parameter pDataBuffer with MD5 into hash2Buffer (256 bytes)\n7. Apply crypto transformation to hash2Buffer using TransformHashData\n8. Process crypto object at g_CryptoCipherObject with hash2Buffer and global state g_dwCryptoContextState\n9. Generate random seed (32 bytes) from g_CryptoRandomSeed into cryptoRandomBuffer\n10. Hash sourceData1 a third time with MD5 into hash3Buffer, store length in hashOutputLength\n11. Generate final cryptographic random data of 0x53 (83) bytes, offset by (hashOutputLength + 0x21)\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npDataBuffer (void*): Input data buffer containing crypto material to process\nsourceData1Pointer (void*): Implicit parameter in ESI register - primary source data for hashing\ncryptoStateFlags (byte): Implicit parameter in DI register - state/mode flags for crypto operations\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success status code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x100 (256 decimal) = MD5 hash output size and buffer size\nMagic number 0xbc (188 decimal) = Cipher object structure size\nMagic number 0x20 (32 decimal) = Random seed buffer size\nMagic number 0x53 (83 decimal) = Final random data generation size\nMagic number 0x21 (33 decimal) = Offset added to hash length for random generation positioning\nThe function reuses the same source data (sourceData1Pointer) for three separate hash operations\nHash lengths are computed and used to derive offsets for output generation\n\nGlobal Data Dependencies:\ng_dwCryptoInitFlag: Initialization status flag (set to 0)\ng_CryptoHashBuffer1: 256-byte buffer for initial MD5 hash output\ng_CryptoCipherObject: Cipher/cipher object structure (0xbc bytes)\ng_CryptoRandomSeed: 32-byte random seed buffer\ng_dwCryptoContextState: Global cryptographic context state object",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:736a86a3bc66b24c6a8ae810c6a1c0a0",
