      "name": "InitializeAndValidateCryptoObject",
      "signature": "uint InitializeAndValidateCryptoObject(ObjectData * pCryptoData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes and validates a cryptographic object with random data generation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ValidateAndProcessCryptoObject with global crypto state (g_dwCryptoContextState) and crypto object status\n2. Zero the output buffer (g_CryptoOutputBuffer, 0x20 bytes)\n3. Test validation result (non-zero indicates success)\n4. If validation succeeded:\n   a. Call SMemRandom to initialize random seed buffer (0x14 bytes) from g_CryptoRandomSeed\n   b. Call GenerateCryptographicRandomData with random buffer and output size 0x54\n   c. Return 1 (success)\n5. If validation failed: Return 0 (failure)\n\nParameters:\n  pCryptoData: Pointer to ObjectData structure (12 bytes) containing crypto state and object references\n\nReturns:\n  uint: 1 if initialization and validation succeeded, 0 if validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic value 0x14 (20 bytes): Random seed buffer size\n  Magic value 0x20 (32 bytes): Output buffer clear size\n  Magic value 0x54 (84 bytes): Cryptographic output buffer size\n  Global g_dwCryptoContextState: Shared crypto context passed to validation\n  Global g_CryptoOutputBuffer: Zeroed buffer for cryptographic output\n  Global g_CryptoRandomSeed: Seed data for random number generation\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type     | Description\n-------|------|---------------|----------|----------------------------------\n  0x0  |  4   | status        | uint     | Validation status flag\n  0x4  |  4   | pObject1      | pointer  | First crypto object reference\n  0x8  |  4   | pObject2      | pointer  | Second crypto object reference",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
