      "name": "MixTransformRound",
      "signature": "void MixTransformRound(uint dwMixState, ushort * pwMixTable, short * pResultBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Performs a cryptographic mixing transformation round on 4 state components using a lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract 4 component words from the input state (packed as 16-bit values in mixState)\n2. Initialize round counter to 8 for the main mixing loop\n3. For each of 8 rounds:\n   a. Load table value and mask component 1 to 16 bits\n   b. Process component 1: if zero return (1 - table_value), if table zero return (1 - component), else multiply and round\n   c. Load table value 2 and add to component 2 state\n   d. Process component 4: apply same zero checks and multiplication logic\n   e. Load table value 3 and XOR with component 2 + component 1, then multiply with result\n   f. Load table value 5 and mix components using XOR and addition, apply multiplication\n   g. Update all 4 state components by XORing with computed mix results\n   h. Advance table pointer by 12 bytes (6 words) and decrement round counter\n4. Post-loop: perform final mixing on component 1 with table value 6\n5. Write 4 transformed components to output buffer at pResultBuffer[0..3]\n\nParameters:\n  mixState (ECX): Packed initial state containing 4x 16-bit components\n  mixTable (EDX): Pointer to mixing lookup table with 10 words per round\n  pResultBuffer (Stack[0x4]): Pointer to output buffer for 4 transformed 16-bit values\n\nReturns:\n  None (void). Results written to pResultBuffer as 4 signed short values.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero component handling: When a component or table value is zero, compute (1 - other_value) instead of multiply\n  - 16-bit masking: All intermediate results masked to 0xffff to extract 16-bit values\n  - Rounding operation: Multiplication uses 32-bit intermediate, right shift by 0x10 extracts high bits, compare for rounding adjustment\n  - Magic constant 0x10: Right shift amount for extracting high 16 bits of 32-bit product\n  - 8 rounds: Fixed iteration count with table advancement pattern\n  - Calling convention: __fastcall with first param in ECX, second in EDX, third on stack",
