      "name": "CleanupNewsTableSystem",
      "signature": "int CleanupNewsTableSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up and resets the news table system to initial state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load news table object pointer from g_pNewsTable for existence check\n2. Clear configuration parameters g_dwNewsConfigParam1 and g_dwNewsConfigParam2 to 0\n3. Check if news table object exists (compare g_pNewsTable against NULL)\n4. If object exists, call DeleteObjectTrampoline with type string szNewsTableItemTypeInfo and deletion mode -2\n5. Clear news table counters g_dwNewsTableCapacity and g_dwNewsItemCount to 0\n6. Clear news table object pointer g_pNewsTable to NULL\n7. Clear initialization flag g_dwNewsTableInitFlag to 0\n8. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating successful cleanup\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pNewsTable is NULL, skips deletion step (no object to clean up)\n- Magic value -2 (0xFFFFFFFE) passed to DeleteObjectTrampoline as deletion mode\n- Uses XOR ESI,ESI pattern to zero register for efficient bulk clearing\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_dwNewsTableInitFlag (offset 0x6ff3f638) - Initialization flag cleared\ng_dwNewsConfigParam1 (offset 0x6ff3f63c) - Config parameter cleared\ng_dwNewsConfigParam2 (offset 0x6ff3f640) - Config parameter cleared\ng_dwNewsTableCapacity (offset 0x6ff3f8cc) - Table capacity counter cleared\ng_dwNewsItemCount (offset 0x6ff3f8d0) - Item count counter cleared\ng_pNewsTable (offset 0x6ff3f8d4) - Table object pointer set to NULL\nTotal: 24 bytes of global state reset",
