      "name": "InitializeNewsTableSystem",
      "signature": "int InitializeNewsTableSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the news table system with configuration parameters and random seed generation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global initialization flag to 1 (g_dwNewsTableInitFlag = 1)\n2. Store configuration parameters from implicit __fastcall registers: ECX \u2192 g_dwNewsConfigParam1, EDX \u2192 g_dwNewsConfigParam2\n3. Delete existing news table object if present (check g_pNewsTableObject non-NULL)\n4. Clear all news table state: g_dwNewsItemCount, g_dwNewsBufferSize, g_pNewsTableObject, g_dwNewsStateCounter, g_dwNewsRandomSeed\n5. Load news table from external source via LoadNewsTable()\n6. If load successful (dwLoadResult != 0), dispatch iteration callbacks via DispatchIterationCallbacks()\n7. Retrieve random seed value from g_dwNewsRandomSeed and generate cryptographic random data with parameter 0x46 (70)\n8. Return 1 (success indicator)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX (implicit __fastcall) - uint dwConfigParam1, first configuration parameter\n  EDX (implicit __fastcall) - uint dwConfigParam2, second configuration parameter\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success indicator (int)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pNewsTableObject is NULL, skips deletion operation (no existing table to clean)\n  - If LoadNewsTable returns 0 (failure), skips callback dispatch but continues with random generation\n  - Magic constant 0x46 (70 decimal) used for cryptographic random data generation\n  - All news table state variables cleared before loading to ensure clean initialization",
