      "name": "CalculateCrc32",
      "signature": "uint CalculateCrc32(byte * pBuffer, uint dwBufferLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Computes CRC32 polynomial-based checksum for a data buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters: buffer pointer must be non-null and length must be positive\n2. If validation fails: trigger assertion failure, retrieve line number, call error handler, and exit with error code -1\n3. Initialize CRC accumulator to 0xFFFFFFFF for standard CRC32 computation\n4. If buffer length is zero: skip to finalization step\n5. For each byte in the buffer:\n   - Extract low byte of current CRC and XOR with current buffer byte\n   - Use result as index (0-255) into pre-computed CRC polynomial lookup table at 0x6ff3dcf0\n   - Right-shift CRC accumulator by 8 bits to remove processed byte\n   - XOR CRC with the polynomial value retrieved from table (4 bytes per entry)\n   - Advance buffer pointer to next byte\n   - Decrement remaining byte counter\n6. Finalize: Apply bitwise NOT operation to CRC value\n7. Return final 32-bit CRC checksum\n\nParameters:\n- pBuffer (ECX): Pointer to byte array containing data to checksum; must be non-NULL\n- bufferLength (EAX): Number of bytes in buffer; must be positive for valid input\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Final CRC32 polynomial checksum (32-bit unsigned integer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty buffer (length=0) returns 0xFFFFFFFF (CRC after NOT of 0x00000000)\n- NULL buffer triggers validation failure, assertion, and program exit with code -1\n- Uses pre-computed 256-entry polynomial table (1024 bytes total) at address 0x6ff3dcf0\n- Each table entry is 4 bytes (DWORD) containing pre-computed polynomial result\n- Called by cache validation and file loading functions to verify data integrity\n\nCalling Convention:\n- __fastcall: First parameter (pBuffer) in ECX, second parameter (bufferLength) in EDX/EAX\n- Caller cleans up stack (no RET immediate value)",
