      "name": "LoadCacheFileFromDisk",
      "signature": "uint LoadCacheFileFromDisk(char * pCacheName, uint * pCacheData, int * pDataBuffer, DWORD * pBytesRead)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Loads a Battle.net cache file from disk and validates its integrity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate all input parameters (cache name, data pointers, output buffers)\n2. Initialize output buffers to zero if pointers provided\n3. Acquire exclusive cache access lock via EnterCriticalSection\n4. Look up cache entry in hash table by cache name\n5. If cache entry not found, release lock and return error code 0\n6. Retrieve cache entry metadata (size, file offset, flags)\n7. Read 4-byte cache file header from disk\n8. Validate magic number equals 0x144\n9. Read 0x140 bytes of cache data from disk\n10. Calculate CRC32 checksum over data\n11. Verify calculated CRC32 matches embedded checksum\n12. Compare cache filename against expected name via strcmp\n13. Get current system time and compare against file timestamp\n14. If timestamp out of valid range, log error and clear cache\n15. Allocate memory buffer for full cache data\n16. Seek to data offset in cache file\n17. Read full cache data into allocated buffer\n18. Write data to output buffer if provided\n19. Verify number of bytes written matches expected\n20. Calculate final CRC32 on written data\n21. Release cache access lock\n22. Return success code 1 if all validations pass\n\nParameters:\npCacheName (char *): Name/key of cache entry to load\npCacheData (uint *): Pointer to receive cache data pointer (nullable)\npDataBuffer (int *): Pointer to output buffer for cache data\npBytesRead (DWORD *): Pointer to receive bytes read count\n\nReturns:\n0x1 (1): Success - cache file loaded, validated, and data returned\n0x0 (0): Failure - invalid parameters, cache lookup failed, or not initialized\nError codes (0x2-0x7): Various validation failures (logged via error format strings)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number validation: Cache files must start with 0x144 signature byte\nCRC32 verification: Protects against file corruption\nFilename comparison: Must match exactly via case-insensitive strcmp\nTimestamp validation: File modification time checked against current time\nSize limit: Cache data cannot exceed 0x1000000 bytes (16 MB maximum)",
