      "name": "ScanToLineEnd",
      "signature": "char * ScanToLineEnd(char * pBufferStart, char * pBufferEnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Scans a buffer for the next line ending character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer bounds: Check that start pointer is less than end pointer\n2. Iterate through buffer from start to end\n3. Load current character from buffer\n4. Check for line ending markers:\n   - Null terminator (0x00) indicates end of string\n   - Carriage return (0x0D) indicates DOS/Windows line ending\n   - Line feed (0x0A) indicates Unix line ending\n5. If any marker found, return pointer to that position\n6. If no marker found, continue to next character\n7. If buffer boundary reached without finding marker, return end pointer\n\nParameters:\npBufferStart: Starting address of buffer to scan (char *)\npBufferEnd: Upper boundary address of buffer (char *). Scanning stops if this address is reached without finding line ending.\n\nReturns:\nchar * - Pointer to the first line ending character found (\\0, \\r, or \n), or pBufferEnd if no ending found before boundary.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pBufferStart >= pBufferEnd (invalid bounds), returns pBufferStart immediately\n- Buffer must be null-terminated or have defined boundary; behavior undefined if neither condition met\n- Used for parsing INI files and text configuration data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1cf4e806563b5f504db52c5d589c23be",
