      "name": "GetGatewayList",
      "signature": "void GetGatewayList(BNGatewayAccess * this, char * szConfigData)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Parses gateway list from configuration data and populates BNGatewayAccess object\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify the gateway buffer is uninitialized (assert check on offset +0x10)\n2. If assertion fails, log line number, call AssertFailed with assertion message, and exit\n3. Initialize local variables for parsing state tracking\n4. Call internal parsing function (0x101fa5e0) to extract gateway count from config data\n5. If parse succeeds and count is non-zero, allocate memory buffer sized to hold gateway data\n6. Store allocated buffer pointer in object at offset +0x10\n7. Call parsing function again with allocated buffer and count to populate gateway data\n8. If second parse fails, deallocate buffer and clear gateway data pointers\n9. Extract total gateway entry count as unsigned long using string-to-unsigned-long conversion\n10. If conversion fails (string pointer unchanged), reset count to zero\n11. Store final gateway count at object offset +0x18\n\nParameters:\nthis: BNGatewayAccess object pointer containing gateway state (ECX)\nszConfigData: Configuration file content string to parse\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored in BNGatewayAccess object fields:\n  +0x10: Pointer to allocated gateway data buffer (or NULL if parse failed)\n  +0x14: Size of allocated buffer in bytes\n  +0x18: Total number of gateways parsed (unsigned long)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure if object already has buffer allocated (+0x10 != 0) indicates reuse attempt\n- Parse may fail on second call if format is invalid; buffer is cleaned up\n- String parsing stops at first non-numeric character; validates pointer movement\n- Magic number 0x82: Maximum expected field count or buffer size unit\n- Magic number 0x148: Source file line number offset (0x148 bytes)\n- Magic number 0x150: Destructor offset for cleanup (0x150 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
