      "name": "FindSectionInIniFile",
      "signature": "char * FindSectionInIniFile(BNGatewayAccess * this, char * szSectionName, char * szSectionContent)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Searches INI file content for a named section header and returns pointer to first line after section.\n\nAlgorithm\n1. Calculate length of sectionName parameter (length without null terminator)\n2. Calculate length of sectionContent parameter (e.g., \"[GATEWAY]\", includes brackets)\n3. Initialize file pointer to start of sectionName buffer\n4. Loop through file content scanning character by character\n5. When '[' character is found, perform case-insensitive comparison of next bytes with sectionContent\n6. If comparison matches, skip to end of line and skip any following whitespace/newlines\n7. Return pointer to first non-whitespace character after section header\n8. If end of file reached without finding match, return NULL\n\nParameters\n- this: BNGatewayAccess * - Class instance pointer\n- sectionName: char * - Section name to search for (e.g., \"GATEWAY\")\n- sectionContent: char * - Full section header including brackets (e.g., \"[GATEWAY]\")\n\nReturns\n- char * - Pointer to first line of content after section header if found, NULL if section not found\n\nSpecial Cases\n- Uses case-insensitive comparison (__strnicmp) for section matching\n- Skips whitespace and blank lines after section header\n- If no section found, calls AssertFailed with line number 0x205 and exits with code -1",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
