      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Extracts and parses a gateway message timestamp value from a string collection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Nth() to retrieve a string at the specified index from the BNGatewayAccess string collection\n2. Check if the retrieved string is null-terminated (first byte is 0x00)\n3. If not empty, call strlen() to get the string length and advance pointer past the string and null terminator\n4. Call _strtol() to parse the remaining string as a base-10 long integer\n5. Return the parsed timestamp value\n\nParameters:\n- nStringIndex: Index into the string collection to retrieve the timestamp string\n\nReturns:\n- long: Parsed timestamp value as a 32-bit signed long integer, or 0 if parsing fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If the retrieved string is empty (null-terminated at first byte), directly parse from the beginning\n- Empty string results in 0 from _strtol()\n- The function assumes the string at the index contains a valid numeric timestamp",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8255851871466712f4843c0893052b76",
