      "name": "GetRealmByIndex",
      "signature": "char * GetRealmByIndex(BNGatewayAccess * this, int nRealmIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the realm name associated with a given index from the BNGatewayAccess realm list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Nth() to get the realm data pointer at the specified index\n2. Load the realm names pointer from offset +0x20 of the BNGatewayAccess structure\n3. Iterate through the realm list, comparing each stored realm name with the target realm data\n4. For each comparison that fails, advance to the next entry by skipping its length + 1 byte\n5. Continue iteration until a match is found (CompareDataThunk returns 0) or end of list is reached\n6. If match found, return pointer to the realm name that follows the target realm data in memory\n7. If no match found or list is empty, return pointer to szDefaultRealmNotFound sentinel value\n\nParameters:\nthis - Pointer to BNGatewayAccess object containing realm configuration\nrealmIndex - Index of realm to lookup (1-based from Nth() function)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to null-terminated realm name string if found, or pointer to szDefaultRealmNotFound if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Realm index must be between 1 and the configured count in BNGatewayAccess.dwRealmCount\n- String comparison is case-sensitive via CompareDataThunk()\n- Returns sentinel string for invalid indices or empty realm list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:11733175d96097366816caf5c9170cf7",
