      "name": "SaveAndUnload",
      "signature": "void SaveAndUnload(BNGatewayAccess * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Saves the current gateway list selection to file and unloads gateway configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if both gatewayName (offset +0x4) and gatewayPath (offset +0x10) are valid\n2. If valid, log the \"Recording gateway list selection\" debug message\n3. Append two ASCII digits representing the current gatewayIndex (offset +0xc) to the end of gatewayPath string\n4. Validate that the last two bytes before the appended digits are null terminators\n5. If validation fails, trigger assertion error with source file location and exit process\n6. Delete gatewayPath object pointer (offset +0x10) using DeleteObjectTrampoline at offset 0xb8\n7. Clear gatewayPath (offset +0x10) and reserved field (offset +0x14)\n8. Delete secondaryGatewayPtr (offset +0x20) using DeleteObjectTrampoline at offset 0xbe\n9. Clear secondaryGatewayPtr (offset +0x20)\n\nParameters:\nthis - BNGatewayAccess instance containing gateway configuration data\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If gatewayPath is NULL, function skips logging and proceeds to cleanup phase\n- Magic number 0x66666667 is used for efficient integer division by 10\n- Two different gateway list strings are used based on gatewayListType (offset +0x1c):\n  * 0x6ff3a95c: \"Override Battle.net gateways\" (when gatewayListType != 0)\n  * 0x6ff3aa2c: \"Diablo II Battle.net gateways\" (when gatewayListType == 0)\n- Source file path \"..\\\\Source\\\\D2BNClient\\\\BNetGW.cpp\" is hardcoded at 0x6ff3a93c\n- Assertion message at 0x6ff3a813 contains obfuscated text",
