      "name": "PickClosestZone",
      "signature": "void PickClosestZone(BNGatewayAccess * this, int timeInSeconds)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Determines the gateway (server) with the closest GMT offset to the requested time.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enable debug logging and extract minutes and seconds from the input timeInSeconds parameter using division and modulo by 60 (0x3c)\n2. Log the formatted time request using the debug format string\n3. Initialize loop counters and set minimum distance tracker (local_10) to 0x564 (1380 decimal)\n4. Iterate through all available gateways (0 to count stored at offset +0x8) using the Nth() method to retrieve each gateway entry string\n5. For each gateway entry: skip the gateway name portion by finding the first null terminator, then parse the GMT offset value from the remaining string using _strtol base 10\n6. Calculate the absolute difference between the gateway's GMT offset (multiplied by 60 to convert to seconds) and the requested time\n7. If this distance is smaller than the current minimum, update the best gateway index and minimum distance\n8. After loop completes, retrieve the best gateway entry name and its GMT offset for logging\n9. Log the selected gateway details including index, name, GMT offset, and original request time\n10. Disable debug logging\n11. Validate that the selection is enabled (offset +0x10 != 0), index is 1-99 inclusive, and index does not exceed gateway count\n12. Clamp the index to maximum of 99 (0x63) if needed\n13. Store the selected gateway index at offset +0xc and set the selection flag at offset +0x4 to 1\n\nParameters:\nthis: Pointer to BNGatewayAccess object containing gateway list and configuration\ntimeInSeconds: Requested time in seconds (0-based, typically 0-86399 for 24-hour period)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies the BNGatewayAccess object's selected gateway index at offset +0xc if validation passes\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic numbers: 0x3c (60 - seconds per minute), 0x564 (1380 - initial min distance), 0x63 (99 - max gateway index)\nStructure offsets: +0x8 (gateway count), +0xc (selected index), +0x10 (enabled flag), +0x4 (selection flag)\nString format: Each gateway entry is \"GatewayName\\0GMTOffset\" with null terminator between name and offset",
