      "name": "ParseAndUpdateGatewayListFromIni",
      "signature": "void ParseAndUpdateGatewayListFromIni(BNGatewayAccess * pGatewayAccess, char * pFilePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Parses gateway list from INI file and updates BNGatewayAccess structure with hashed gateway data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate length of input file path string using null-terminator scan\n2. Find \"Server List Version\" section in INI file structure\n3. Find \"VER\" key within version section, retrieve version number via strtoul\n4. If stored version >= new version, exit (no update needed)\n5. Log \"Parsing new gateway list\" message with version number\n6. Determine timezone offset (system timezone if not set, else GMT-based)\n7. Clear and reinitialize gateway fields at offsets +0x4, +0x1c, +0x1d, +0x1e, +0x1f\n8. Save current state and deallocate old data\n9. Allocate new buffer for hashed gateway data (size = 2 * filepath_length)\n10. Format version string into new buffer using \"%d\" format, pad with \"00\"\n11. Find \"Server Gateways\" section in INI\n12. Loop through numbered gateway entries (Gateway_1, Gateway_2, etc):\n    a. For each gateway key, get end-of-line position\n    b. Hash gateway key data to buffer\n    c. Find section matching hashed key name\n    d. If section found:\n       - Hash \"ZONE\" key value (or default \"0\") to buffer\n       - Hash \"ENU\" (region) key value to buffer\n       - Advance buffer pointer by accumulated hash sizes\n13. Null-terminate hash buffer and validate:\n    a. Check that hash buffer fits within allocated size\n    b. Verify last two bytes are null terminators\n14. Store buffer pointers in BNGatewayAccess structure (+0x10, +0x14)\n15. Pick closest timezone zone based on offset\n16. Save final state and load/validate gateway data\n\nParameters:\npGatewayAccess - Pointer to BNGatewayAccess structure (modified in-place)\n                 Fields at: +0x4 (flags), +0x10 (pointer), +0x14 (pointer),\n                           +0x18 (version), +0x1c-0x1f (reserved)\npFilePath - Path to INI configuration file (not modified)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Structure modified in-place or process exits with assertion on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Version mismatch triggers full reparse of gateway data\n- Missing required keys (VER, ZONE, ENU) handled with default values\n- Assertion failure and exit(-1) if gateway data validation fails\n- Buffer overflow checked against allocated size",
