      "name": "WriteDefaultGatewayList",
      "signature": "void WriteDefaultGatewayList(BNGatewayAccess * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Writes the default gateway configuration list from the gateways data file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Log debug message indicating gateway list write operation\n2. Initialize file size counter to zero\n3. Call ReadFileData to load gateways.txt from DATA\\GLOBAL directory into memory buffer\n4. Check if file read succeeded (readResult == 0 indicates failure)\n5. If read failed: obtain assertion line number, log assertion failure, and exit with code -1\n6. If read succeeded: check if file size (fileSize) is non-zero\n7. If file size > 0: call UpdateGatewaysFromIni to parse and apply gateway configuration from loaded file\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nthis (BNGatewayAccess *): Pointer to BNGatewayAccess object containing gateway configuration state\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value (function terminates via exit(-1) on error or normal return on success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- File not found or read failure: Calls _exit(-1) to terminate program with error code\n- Empty file (fileSize == 0): Skips UpdateGatewaysFromIni call (no gateways to process)\n- Line number for assertion obtained from GetLineNumberForAssertion (line 440, 0x1b8)",
