      "name": "LoadBNGatewayDataAndValidate",
      "signature": "void LoadBNGatewayDataAndValidate(BNGatewayAccess * this, BNGatewayAccess * pThis)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Loads Battle.net gateway data from a binary file and validates the configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if already loaded (offset +0x10): if non-zero, return immediately (idempotent)\n2. Initialize gateway access structure: clear all fields (offsets +0x8, +0xc, +0x10, +0x14, +0x18, +0x1c)\n3. Read gateway data file \"Data\\Global\\Realms.bin\" using ReadFileData: output to ppGatewayDataBuffer\n4. If file read fails: trigger assertion and exit with code -1\n5. Attempt to parse \"Override Battle.net gateways\" config section via GetGatewayList\n6. If override gateways not found: attempt to parse \"Diablo II Battle.net gateways\" config section\n7. If gateways found: mark as override (offset +0x1c = 1), otherwise write default gateway list\n8. Validate gateway count at offset +0x18: must be >= 1000; if obsolete (<1000): log warning, clear config, write to INI, trigger assertion\n9. Count total gateway string lengths: loop through gateway list at offset +0x10, calculate cumulative size at offset +0x14\n10. Calculate number of gateways: (total_bytes - 1) / 3 (since each gateway is 3 strings: IP, port, description)\n11. Extract first gateway data: skip initial string, parse second string as selected gateway ID using strtoul with base 10\n12. Validate gateway ID: must be >= 1 and <= gatewayCount; if invalid: auto-pick gateway using GetSystemTimeZone and PickClosestZone\n13. Return successfully with gateway data validated and selected\n\nParameters:\n(implicit this) - Pointer to BNGatewayAccess object containing gateway state at offsets 0, 4, 8, 10, 14, 18, 1c, 20\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function never returns to caller on error (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Idempotent: checks offset +0x10 at start; if already loaded, returns immediately\n- Assertion triggered if file not read or gateway count < 1000: exits with -1\n- String parsing assumes multi-string format with null terminators: \"IP\\0port\\0desc\\0IP2\\0port2\\0desc2\\0...\"\n- Gateway count calculated as (accumulated_string_length - 1) / 3: validates modulo 3 == 0\n- Selected gateway ID must be 1-based (minimum 1, not 0)\n- Auto-picks gateway based on system GMT timezone if configured ID is invalid\n\nStructure Layout (BNGatewayAccess):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type          Description\n+0      1     dwFlags                 byte          Initialization flags\n+4      4     dwSelectedMode          DWORD         Current selection mode (0=default, 1=override)\n+8      4     dwGatewayCount          DWORD         Number of gateways parsed\n+0xc    4     dwSelectedGatewayId     QWORD         Selected gateway index (1-based ID)\n+0x10   4     pGatewayDataBuffer      void*         Pointer to loaded gateway strings\n+0x14   4     dwGatewayDataSize       DWORD         Total size of concatenated gateway strings\n+0x18   4     dwListTimestamp         DWORD         Gateway list version/timestamp\n+0x1c   4     dwIsOverride            DWORD         Flag: 1=using override gateways, 0=using defaults\n+0x20   4     pConfigBuffer           void*         Pointer to config file buffer (allocated by ReadFileData)",
