      "name": "InitializeGridBuffers",
      "signature": "void InitializeGridBuffers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes two grid buffers with template data, validating encryption status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if first grid buffer pointer (EBX implicit parameter) is valid (non-null)\n2. If valid, allocate 0x48 (72) bytes of memory for first grid buffer\n3. Copy template data from g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate to allocated buffer using optimized memcpy\n4. Divide size by 4 to copy 72 bytes as 18 DWORDs using REP MOVSD instruction\n5. Copy remaining alignment bytes (0-3) individually using REP MOVSB instruction\n6. Test if second grid buffer pointer (stack parameter) is valid (non-null)\n7. If valid, allocate 0x48 (72) bytes of memory for second grid buffer\n8. Copy template data from g_pSecondGridBufferTemplate to allocated buffer using same optimized memcpy\n9. Divide size by 4 and copy as DWORDs, then copy remaining bytes for alignment\n10. Test first buffer validity; if allocated, call ValidateEncryptedData with buffer size=0x48 and buffer pointer\n11. If validation fails (returns 0), call DeleteObjectTrampoline to free buffer and set pointer to null\n12. Test second buffer validity; if allocated, call ValidateEncryptedData with buffer size=0x48\n13. If validation fails (returns 0), call DeleteObjectTrampoline to free buffer and set pointer to null\n14. Return to caller with __stdcall stack cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n- ppFirstGridBuffer (IMPLICIT EBX): Pointer to void* that receives allocated first grid buffer\n- ppGridBuffer2: Pointer to void* that receives allocated second grid buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void (buffers allocated and stored in output pointers, or set to null on validation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x48 (72 bytes): Fixed size of each grid buffer template\n- Validation function ValidateEncryptedData uses EDI for size parameter and ESI for buffer pointer\n- Both buffers validated independently; failure of one does not affect the other\n- Function preserves ESI, EDI, EBP registers (callee-saved)\n- File: ..\\Source\\D2BNClient\\grid.cpp, lines 0x199-0x1aa (409-426 decimal)\n- Uses custom calling convention with implicit EBX first parameter (non-standard)\n- Memory copy loop unrolled: REP MOVSD copies 4 bytes per iteration, REP MOVSB handles alignment\n- Source pointers g_pFirstGridBufferTemplate and g_pSecondGridBufferTemplate point to constant template data\n- Size parameters g_dwFirstGridBufferSize and g_dwSecondGridBufferSize are both 0x48 (72 bytes)",
