      "name": "HandlePureVirtualCall",
      "signature": "uint HandlePureVirtualCall(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles pure virtual function call exceptions by validating and terminating.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference exception object pointer (EAX parameter)\n2. Load magic validation constant from first field (offset 0)\n3. Compare magic constant with C++ exception magic value 0xe06d7363\n4. If magic matches: retrieve thread local data, clear purecall flag, call terminate()\n5. If magic does not match: return 0 (indicates invalid/corrupted exception)\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionObject (void * in EAX): Pointer to C++ exception object structure\n    Offset 0: Magic constant field (uint32) - must equal 0xe06d7363\n\nReturns:\n  int: 0 if exception magic is invalid or missing (exception rejected)\n       Does not return if magic is valid (calls terminate() which never returns)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic Constant 0xe06d7363: Standard C++ exception magic number for validation\n  Thread Local Data: Uses __getptd() to access _ptiddata structure\n  Purecall Flag: Cleared at offset 0x84 in thread local data before terminate()\n  \nStructure Layout (C++ Exception Object):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  0x00    4     magic           uint32    C++ exception magic (0xe06d7363)\n  \nThread Local Data (_ptiddata):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  0x84    4     _purecall       void*     Pure call handler pointer (cleared to NULL)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
