      "name": "DeleteGlobalObject",
      "signature": "void DeleteGlobalObject(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deletes the global game object by invoking the delete operation trampoline.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global game object pointer from g_pGlobalGameObject\n2. Test if pointer is non-null\n3. If null, skip deletion and exit\n4. If non-null, invoke DeleteObjectTrampoline with:\n   - Object pointer as first parameter\n   - \"delete\" marker string as operation identifier\n   - -1 as third parameter (delete flags)\n   - 0 as fourth parameter (reserved)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n(none - parameterless function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function always succeeds whether object exists or not.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pGlobalGameObject is NULL, function returns immediately without calling DeleteObjectTrampoline\n- The -1 and 0 parameters are standard sentinel values for the delete operation\n- This function is part of the shutdown sequence for cleanup\n\nDependencies:\n- Calls DeleteObjectTrampoline to perform actual deletion\n- References g_pGlobalGameObject global pointer\n- Uses szDeleteObjectMarker string constant for operation identification",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
